@prefix pmt:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/traditions/> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix pmp:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/practices/> .
@prefix pmw:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/works/> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018)
#
# The harvest of Zeland's book on the priestess Tufti, kept apart from
# traditions/transerfing.ttl, which declares the tradition and its works.
# Read whole on 2026-11-19 in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova,
# Жрицата Тафти (e-book of spiralata.net,
# translation © 2018), the only carrier reached: no Russian and no English
# text layer was found. Places are cited by section heading and e-book page.
# The closing excerpt Червената принцеса belongs to the novel Zhritsa Itfat
# (pmw:TranserfingZhritsaItfat) and is not harvested.
#
# Two independent passes over three parts with reconciliation, then one
# integrator per part reading the whole part (prima-materia#924). Parts:
# opening address to Сценарият (pp. 1-22); Искрата на Създателя to Мисъл
# маркери (pp. 22-43); Лакомите ловци to the overview of principles
# (pp. 44-65). Shared system terms are typed once, under fixed identifiers;
# every new node carries the suffix Tf. The harvests of Stupen' I to V are
# linked, not repeated.
#


#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), part 1:
# the opening address and the sections from Acquaintance to The scenario
# (offsets 0-85495 of the folded text, e-book pp. 1-22), read in the
# Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, the only translation reached.
#
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 246 records, B 240;
# 5 records of B without counterpart in A: 1 added, 4 covered, 0 not owed);
# the reader of the whole part added 4 records both passes missed
# (clairvoyance and moving actuality from the night dream as capacities, the
# announced outcomes of the mannequin question and of the dream mirror as
# signs of success). Left out: 15 lesson recaps that restate the lesson
# before; 1 record already carried by Stupen' I (pmc:TranserfingScriptUnchangeable);
# 4 records merged into others (the two namings of Tafti are one node, the
# metapower concept and capacity are one node, the two orders of simple
# before complex frame steering are one, the punishment of arrogance is the
# consequence of the prerequisite of goodwill). 21 nodes restate a node of
# Stupen' I to V with a difference and say so in a note. Seven small nodes
# carry the prior steps that the prerequisites name.
#
# Shared terms typed here: pmc:TranserfingTaftiTf, pmc:TranserfingTaftiReceivingTf,
# pmc:TranserfingFilmReelTf, pmc:TranserfingDreamSpaceTf,
# pmc:TranserfingTwoScreensTf, pmc:TranserfingCentreOfAwarenessTf,
# pmc:TranserfingWakingInTheFilmTf, pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf,
# pmc:TranserfingMetapowerTf, pmc:TranserfingScenarioTf,
# pmc:TranserfingPresenceTf, pmc:TranserfingMannequinsTf. The mannequins are a
# concept, not a naming: the text holds them to be soulless templates. The
# plait technique, the activators and the imitation game are first stated
# here and restated in part 2. No series is typed: the numbered lists of this
# part are steps of one procedure or the author's own sets.
#

#
# opening address (cover blurb)
#

pmc:TranserfingWhyWishesFailLedScenarioFightingTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why wishes fail: led by a scenario, fighting the current frame"@en, "Warum Wünsche scheitern: vom Szenario geführt, Kampf mit dem aktuellen Bild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Things do not turn out as wanted because one is not acting by one's own will but is led by a scenario, does not know how to act so that it works, and struggles with actuality in the present frame instead of creating reality on the future film reel."@en ;
    skos:note "Pass A read this as a condition of failure; it names no practice, so it stands as a concept."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: сценарий."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), opening address, p. 1; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingActualityExistsOnceNowTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Actuality exists only once and now"@en, "Die Wirklichkeit ist nur einmal und jetzt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text holds that actuality never was and never will be; it only is, a single time, now. It exists only because it has already happened, so it cannot be changed; everything around a person is already accomplished."@en ;
    skos:note "Stated in the cover blurb and repeated as the core thesis in later lessons."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: действителността."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), opening address, p. 1; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingChangeFilmMustWakeUpComeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "To change the film one must wake up and come alive in it"@en, "Um den Film zu ändern, muss man darin erwachen und lebendig werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The governing claim of the book: changing the course of the film requires waking up within it and becoming a living (self-aware) participant."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), opening address, p. 1; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО' (Acquaintance)
#

pmc:TranserfingTaftiReceivingTf a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "The book as the speech of Tafti"@en, "Das Buch als Rede der Tafti"@de ;
    skos:definition "The whole book is voiced as the speech of Tafti, who says she was a priestess of Isis three thousand years ago and has come to the readers from Time; since Time is eternal, from it one can go anywhere and anywhen. Vadim Zeland stands on the title as author."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Tafti, priestess of the temple of Isis three thousand years ago, who says she has come from Time" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "The text states only that she has come to the readers from Time, whose eternity reaches any place and moment, and once that she steps out of her film into the book to meet them there (section on the illusion of the acting spectacle, p. 11). No circumstance of reception beyond that is given: the author does not say how, when or in what state the speech reached him, and no record other than the printed book is mentioned." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 1; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTaftiTf a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Tafti, priestess of Isis"@en, "Tafti, Priesterin der Isis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tafti is held to be a priestess of the temple of Isis three thousand years ago who has come to the readers from Time; who she is now she promises to say later. She styles herself their Supreme Priestess, the priestess whose despotism they must bear, and their Mistress who may do with them as she pleases; the readers are her pupils and subjects."@en ;
    skos:note "Pass A typed the priestess and the Mistress as two namings; they name one figure and are one node here."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Тафти (Tafti); calls herself Върховна жрица (Supreme Priestess) and Господарка (Mistress)" ;
    pm:nameRole "priestess of the temple of Isis three thousand years ago, come from Time; self-styled Supreme Priestess and Mistress of the readers" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 1; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingControllingThoughtsMattersMoreThanControllingTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Controlling thoughts matters more than controlling actions"@en, "Gedanken zu steuern ist wichtiger als Handlungen zu steuern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti says people believe they have their own opinion while it was implanted in them, and believe they steer their actions, while what matters more is steering their thoughts, which they cannot do."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 1; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamSpaceTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The dream space is a real archive of film reels"@en, "Der Traumraum ist ein reales Archiv von Filmrollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reality is layered like an onion; people know two layers, material actuality and the space of dreams. The dream space is no fantasy but really exists as an archive of film reels holding all that was, will be and could be. A dream is watching one of these films: the film watched is virtual, the reel is real."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: пространството на сънищата."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingProstranstvoVariantov: the alternatives space of Stupen' I is called the dream space and pictured as an archive of film reels, one space for night dreams and waking reality alike; the dream as true seeing of stored frames is carried by pmc:TranserfingDreamingAsTheSoulsFlightCh17 and linked."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 2; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFilmReelTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Film reel and moving frame"@en, "Filmstreifen und wanderndes Bild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reality is modelled as a film reel along which a single frame moves from past to future; actuality exists only for the instant of that frame, and the same movement runs in night dreams and in waking life."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: кадър."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingStaticTime: the reel of Stupen' I, there an image for static time, carries the whole teaching here; only the lit frame is real."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 2; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamWakingSameOrderTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dream and waking are of the same order"@en, "Traum und Wachsein sind von gleicher Art"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dream and waking reality are roughly the same; small children do not distinguish them, adults instilled the false belief that the dream world is unreal. The dream world is as real, only in another space; falling asleep and waking move one between the spaces, an event of the same order as life and death (life is the dream, death the awakening)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 2; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingInTheFilmTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking in the film"@en, "Erwachen im Film"@de ;
    skos:definition "Becoming aware inside either kind of dreaming, the night dream and waking life, which Tafti promises to teach: attention leaves the screens, and one stops being a character carried by the scenario."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 2; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLostSkillLookingAheadTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lost the skill of looking ahead"@en, "Die Fähigkeit, nach vorn zu blicken, verloren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The movement of the frame goes unnoticed because people look only at their feet; they lost the skill of looking ahead when they believed adults that the dream is unreal."@en ;
    skos:note "Pass A read this as a condition of failure; it names no practice, so it stands as a concept."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 2; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFrameNotSteeredBecauseAttentionBlockedTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Frame not steered because attention is blocked in the current frame"@en, "Das Bild wird nicht gesteuert, weil die Aufmerksamkeit im aktuellen Bild blockiert ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "People do not steer the frame, first because they sleep, second because they do not know it is possible; their attention is blocked in the current frame."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: People do not steer the frame, first because they sleep, second because they do not know it is possible; their attention is blocked in the current frame. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingMovingTheFrameTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 2; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMovingTheFrameTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Moving reality: steering the movement of the frame"@en, "Die Wirklichkeit bewegen: die Bewegung des Bildes steuern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The claimed power to steer the movement of the frame, i.e. to move reality, in dream and in waking life; it requires first understanding, not merely knowing, how attention is blocked in the current frame."@en ;
    skos:note "Repeated at the end of the dream-walk lesson as the next goal beyond the walk."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: да движите реалността."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 2; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThreePostulatesTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three postulates: three likenesses of dream and waking"@en, "Drei Postulate: drei Ähnlichkeiten von Traum und Wachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti's three postulates on how dream and waking resemble each other (a single difference is deferred): (1) helplessness, because one is asleep in both and both run regardless of one's will; (2) in both, reality advances frame by frame, unnoticed by someone staring at their feet; (3) in both this advance is steerable, yet nobody steers it, attention being stuck in the present frame."@en ;
    skos:note "The one difference between dream and waking is announced but deferred."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: трите постулата."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 2; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoScreensTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two screens, inner and outer, and attention"@en, "Zwei Bildschirme, innen und außen, und die Aufmerksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Model: a person has two screens, an inner one (thoughts) and an outer one (the surroundings), plus attention, which is almost always on one of them and very seldom in between; hence one is constantly asleep. Absorbed in thought, attention is wholly in the inner screen and one acts automatically; absorbed in something external, one forgets oneself and again acts without control."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: вътрешен и външен екран."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 2; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSleepDefinedAttentionAbsorbedScreenTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sleep defined as attention absorbed in a screen"@en, "Schlaf definiert als in einem Bildschirm versunkene Aufmerksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sleep is the uncontrolled state in which attention is sunk in either the inner or the outer screen; there one controls neither oneself nor what happens. The text distinguishes the sleeping state (сънуване, a kind of suspended animation) from the dream (сън), what is dreamt in the dream space or in real space; reality is also dreamt."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: сънуване."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWakingDreamCh17: waking life as unconscious dream is defined here by a mechanism, attention absorbed in one of two screens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionToTheCentreTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking: shift attention to the centre of consciousness (finger snap)"@en, "Erwachen: Aufmerksamkeit ins Zentrum des Bewusstseins holen (Fingerschnippen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "To wake in dream or in waking: tear attention away from the outer or inner screen and move it to the centre of consciousness. Steps: snap your fingers beside your nose; ask yourself where you were just now and in which screen your attention was sunk, and where it is now; find the middle point between the screens, from which you observe at once your thoughts and what happens to you, the surrounding reality and yourself in it."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: центъра на съзнанието."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingWakingUpFromSleepInWakingCh16: waking is done by moving attention to a centre between two screens, cued by a finger snap, not by surveying pendulums."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingShiftingAttentionCentreYieldsWakingDreamTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Shifting attention to the centre yields waking in dream or waking life"@en, "Verlagerung ins Zentrum ergibt Erwachen im Traum oder Wachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tearing attention out of either screen into the centre is stated to be what waking up, in dream or in waking life, consists of."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionToTheCentreTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWakingInTheFilmTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingShiftingAttentionCentreYieldsWatchingBothTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Shifting attention to the centre yields watching both screens"@en, "Verlagerung ins Zentrum ergibt das Beobachten beider Bildschirme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving attention to the midpoint between the screens is said to give simultaneous observation of thoughts and surroundings."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionToTheCentreTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWatchingBothScreensOnceTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWatchingBothScreensOnceTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Watching both screens at once"@en, "Beide Bildschirme zugleich beobachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti says nothing prevents one from watching both screens simultaneously and that the readers already have this ability, only nobody told them it was possible or useful."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingHowAttentionBecameGluedScreensTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "How attention became glued to the screens"@en, "Wie die Aufmerksamkeit an den Bildschirmen festklebte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Adults trained children to fix attention on the outer screen through commands to look and listen; failures and sadness taught them to retreat into the inner screen as their only refuge. Gradually attention learned to stick to one screen or the other, stopped obeying and drifts freely, so one keeps sliding into an unconscious state."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingUnconsciousStateEffectiveness510Tf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "In the unconscious state effectiveness is only 5-10%"@en, "Im unbewussten Zustand nur 5-10 % Wirksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the drifting, unconscious state one cannot act effectively: one can be deceived, insulted, frightened, robbed or beaten without responding with dignity, fights inner complexes, depends on outside circumstance and chases luck; the text puts effectiveness in this state at no more than 5-10 percent."@en ;
    skos:note "Tufti adds that this can all be fixed."@en ;
    skos:note "Pass A read this as a condition of failure; it names no practice, so it stands as a concept."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАПОЗНАНСТВО', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА' (A walk in the dreams)
#

pmc:TranserfingCentreOfAwarenessTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Centre of consciousness as observation point"@en, "Zentrum des Bewusstseins als Beobachtungspunkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The centre of consciousness is the vantage point from which one sees where one's consciousness currently is and what it is occupied with, and at the same time what happens around and what one is doing oneself. Being there is called the point of awareness."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: точката на осъзнаване."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingInnerGuardian: the observing instance is a point between the two screens, not an inner witness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingAwarenessFormulaTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking self-query and the awareness formula"@en, "Erweckende Selbstbefragung und Formel der Bewusstheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wake up and ask yourself: where am I, what am I doing, where is my attention? Then register: this is me and this is the reality around me; I see myself and reality. Doing so means you have woken and stand in the point of awareness."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: виждам себе си и реалността."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingWakingUpFromSleepInWakingCh16: the formula is shortened to seeing oneself and reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingStateOfAwarenessTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "State of awareness (being in the point of awareness)"@en, "Zustand der Bewusstheit (im Punkt der Bewusstheit sein)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state of awareness in which one sees oneself and reality; Tufti says it is not native to the readers and appears only in rare flashes, otherwise they are sunk in a screen."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: осъзнаване."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfQueryYieldsStateAwarenessTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Self-query yields the state of awareness"@en, "Selbstbefragung ergibt den Zustand der Bewusstheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asking where one is and where attention is and registering self and reality is said to put one into the point of awareness."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAwarenessFormulaTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingStateOfAwarenessTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingHourOfAwarenessTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Hold the state of awareness for one hour"@en, "Den Zustand der Bewusstheit eine Stunde halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Try to stay in the state of awareness for at least one hour and observe what happens; best done in the morning, when well rested and cheerful."@en ;
    skos:note "Tufti says the result will be interesting; no specific sign is announced."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingGoodMoodWellBeingBeforeAttemptingTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Good mood and well-being before attempting"@en, "Gute Stimmung und Wohlbefinden vor dem Versuch"@de ;
    skos:definition "The hour-long awareness exercise requires a good mood and feeling well; with poor mood or self-feeling one should not try at all."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingHourOfAwarenessTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingGoodMoodTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Tufti says nothing will come of it." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingGoodMoodTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Good mood and well-being"@en, "Gute Stimmung und Wohlbefinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being rested, cheerful and in good spirits, the state in which the hour of awareness is to be tried, preferably in the morning."@en ;
    skos:note "Typed to carry the prerequisite for the hour of awareness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBadMoodExerciseWillNotWorkTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bad mood: the exercise will not work"@en, "Schlechte Stimmung: die Übung gelingt nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "A failure condition: attempted with low mood or poor self-feeling, the awareness exercise yields nothing."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A failure condition: attempted with low mood or poor self-feeling, the awareness exercise yields nothing. It bears on pmp:TranserfingHourOfAwarenessTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 3; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingDreamWalkAwakeTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Walking in the dream while awake"@en, "Wachend im Traum spazieren gehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enter the point of awareness by telling yourself you see yourself and reality; instruct yourself that today you will walk in your dream while awake; then go anywhere (work, school) in this state of clarity. For more effect go where no one knows you, e.g. a walk, a shopping or entertainment centre. Example: switch awareness on, enter a shop, greet, pass the counters, look around, ask something and watch the staff's reactions; never fall asleep; before addressing anyone, always place attention in the centre first."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: разходка в съня наяве."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingLucidWakingDreamMasteryOfSituationCh16: the lucid waking dream becomes an exercise, a walk among strangers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAwarenessDuringWalkYieldsSelfSituationTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness during the walk yields self- and situation mastery"@en, "Bewusstheit beim Spaziergang ergibt Selbst- und Situationsbeherrschung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being aware during the walk is said to make the dream conscious and bring mastery of self and situation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDreamWalkAwakeTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingMasteryOneselfSituationTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMasteryOneselfSituationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mastery of oneself and of the situation"@en, "Beherrschung seiner selbst und der Situation"@de ;
    skos:definition "When aware, one is freed: the dream, by night or by day, becomes conscious; one masters oneself and, more importantly, gains the ability to master the situation; in a screen, every situation turns into a dream that masters you."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCentreAttentionBeforeAddressingAnyoneTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Centre attention before addressing anyone"@en, "Vor jedem Ansprechen die Aufmerksamkeit zentrieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "During the dream walk, centring attention (seeing self and reality) must come before speaking to anyone."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingDreamWalkAwakeTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingAwarenessFormulaTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOthersLookYouCuriosityUnusualSympathyTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Others look at you with curiosity and unusual sympathy"@en, "Andere sehen einen neugierig und mit ungewohnter Sympathie an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: during the waking dream walk you will find people looking at you with curiosity and treating you with a special sympathy that you have not experienced before; strangers sense dimly that you are not of this world without knowing why."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced sign: during the waking dream walk you will find people looking at you with curiosity and treating you with a special sympathy that you have not experienced before; strangers sense dimly that you are not of this world without knowing why. It bears on pmp:TranserfingDreamWalkAwakeTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOthersRemainAsleepLikeFilmCharactersTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Others remain asleep, like film characters"@en, "Die anderen schlafen weiter, wie Filmfiguren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Others keep sleeping: their attention is sunk, they are drawn into the everyday scenario as into a film, their thoughts are vague and actions unaware; they live like characters of a film. The awakened one has stepped down from the cinema screen into the hall and can leave or re-enter the film and walk among the characters independent of the scenario."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotLetYouKnowSomethingTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not let on that you know something others do not"@en, "Nicht zeigen, dass man etwas weiß, was die anderen nicht wissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "People are not aware they treat you with curiosity; do not give any sign that you know something they do not."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDreamWalkAwakeTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAwareEnergyFlowsDifferentlyFeltSubconsciouslyTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Aware energy flows differently and is felt subconsciously"@en, "Bewusste Energie fließt anders und wird unbewusst gespürt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Explanation of the sympathy: in the state of awareness one's energy flows differently; this is not visible but is sensed subconsciously, so to others one is like a firefly in a realm of darkness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamWalkYieldsOthersAttentionSympathyTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dream walk yields others' attention and sympathy"@en, "Traumspaziergang ergibt Aufmerksamkeit und Sympathie anderer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The waking dream walk is said to yield, at minimum, others' attention, sympathy and pleasant acquaintances."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDreamWalkAwakeTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAttractingAttentionSympathyOthersTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAttractingAttentionSympathyOthersTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Attracting attention and sympathy from others"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit und Sympathie anderer gewinnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the least, walking awake in one's dream brings attention and sympathy from others, pleasant acquaintances, enjoyable time and pleasure in contact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingJokingWarningProvidedYouDoNotTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Joking warning: provided you do not go mad meanwhile"@en, "Scherzhafte Warnung: sofern man nicht inzwischen verrückt wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti tells the readers to learn to move reality, adding, half in jest, the proviso that they not go crazy in the meantime, then tells them not to be scared."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMovingTheFrameTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗХОДКА В СЪНИЩАТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА' (First outing into reality)
#

pmc:TranserfingFilmComparisonNoAllegoryTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The film comparison is no allegory"@en, "Der Filmvergleich ist keine Allegorie"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the dream walk the comparison of reality with a film is said to be literal: one was present as a character come alive while the other participants moved as in sleep, obeying an external scenario; daytime awareness of ordinary people is negligibly small."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRepeatedlyCatchingOneselfSunkScreenAgainTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Repeatedly catching oneself sunk in a screen again"@en, "Sich immer wieder im Bildschirm versunken ertappen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sign of lapse during dream walks: you will constantly catch yourself having sunk into a screen and fallen asleep again; something distracted you or you got lost in thought, and from then on you no longer exist as an aware individual and do not belong to yourself."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Sign of lapse during dream walks: you will constantly catch yourself having sunk into a screen and fallen asleep again; something distracted you or you got lost in thought, and from then on you no longer exist as an aware individual and do not belong to yourself. It bears on pmp:TranserfingDreamWalkAwakeTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingScenarioTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "An external scenario leads the sleeping character"@en, "Ein äußeres Szenario führt die schlafende Figur"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asleep or awake one is in a film and dragged by the flow of the scenario, as a character in it; one does not belong to oneself because one's attention does not belong to oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: външен сценарий."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingScriptUnchangeable: there a script belongs to a sector of the alternatives space; here the scenario is an outer program that owns the character through its attention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 4; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingControllingAttentionYieldsReleaseScenarioTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Controlling attention yields release from the scenario"@en, "Aufmerksamkeitskontrolle ergibt Befreiung vom Szenario"@de ;
    skos:definition "Waking and controlling attention (centre of consciousness) is said to remove the scenario's power."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionToTheCentreTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReleaseScenarioHoldTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingReleaseScenarioHoldTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Release from the scenario's hold"@en, "Befreiung vom Griff des Szenarios"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once awake and controlling attention, the scenario at once loses its power over you; everyday duties remain, but no longer as strictly as the scenario dictates; you see yourself and reality and can consciously steer your will, the first ascent to a new level of mastery of self and reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoLevelsOfWakingTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two levels: waking in the night dream and waking in reality"@en, "Zwei Stufen: Erwachen im Nachttraum und Erwachen in der Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unlike dream characters, a person can raise attention one level, waking inside the dream itself, and even two levels, waking into reality. In an ordinary dream not recognised as such one is helpless and fully captured."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingLucidityInDreamCh7: lucidity in the night dream is one level up, waking in reality a second level."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMannequinsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mannequins"@en, "Puppen (Manekene)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dream characters are held to be mannequins: without self-awareness (they do not experience themselves as persons), without will (subject to the scenario) and without soul, mere templates; each lives in its film like a character once recorded on a reel stored in the archive of Eternity."@en ;
    skos:note "Typed as a concept, not a naming: the text holds the mannequins to be soulless templates without self-awareness or will, not beings. When a dream or a film ends, it says, they freeze until the next showing or for good (detail from pass B, section on the illusion of the acting spectacle)."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: манекени."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingQuestioningAMannequinTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Experiment: question a dream mannequin"@en, "Experiment: eine Traumfigur befragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once able to wake within a dream, ask a mannequin who it is; it will dodge or name its role in the scenario but never say it is itself, having no I. Or ask whether it knows that you are asleep and it is being dreamed by you; the question confuses it because it has never slept or woken."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLucidWakingDreamBeforeMannequinExperimentTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Lucid waking in dream before the mannequin experiment"@en, "Luzides Erwachen im Traum vor dem Mannequin-Experiment"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mannequin experiment presupposes being able to wake up inside a dream."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingQuestioningAMannequinTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingTwoLevelsOfWakingTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMannequinDodgesTheQuestionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mannequin dodges or names its role"@en, "Die Puppe weicht aus oder nennt ihre Rolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked who it is, a dream mannequin will evade or give its role in the scenario and will never say that it is itself; asked whether it knows it is being dreamed, it becomes confused."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Asked who it is, a dream mannequin will evade or give its role in the scenario and will never say that it is itself; asked whether it knows it is being dreamed, it becomes confused. It bears on pmp:TranserfingQuestioningAMannequinTf."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLivingPeopleSoulWillSelfAwarenessTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living people: soul, will, self-awareness, but asleep"@en, "Lebende Menschen: Seele, Wille, Selbstbewusstsein, aber schlafend"@de ;
    skos:definition "Living people have soul, will and self-awareness and can say \"this is me\", though that is all they can say of themselves; their self-awareness sleeps and they use will rarely, when they must mobilise for action."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWillOperatesWithinCurrentFrameTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Will operates only within the current frame"@en, "Der Wille wirkt nur im aktuellen Bild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Will is used only within the bounds of the current frame (to be developed later)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЪРВО ИЗЛИЗАНЕ В РЕАЛНОСТТА', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО' (Tracking attention)
#

pmc:TranserfingFilmTermsUsedConveniencePerceptionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Film terms used for convenience of perception"@en, "Filmbegriffe zur Erleichterung der Wahrnehmung verwendet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti states she uses this film vocabulary for the convenience of the readers' perception, because in dream and in waking they do nearly the same: watch a movie and play in it as role characters without the right to arbitrary behaviour."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on the status of the model: the terms are a didactic convenience."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingCheckingWhereAttentionWasTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Check where your attention just was"@en, "Prüfen, wo die Aufmerksamkeit eben war"@de ;
    skos:definition "To convince yourself that you act under compulsion rather than independently, look at your attention: where was it just now and to whom did it belong?"@en ;
    skos:note "Verification exercise: the expected finding is that it belonged to the scenario."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingIAttentionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The I is one's attention"@en, "Das Ich ist die eigene Aufmerksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The I is identified with attention; without self-control the scenario leads, whether by night or by day. Waking life counts as dreaming awake, ordinary sleep as dreaming asleep; each may be aware or unaware."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Аз."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAttentionControlYieldsActingOwnWillTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Attention control yields acting by own will"@en, "Aufmerksamkeitskontrolle ergibt Handeln aus eigenem Willen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Controlling attention is said to make one come alive in the film and act by own will."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionToTheCentreTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingComingAliveInTheFilmTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingComingAliveInTheFilmTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Coming alive in the film: acting by one's own will"@en, "Im Film lebendig werden: aus eigenem Willen handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Controlling attention one comes alive in the film and gains the ability to act independently, by one's own will; one becomes a sane character able to walk freely in one's dream, already tried while awake and later to be learned in night dreams as well. Tufti says this ability in waking life matters more, since the dream film is virtual while life is real and there one either follows another's scenario or realises one's own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 5; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingObstacleHabitSinkingScreensTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Obstacle: the habit of sinking into the screens"@en, "Hindernis: die Gewohnheit, in die Bildschirme zu versinken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The only obstacle is the habit of sinking into outer and inner screens; one cannot hold attention in the centre for long."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The only obstacle is the habit of sinking into outer and inner screens; one cannot hold attention in the centre for long. It bears on pmp:TranserfingAttentionTrackingTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingComingAliveInTheFilmTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingAttentionTrackingTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Attention tracking: build the habit of returning to the centre"@en, "Aufmerksamkeitsverfolgung: Gewohnheit der Rückkehr ins Zentrum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Build a new habit of returning attention to the centre: when setting out on a dream walk, instruct yourself not to forget to wake, literally set this as a goal; while walking, keep reminding yourself that you constantly sink and fall asleep, do not be sad, bring attention back again and again; organise the tracking of attention by attention itself, i.e. of yourself. It is not necessary to hold attention in the centre all the time; what matters is the ability to react to what happens by waking instead of falling asleep."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: проследяване на вниманието."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSetGoalWakingBeforeWalkTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Set the goal of waking before the walk"@en, "Vor dem Spaziergang das Ziel des Erwachens setzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before the dream walk one must literally set oneself the goal of remembering to wake."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingAttentionTrackingTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingSettingTheGoalToWakeTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Otherwise one simply forgets what to do." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingSettingTheGoalToWakeTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Setting the goal to wake"@en, "Sich das Erwachen zum Ziel setzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before setting out on a dream walk, instruct oneself, literally as a goal, not to forget that one must wake."@en ;
    skos:note "Typed to carry the prerequisite for attention tracking."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingForgettingLazinessNothingWillLearnedTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forgetting and laziness: nothing will be learned"@en, "Vergessen und Faulheit: man lernt nichts"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one forgets and is lazy, one learns nothing."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If one forgets and is lazy, one learns nothing. It bears on pmp:TranserfingAttentionTrackingTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingTwoActivatorsTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The two activators: external and internal"@en, "Die zwei Aktivatoren: äußerer und innerer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every event, even a slight stir in the surroundings, must become a signal to wake, and every own action a reminder to check attention. External activator: as soon as something happens (meeting someone, being addressed, a sound or movement nearby, anything that used to pull you in) wake up; turn attention to it but keep it in the centre. Internal activator: before you do anything (go somewhere, do something, address someone) set attention in the centre first."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: активатор."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingInternalActivatorAfterActionTooLateTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Internal activator after the action is too late"@en, "Innerer Aktivator nach der Handlung ist zu spät"@de ;
    skos:definition "The internal activator must fire before the action; afterwards it is too late, and one only discovers that one first fell asleep and then woke up and remembered having slept."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The internal activator must fire before the action; afterwards it is too late, and one only discovers that one first fell asleep and then woke up and remembered having slept. It bears on pmp:TranserfingTwoActivatorsTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLearningThroughManyRepetitionsMartialArtsTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Learning only through many repetitions, as in martial arts"@en, "Lernen nur durch viele Wiederholungen, wie in Kampfkünsten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attention control can be learned only by many repetitions, as in martial arts."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingComingAliveInTheFilmTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingAttentionTrackingTf, pmp:TranserfingTwoActivatorsTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Tufti says there is no other way to learn it." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingManagingAttentionBeforeManagingLifeTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Managing attention before managing life"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit steuern vor Leben steuern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Managing one's life comes only after one has learned to manage attention."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingManagingLifeTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingComingAliveInTheFilmTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingManagingLifeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Managing one's life"@en, "Das eigene Leben steuern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once one learns to manage attention, one can manage one's life, which may then cease to be useless."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotTakeYourAdvantageSuperiorityTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not take your advantage for superiority"@en, "Den Vorteil nicht für Überlegenheit halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having woken in the dream and gained strength while others sleep, do not regard the advantage as superiority and do not treat sleepers arrogantly or condescendingly (Tufti reserves this for herself)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAwakenedWhoLookDownBecomeOutcastsCh16: there looking down on sleepers makes an outcast; here it is forbidden and reality punishes it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDreamWalkAwakeTf, pmc:TranserfingReleaseScenarioHoldTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ' (Creating reality)
#

pmc:TranserfingAttentionTrackingYieldsManagingLifeTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Attention tracking yields managing one's life"@en, "Aufmerksamkeitsverfolgung ergibt das Steuern des Lebens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the three tracking rules is said to build the habit of steering attention and ultimately one's life."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAttentionTrackingTf, pmp:TranserfingTwoActivatorsTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingManagingLifeTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingObserveSleepersUnnoticedPretendSleepTooTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Observe sleepers unnoticed; pretend to sleep too"@en, "Schlafende unbemerkt beobachten, selbst Schlaf vortäuschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not look down on the sleepers; observe them unnoticed, do not show that you know what they do not, and pretend to be asleep as well; this applies to all walks, waking and dreaming."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDreamWalkAwakeTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPositiveDispositionTowardOthersBeforeDreamTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Positive disposition toward others before a dream walk"@en, "Positive Haltung gegenüber anderen vor dem Traumspaziergang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before a dream walk one must be positively disposed toward the people around."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNoPuppeteerCh7: the slap for conceit is tied here to the dream walk and needs a positive disposition first."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingDreamWalkAwakeTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingPositiveDispositionTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Otherwise one is punished: the arrogant, spiteful, haughty, proud, squeamish or self-satisfied braggart gets a flick on the nose from reality itself. The text says the punishment comes from reality, not from Tafti." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPositiveDispositionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Positive disposition toward others"@en, "Wohlwollende Haltung gegenüber anderen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being kindly inclined toward the people around, required before any dream walk."@en ;
    skos:note "Typed to carry the prerequisite for the dream walk."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 6; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLitFrameRealPastFutureInformationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Only the lit frame is real; past and future are information"@en, "Nur das beleuchtete Bild ist real; Vergangenheit und Zukunft sind Information"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only the momentary imprint of actuality, the illuminated frame, is real; past and future are virtual and kept forever in the archive of reels. Past and future are immaterial information with material carriers that can be found, which is why clairvoyants can look into the past and predict the future. The archive exists though intangible, like the ether."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: осветеният кадър."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 7; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingClairvoyanceTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Clairvoyance into past and future"@en, "Hellsehen in Vergangenheit und Zukunft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seers are said to be able to look into the past and foretell the future, because past and future are immaterial information whose carriers are material and can be found in the archive."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes. No practice for it is given in this part."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 7; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamSpaceCommonArchiveEachFrameTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dream space as common archive; each frame a new realisation"@en, "Traumraum als gemeinsames Archiv; jedes Bild eine neue Verwirklichung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ethereal substance hangs in the dream space, which is one for dreams and for reality. In dreams one sees what could have happened or could happen; whether it did or will is not given, variants are countless. What can happen in dream could be in reality and vice versa. One can view the archive or exist in it, but in each frame only once; each next frame is a new realisation, an upgrade of everything down to the atomic level."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 7; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSoulsInvariantAcrossFramesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Only souls are invariant across frames"@en, "Nur die Seelen bleiben über die Bilder hinweg unverändert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only the souls of living beings are unchanged; they can watch the dream reels or move along them in reality with the frame, so the I is the same that was in the past, flew in dreams and will appear in the future."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 7; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLifeCanDetermineRealityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Life can determine reality"@en, "Das Leben kann die Wirklichkeit bestimmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The world exists in animate and inanimate form: reality is inanimate substance, life is animate, life permeates material actuality, can influence the course of reality and can determine it. Tufti calls this the main thesis to grasp."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 7; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating reality: choosing which reel the frame runs along"@en, "Wirklichkeit erschaffen: wählen, auf welcher Rolle das Bild läuft"@de ;
    skos:definition "To create means to determine in which direction and along which reel the frame will move; everyone has this possibility but does not use it, just as they do not use attention control. Reality must be created in advance, not fought in the present frame."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: създаване на реалност."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 7; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTryingChangeGivenRealityCurrentFrameTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trying to change the given reality in the current frame"@en, "Versuch, die gegebene Wirklichkeit im aktuellen Bild zu ändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The core error: people try to change the reality given in the current frame, i.e. what has already happened; being in the present they actually dwell in the past, attention sunk in the current frame, an illusion that keeps them from the future, so the future does not depend on them."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The core error: people try to change the reality given in the current frame, i.e. what has already happened; being in the present they actually dwell in the past, attention sunk in the current frame, an illusion that keeps them from the future, so the future does not depend on them. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 7; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDecisiveActionCurrentFrameStillBeingTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Decisive action in the current frame is still being dragged"@en, "Entschlossenes Handeln im aktuellen Bild ist doch nur Mitgeschleiftwerden"@de ;
    skos:definition "One may seem to act consciously, decide, solve problems and reach goals, but all this happens in the current frame and in an unaware state, so the scenario drags one along a reel one did not choose; one only flails helplessly."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: One may seem to act consciously, decide, solve problems and reach goals, but all this happens in the current frame and in an unaware state, so the scenario drags one along a reel one did not choose; one only flails helplessly. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА РЕАЛНОСТ', p. 7; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО' (The plait of intention)
#

pmc:TranserfingSupremeCreatorTf a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Supreme Creator"@en, "Höchster Schöpfer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The readers are told to thank a Supreme Creator for being allowed to move the frame; who shot the archive of reels and sealed it for ever is said to be beyond them. Later the Creator is said to have conceived people as luminous beings looking ahead, as they once were."@en ;
    skos:note "Added from pass B. The later passage is pmc:TranserfingFromSnailToFireflyTf."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Върховния Създател (Supreme Creator); also Създателя" ;
    pm:nameRole "the creator who permits people to move the frame and who conceived them as luminous beings" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAttentionAndIntentionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two control functions: attention and intention"@en, "Zwei Steuerfunktionen: Aufmerksamkeit und Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "One has two control functions: attention, responsible for one's sanity (awareness), and intention, responsible for action: before doing something one must have the intention, which is realised in the action. All actions refer to the current frame because intention is stuck there, just as attention sticks to a screen."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: намерение."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNamerenie: intention is one of two control functions, beside attention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoCentresOfIntentionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two centres of intention: inner (forehead) and outer (plait tip)"@en, "Zwei Zentren der Absicht: inneres (Stirn) und äußeres (Zopfende)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intention has an inner and an outer centre. The inner one, in the frontal part of the skull, serves ordinary functioning: in concentration one frowns, in intending to do something the muscles tense; it permits primitive actions in the current frame. The outer centre is not used at all, yet it is what moves the future frame."@en ;
    skos:note "Source slip: the recap that opens the section on using the plait names the inner centre twice, at the forehead and at the plait tip; the second must be the outer centre, as the preceding section states."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: външен център на намерението."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie and pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie: the two intentions are located in the body, at the forehead and at the tip of the plait."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The plait (braid) of intention"@en, "Der Zopf der Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everyone has a plait of intention: an energy braid like an ordinary plait, invisible but perceptible as a phantom body part that once existed and still seems present; it does not hang down but sticks out at an angle to the spine. At its tip lies the outer centre of intention, between the shoulder blades but a little away from the back."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: плитка на намерението."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingLocatingTheOuterCentreTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Locating the outer centre of intention"@en, "Das äußere Zentrum der Absicht finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Locate the outer centre intuitively: direct attention to the spot just behind the back between the shoulder blades and you will feel it; the exact distance does not matter. If you still do not feel it, read the chapter on the plait and energy flows."@en ;
    skos:note "Cross-reference to a chapter titled on the plait and energy flows."@en ;
    skos:note "The text refers the reader to a chapter on the plait and energy flows for those who do not yet feel it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFeelingPlaitOuterCentreTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling the plait and its outer centre"@en, "Den Zopf und sein äußeres Zentrum spüren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The claimed ability to sense the plait as a phantom limb and its tip as the outer centre of intention, which Tufti says can be found instantly, right now."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDirectingAttentionSpotYieldsFeelingPlaitTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Directing attention to the spot yields feeling the plait"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit auf die Stelle ergibt das Spüren des Zopfes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pointing attention at the spot behind the shoulder blades is said to make one feel the outer centre."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLocatingTheOuterCentreTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFeelingPlaitOuterCentreTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingLightingFromThePlaitTipTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Basic plait use: picture the wanted event from the plait tip"@en, "Grundgebrauch des Zopfes: gewünschtes Ereignis vom Zopfende aus vorstellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Direct attention to the tip of the plait and imagine a picture of an event you would like to draw into your life; this illuminates the future frame and it is realised."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFindingPlaitTipBeforeUsingTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding the plait tip before using it"@en, "Das Zopfende finden, bevor man es nutzt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Using the outer centre presupposes locating and feeling the plait tip."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingLightingFromThePlaitTipTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingLocatingTheOuterCentreTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlaitUseYieldsCreatingRealityLightingTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Plait use yields creating reality (lighting the future frame)"@en, "Zopfgebrauch ergibt Wirklichkeitserschaffung (Beleuchten des künftigen Bildes)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Picturing the wanted event with attention on the plait tip is said to light up the future frame, which then comes true."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLightingFromThePlaitTipTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingStuckWhatEyesSeeRetreatInnerTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Stuck to what the eyes see; retreat into the inner screen"@en, "An das Gesehene gebunden; Rückzug in den inneren Bildschirm"@de ;
    skos:definition "Why the simple method was unknown and unused: people are stuck in the current frame, used to what their eyes see in front of them, believing they can act only according to that; when something fails they sink into the inner screen of feelings and reflections, which again concern what they see. So neither attention nor intention is theirs."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Why the simple method was unknown and unused: people are stuck in the current frame, used to what their eyes see in front of them, believing they can act only according to that; when something fails they sink into the inner screen of feelings and reflections, which again concern what they see. So neither attention nor intention is theirs. It bears on pmp:TranserfingLightingFromThePlaitTipTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingUsingInnerCentreDreamsStayUnrealisedTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Using only the inner centre: dreams stay unrealised"@en, "Nur das innere Zentrum: Träume bleiben unverwirklicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "People can invent their own scenario but cannot realise it; they dream or want something from the future, but the future frame can be lit only from the outer centre of intention, while they habitually use only the inner one. The current frame is an illusion and a trap."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: People can invent their own scenario but cannot realise it; they dream or want something from the future, but the future frame can be lit only from the outer centre of intention, while they habitually use only the inner one. The current frame is an illusion and a trap. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА НА НАМЕРЕНИЕТО', p. 8; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'How to use the plait' (Cyrillic heading in dcterms:source)
#

pmc:TranserfingDoFirstUnderstandLaterTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Do first, understand later"@en, "Erst tun, dann verstehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti postpones the explanation of why dreams do not come true and goes straight to the technique, saying it is better for the readers to do first and understand afterwards."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Plait technique in three steps"@en, "Zopftechnik in drei Schritten"@de ;
    skos:definition "First, wake and enter the point of awareness with the usual formula of seeing self and reality. Second, activate the plait: feel it; as soon as you attend to it, it rises at an angle to the back and is active. Third, without moving attention away from the plait, imagine the picture of the future: create your reality in thought, in words or on the screen, as you are able. Summary: wake, attend to the plait, and while keeping the sensation of it picture on your screen the wished-for thing happening."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: активирайте плитката."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingPrecedesPlaitActivationTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking precedes plait activation"@en, "Erwachen geht der Zopfaktivierung voraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the plait technique, waking into the point of awareness comes first, then plait activation, then the picture."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingAwarenessFormulaTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingEyesShiftAnotherModeWhenPlaitTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Eyes shift into another mode when the plait is active"@en, "Die Augen wechseln bei aktivem Zopf in einen anderen Modus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: on activating the plait the eyes enter a different mode, they widen slightly and seem to begin to radiate; this is a new, unfamiliar mode of functioning."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced sign: on activating the plait the eyes enter a different mode, they widen slightly and seem to begin to radiate; this is a new, unfamiliar mode of functioning. It bears on pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWindingOwnFilmReelTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Winding one's own film reel"@en, "Die eigene Filmrolle selbst weiterspulen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of watching and obeying an external film, one becomes able to wind one's own film reel oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueYieldsWindingOwnReelTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Plait technique yields winding one's own reel"@en, "Zopftechnik ergibt das Spulen der eigenen Rolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working with the activated plait is said to switch one into the mode of winding one's own reel."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWindingOwnFilmReelTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueYieldsCreatingRealityTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Plait technique yields creating reality"@en, "Zopftechnik ergibt Wirklichkeitserschaffung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Waking, attending to the plait and picturing the wish coming true is the stated way to create reality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlaitAsProjectorTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The plait as projector"@en, "Der Zopf als Projektor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The plait works like a film projector. Endlessly running wanting and dreaming on the inner screen is inefficient, nearly idling; the projector runs at full power when thoughts, words and images issue from the outer centre of intention. To affect reality rather than toil in thought, switch the plait on."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: прожекционен апарат."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWishingInnerScreenIdleRunningTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wishing on the inner screen is idle running"@en, "Wünschen auf dem inneren Bildschirm ist Leerlauf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wanting and dreaming only on the inner screen, without the plait, is ineffective, almost idling."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Wanting and dreaming only on the inner screen, without the plait, is ineffective, almost idling. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlaitActivationIndividualDetailsNotFixedTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Plait activation is individual; details are not fixed"@en, "Zopfaktivierung ist individuell; Details sind nicht festgelegt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Statement on how fixed the method is: attention need not stay on the plait tip, it suffices to feel the whole plait as a phantom body part; one may activate it however is convenient, sensations are individual; the eyes need no attention and may be closed or even blind. What matters is running thoughts, words and images in connection with the plait."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPracticalHabitsFrameSteeringFirstTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Practical habits of frame steering first"@en, "Zuerst praktische Gewohnheiten der Bildsteuerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before amazing anyone, one must amaze oneself, and for this one must acquire practical habits of steering the movement of the frame, starting with something elementary. Training starts with the simplest events that fit into a single frame; more complex movements of the frame come later and need more complex actions."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingMovingTheFrameTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingFulfillingMomentaryWishesTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingFulfillingMomentaryWishesTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Fulfilling momentary wishes"@en, "Erfüllung augenblicklicher Wünsche"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choose an upcoming event whose outcome may go either way, starting with the simplest that fits within one frame (a purchase in a shop, a parking place, any daily act at work, school, outdoors or at home). Wake, activate the plait and, still feeling it, picture the wish being fulfilled; then stop feeling the plait and act as usual. For more certainty one may repeat lighting the frame several times."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingContradictoryFeelingsSeeingImpossibleHappenTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Contradictory feelings on seeing the impossible happen"@en, "Widersprüchliche Gefühle, wenn das Unmögliche geschieht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: you will see for yourself; you will feel very mixed emotions on realising that something that cannot be has happened, and it will be hard to believe that outer reality obeys your will."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced sign: you will see for yourself; you will feel very mixed emotions on realising that something that cannot be has happened, and it will be hard to believe that outer reality obeys your will. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFulfillingMomentaryWishesTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSuccessRateDependsFeltRealityWhatTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Success rate depends on the felt reality of what happens"@en, "Erfolgsquote hängt vom Wirklichkeitsgefühl ab"@de ;
    skos:definition "The success statistics of the experiments depend on one's sense of the reality of what happens; the criterion of reality is the everyday, habit, what has happened more than once; only what fits the template of one's world-sense is possible. As with riding a bicycle one did not know was possible, one cannot steer the frame while this seems unreal."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The success statistics of the experiments depend on one's sense of the reality of what happens; the criterion of reality is the everyday, habit, what has happened more than once; only what fits the template of one's world-sense is possible. As with riding a bicycle one did not know was possible, one cannot steer the frame while this seems unreal. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFulfillingMomentaryWishesTf, pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingMovingTheFrameTf."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: шаблона на светоусещането."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTemplateOfWorldSenseTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The template of world-sense"@en, "Die Schablone des Weltempfindens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Model: a person's template of world-sense, built from everyday experience, fixes what counts as possible; nothing that does not fit one's picture of the world and oneself can happen to one."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: шаблон."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СИ СЛУЖИТЕ С ПЛИТКАТА', p. 9; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ' (Illusion of the acting spectacle)
#

pmc:TranserfingDoubtBlocksFrameSteeringTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Doubt blocks frame steering"@en, "Zweifel blockiert die Bildsteuerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "In dreams the incredible happens only because critical judgement is lowered; awake, everything is strictly checked against the template. So the ability to move the frame depends on admitting the possibility unconditionally; doubt defeats it."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: In dreams the incredible happens only because critical judgement is lowered; awake, everything is strictly checked against the template. So the ability to move the frame depends on admitting the possibility unconditionally; doubt defeats it. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingMovingTheFrameTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 10; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSimpleMiraclesEasyComplexMovesNeedTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Simple miracles are easy; complex moves need complex actions"@en, "Einfache Wunder sind leicht; komplexe Bewegungen brauchen komplexe Handlungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Simple \"miracles\" will come easily: one succeeds in everything that agrees with everyday experience, which is the template; more complex movements of the frame require more complex actions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 10; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingReelLifeLineScenarioFateTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reel as life line, scenario as fate"@en, "Rolle als Lebenslinie, Szenario als Schicksal"@de ;
    skos:definition "Roughly, the reel corresponds to one's line of life and the scenario to fate; people neither pick their fate nor attempt to alter it, though they could; consoling oneself that a predetermined fate is still in one's hands is self-deception, for a rigidly fixed scenario is in charge."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingLiniyaZhizni: the life line is the reel, and fate is the scenario that drags the character along it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 10; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingIllusionOfTheSpectacleTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The illusion of the acting spectacle"@en, "Die Illusion des handelnden Schauspiels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not only what one sees but also what one does can be illusory: it only seems one acts at one's discretion. One cannot recognise this illusion because one lives in it constantly. Neither the dream mannequin nor a film character can recognise the illusion of its own actions; people can, but do not. One is aware only at the moment of asking where and who one is; otherwise attention is sunk in a screen and intention in the current frame, so motives and actions are not one's own: a wish arising and the urge to act on it are written in the scenario. Life is not lived, it happens to one."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: илюзия на действащия спектакъл."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGameAsUnrecognisedDream: the illusion extends from what one sees to what one does."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 10; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnMannequinsReelsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One's own mannequins in the reels"@en, "Die eigenen Mannequins in den Filmrollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The reels in the archive contain one's own mannequins; dreaming a reel, consciousness finds its mannequin, which comes alive and moves, and one lives in its body as one of many variants. In waking life the same happens: consciousness enters the next version of the mannequin, which comes alive and becomes oneself in the current frame."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 10; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingMirrorInTheDreamTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Look in a mirror while dreaming"@en, "Im Traum in einen Spiegel schauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Occasionally, while dreaming, look at yourself in a mirror; Tufti says you will not recognise yourself, since you inhabit a mannequin as one of many variants."@en ;
    skos:note "Given as a check illustrating the mannequin model."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 10; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSnailTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The snail: primitive reactive psyche"@en, "Die Schnecke: primitive reflexhafte Psyche"@de ;
    skos:definition "People living as in sleep are likened to snails that respond the same primitive way to every outside stimulus, pulling in their horns and hiding in their shells; one's fate is predetermined to the extent that one is predictable."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: рогцата на охлюва."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNotRecognisingOneselfTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not recognising oneself in the dream mirror"@en, "Sich im Traumspiegel nicht erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Looking into a mirror while dreaming, one will not recognise oneself, since one is living in a mannequin as one variant among many."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Looking into a mirror while dreaming, one will not recognise oneself, since one is living in a mannequin as one variant among many. It bears on pmp:TranserfingMirrorInTheDreamTf."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWhileTeachingDoesNotFitTemplateTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "While the teaching does not fit the template: free in dreams, unfree in fate"@en, "Solange die Lehre nicht in die Schablone passt: frei im Träumen, unfrei im Schicksal"@de ;
    skos:definition "As long as what was learned seems unattainable and does not fit one's template, one stays free in one's dreams and unfree in one's fate."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: As long as what was learned seems unattainable and does not fit one's template, one stays free in one's dreams and unfree in one's fate. It bears on pmp:TranserfingImitationGameTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingWalkingAliveRealityChoosingNewReelTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSheddingIllusionsBeforeChoosingNewReelTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Shedding illusions before choosing a new reel"@en, "Illusionen ablegen, bevor man eine neue Rolle wählt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choosing a new reality requires first seeing through and getting rid of one's illusions."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingWalkingAliveRealityChoosingNewReelTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingSeeingThroughTheIllusionTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSeeingThroughTheIllusionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing through and shedding the illusions"@en, "Die Illusionen durchschauen und ablegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Finally grasping the illusions of image and spectacle and getting rid of them, after which one can walk alive in reality and pick a new reel."@en ;
    skos:note "Typed to carry the prerequisite for walking alive in reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWalkingAliveRealityChoosingNewReelTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Walking alive in reality and choosing a new reel"@en, "Lebendig in der Wirklichkeit gehen und eine neue Rolle wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once one sees through and sheds the illusions, one can walk in reality as a living being in the reel and choose a new reality like a reel from the archive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИЛЮЗИЯ ЗА ДЕЙСТВАЩИЯ СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'How to get out of the trap' (Cyrillic heading in dcterms:source)
#

pmc:TranserfingMomentSelfAwarenessDoesNotFreeTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A moment of self-awareness does not free one from the scenario"@en, "Ein Moment der Selbstbewusstheit befreit nicht vom Szenario"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warning against overrating the awareness exercise: one is aware only while asking the question; the rest of the time consciousness sleeps and obeys the external scenario, so the ability to become aware for an instant does not release one; the trap holds firm whatever one imagines about oneself."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAwarenessFormulaTf, pmc:TranserfingStateOfAwarenessTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeObstaclesTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three obstacles to escaping the trap"@en, "Drei Hindernisse beim Entkommen aus der Falle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Three main obstacles: (1) not knowing that one is a character; (2) the reflexive psyche, the snail's horns; (3) the template bounded by the limits of possible and impossible. The first is already removed by knowing; the other two, habits and beliefs, remain."@en ;
    skos:note "The first obstacle is met by pmc:TranserfingKnowingOneIsACharacterTf; the snail's horns are pmc:TranserfingSnailTf; the template is pmc:TranserfingTemplateOfWorldSenseTf."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingKnowingAboutIllusionFirstConditionEscapeTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing about the illusion is the first condition of escape"@en, "Wissen um die Illusion ist die erste Bedingung des Entkommens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing that one is a character in the spectacle is the first thing needed for escaping."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingReleaseScenarioHoldTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingKnowingOneIsACharacterTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Whoever does not know about the illusion will remain in it forever." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingKnowingOneIsACharacterTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing that one is a character"@en, "Wissen, dass man eine Figur ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowledge, now given, that one is a character inside the spectacle; the first of three things needed to escape the trap."@en ;
    skos:note "Typed to carry the prerequisite for release from the scenario."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingKnowingNotEnoughTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing is not enough"@en, "Wissen reicht nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowledge alone does not change anything, as a snail who learns it is a snail remains one; lamenting changes nothing. One cannot simply come alive and do as one pleases outside the scenario; two further barriers, habits and beliefs, must be overcome, which actually rule the person."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingKnowingOneIsACharacterTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPassiveHabitExpectingHopingTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The passive habit of expecting and hoping"@en, "Die passive Gewohnheit des Erwartens und Hoffens"@de ;
    skos:definition "What makes one a snail is the habit not of determining reality but of waiting and hoping (will it work or not?); from this passive position one can only feel out reality and pull in one's horns at the first fright."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: What makes one a snail is the habit not of determining reality but of waiting and hoping (will it work or not?); from this passive position one can only feel out reality and pull in one's horns at the first fright. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSwitchingActiveModeTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Switching to active mode"@en, "Umschalten in den aktiven Modus"@de ;
    skos:definition "To stop being a snail one must switch to active mode: not expect and hope but create reality."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingActiveModeTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Otherwise one stays a snail in the trap of the current frame, only feeling reality out." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingActiveModeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Active mode"@en, "Aktiver Modus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creating one's reality instead of expecting and hoping; the opposite of the passive stance of a snail that only feels reality out."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: активен режим."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTemplateDeniesRealityCanCreatedSnailTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The template that denies reality can be created is the snail's shell"@en, "Die Schablone, die Wirklichkeitserschaffung leugnet, ist das Schneckenhaus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The obstacle is the template by which reality cannot be created; this is the snail's house."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNewHabitsBeliefsManyRepetitionsTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "New habits and beliefs only by many repetitions"@en, "Neue Gewohnheiten und Vorstellungen nur durch viele Wiederholungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "New habits and beliefs are formed the same way the old took root, through many repetitions; from now on one actively steers the movement of the frame instead of following reality."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingMovingTheFrameTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRepeatedFrameLightingYieldsActiveSteeringTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Repeated frame lighting yields active steering of the frame"@en, "Wiederholtes Bildbeleuchten ergibt aktives Steuern des Bildes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through repeated practice on the upcoming frame one comes to steer the movement of the frame actively instead of following reality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingMovingTheFrameTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAttentionDirectedSeveralFramesAheadTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Attention directed several frames ahead"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit mehrere Bilder voraus richten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The frame to steer is not the present one but the upcoming one; the present has already happened and cannot be changed, only upcoming reality can be created, so attention must be aimed several frames ahead."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 11; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Algorithm of lighting the frame (with three activators)"@en, "Algorithmus der Bildbeleuchtung (mit drei Aktivatoren)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Track the upcoming frame as attention was tracked. Three activators: expectation (something should happen, you wait or hope), intention (you mean to go somewhere or do something), problem (something happened that needs solving). Each time, do not wait, hope or fuss, and before acting create reality first. Steps: (1) recognise you are in one of the activators; (2) wake: I see myself and I see reality; (3) activate the plait and, keeping the sensation on it, create reality; (4) take the sensation off the plait; (5) if the event matters, repeat the lighting several times. Try to remember the upcoming frame constantly."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: алгоритъм на осветяване."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 12; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFirstWillNotWorkEveryTimeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "At first it will not work every time; constant forgetting"@en, "Anfangs klappt es nicht jedes Mal; ständiges Vergessen"@de ;
    skos:definition "It will not work every time; at first one will keep forgetting. The old habit does not go away by itself, it must be destroyed and replaced with a new one; laziness is not allowed."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: It will not work every time; at first one will keep forgetting. The old habit does not go away by itself, it must be destroyed and replaced with a new one; laziness is not allowed. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'КАК ДА СЕ ИЗМЪКНЕТЕ ОТ КАПАНА', p. 12; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ' (Working out)
#

pmp:TranserfingLightingCertainEventsTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Light the frame even for certain events"@en, "Das Bild auch für sichere Ereignisse beleuchten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Create not only events of unknown outcome but also those that will certainly happen. Example: on the way somewhere, intending to go through a certain door, light this frame too: picture, in thought, in words or best visually, opening the door and walking through."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 12; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRepeatedSelfConvictionEmbedNewSkillTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Repeated self-conviction to embed the new skill in the template"@en, "Wiederholte Selbstüberzeugung, um die neue Fähigkeit in die Schablone einzubetten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Endless repetition is needed to embed the new development into the snail template."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingMovingTheFrameTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingLightingCertainEventsTf, pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "One will not believe reality can obey until one has convinced oneself, many times over." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 12; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeResultsOfTrainingTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three results of training on simple events"@en, "Drei Ergebnisse des Trainings an einfachen Ereignissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steering the frame on simple events is called the most effective training; it results in: (1) learning to wake and manage attention; (2) developing the plait, visualisation and intention; (3) switching to active mode and eventually gaining the ability to free oneself from the leading scenario and determine one's reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Members, as yieldings: pmc:TranserfingSimpleEventFrameSteeringYieldsWakingTf, pmc:TranserfingSimpleEventTrainingYieldsPlaitVisualisationTf, pmc:TranserfingSimpleEventTrainingYieldsFreedomScenarioTf, pmc:TranserfingSimpleEventTrainingYieldsDeterminingRealityTf."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 12; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSimpleEventFrameSteeringYieldsWakingTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Simple-event frame steering yields waking and attention control"@en, "Bildsteuerung an einfachen Ereignissen ergibt Erwachen und Aufmerksamkeitskontrolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Training on simple events is said to teach waking and managing attention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLightingCertainEventsTf, pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWakingInTheFilmTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 12; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDevelopedPlaitVisualisationIntentionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Developed plait, visualisation and intention"@en, "Entwickelter Zopf, Visualisierung und Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Strengthened plait, visualisation and intention, claimed as a training result."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 12; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSimpleEventTrainingYieldsPlaitVisualisationTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Simple-event training yields plait, visualisation and intention"@en, "Training an einfachen Ereignissen ergibt Zopf, Visualisierung, Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Training on simple events develops plait, visualisation and intention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLightingCertainEventsTf, pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDevelopedPlaitVisualisationIntentionTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
