pmc:TranserfingSimpleEventTrainingYieldsFreedomScenarioTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Simple-event training yields freedom from the scenario"@en, "Training an einfachen Ereignissen ergibt Freiheit vom Szenario"@de ;
    skos:definition "Training on simple events eventually yields the ability to free oneself from the leading scenario."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLightingCertainEventsTf, pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReleaseScenarioHoldTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 12; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSimpleEventTrainingYieldsDeterminingRealityTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Simple-event training yields determining one's reality"@en, "Training an einfachen Ereignissen ergibt Bestimmen der eigenen Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Training on simple events eventually yields the ability to determine one's reality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLightingCertainEventsTf, pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 12; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingActivatedCharacterNotObeyingScenarioTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The activated one is the only character not obeying the scenario"@en, "Der Aktivierte ist die einzige Figur, die dem Szenario nicht gehorcht"@de ;
    skos:definition "After activation one is the only character in one's surroundings not subject to the external scenario; forgetting oneself and sinking into the film, one at once identifies with it and becomes a dependent part of it, a mannequin. Pulling attention out of the current frame and switching on the lighting of the future frame, one comes alive and moves freely, still in the mannequin but in a different quality, like a shop mannequin stepping off its display and walking away."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 12; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnFrameRateTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Own frame rate out of phase with reality"@en, "Eigene Bildfrequenz außer Phase mit der Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "One remains in the film but drops out of its sequence, as if one's own frame could move freely along the reel; one's frame rate now differs from reality's, which allows detaching from the leading scenario, as a helicopter rotor or bicycle wheel on film seems slowed or reversed when its rotation is out of step with the frames. Manipulations of attention and plait pull one out of reality's frequency and phase."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: честота на кадрите."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 12; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFutureBelongsNobodyUntilSomeoneCreatesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The future belongs to nobody until someone creates it"@en, "Die Zukunft gehört niemandem, bis jemand sie erschafft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Grasping the not-yet-arrived future and trying to influence it pulls one out of the unfolding present. Future reality is recorded in the archive but always multi-variant, not finally determined and created by no one, so for now it belongs to nobody; if someone creates it, it obeys, and if that someone is you, it becomes yours."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 13; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFollowingReplacedAnticipatingTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Following replaced by anticipating"@en, "Folgen wird durch Vorauseilen ersetzt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creating reality is a fundamentally new way of reacting, behaving and existing: attention no longer bogs down in the current frame but strives forward; following is replaced by getting ahead and passive waiting by active influence; one no longer trails reality on a leash but directs and pushes it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 13; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingReworkingRePatterningOneselfBeforeRealityTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Reworking (re-patterning) oneself before reality becomes one's own"@en, "Umarbeitung seiner selbst, bevor die Wirklichkeit einem gehört"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before reality truly becomes one's own, one must carry out one's own reworking; Tufti says she cannot do it for anyone."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: преработване."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingReworkingTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Until one is finally convinced one can create one's reality, it will slip away and not yield." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 13; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingReworkingTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reworking oneself"@en, "Umarbeitung seiner selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "The re-cutting of one's template that each person must carry out alone before reality becomes truly one's own; it is done through the daily training of frame steering and is unfinished while doubt still gnaws."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: преработване (also разработване)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 13; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNotEverythingOnceWhatFitsEverydayTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not everything at once: only what fits everyday experience"@en, "Nicht alles sofort: nur was zur Alltagserfahrung passt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not everything will work, and not immediately; only what agrees with one's everyday experience will succeed."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Not everything will work, and not immediately; only what agrees with one's everyday experience will succeed. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 13; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTemplateReCutDailyPracticeTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The template is re-cut only by daily practice"@en, "Die Schablone wird nur durch tägliche Praxis umgeschnitten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The template can be re-cut only the way it was made, by everyday habitual practice: tracking the upcoming frame, tracking oneself, creating one's reality, repeated constantly until it becomes habit."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingReworkingTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingAttentionTrackingTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Otherwise one learns nothing (Tufti jokingly threatens to turn the failures into shell-less slugs)." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'РАЗРАБОТВАНЕ', p. 13; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ' (Transformation)
#

pmc:TranserfingFrameSteeringTrainingYieldsTransformationFireflyTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Frame-steering training yields transformation into a firefly"@en, "Bildsteuerungstraining ergibt die Verwandlung zum Glühwürmchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steering the frame on simple events (tracking the upcoming frame, tracking oneself, creating reality) is said to transform the practitioner."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingLightingCertainEventsTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFromSnailToFireflyTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 13; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFromSnailToFireflyTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transformation from snail into firefly (luminous being)"@en, "Verwandlung von der Schnecke zum Glühwürmchen (leuchtendes Wesen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Training and reworking are also a transformation: gradually one turns from a snail into a firefly; lighting the frame, one emits an inner light and wished-for events fly toward one like midges. Tufti says the Creator conceived people as luminous forward-looking beings, as they once were before sinking into the illusion of the spectacle; much is lost but something can be regained."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: светулки."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 13; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOthersDrawnCloserCuriosityWishedEventsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Others are drawn closer with curiosity; wished events fly toward you"@en, "Andere kommen neugierig näher; gewünschte Ereignisse fliegen zu"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced signs: people who remain snails will stretch their horns toward you and crawl closer with curiosity; when you light the frame you radiate inner light and desired events come flying to you."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced signs: people who remain snails will stretch their horns toward you and crawl closer with curiosity; when you light the frame you radiate inner light and desired events come flying to you. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 13; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWormDoubtReworkingNotYetCompleteTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The worm of doubt: reworking not yet complete"@en, "Der Wurm des Zweifels: Umarbeitung noch nicht abgeschlossen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sign it has not yet worked: at first not everything succeeds; one may understand that one can create reality while a worm of doubt gnaws somewhere deep in consciousness; this means the reworking is not finished, which is why the training is needed to bring one into active mode, teach looking ahead and finally convince one."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Sign it has not yet worked: at first not everything succeeds; one may understand that one can create reality while a worm of doubt gnaws somewhere deep in consciousness; this means the reworking is not finished, which is why the training is needed to bring one into active mode, teach looking ahead and finally convince one. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingAttentionTrackingTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingReworkingTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 13; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTryWithoutEffortNoStrainingTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Try without effort; no straining"@en, "Sich bemühen ohne Anstrengung; kein Anspannen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One must be diligent without exerting effort; for successful lighting of the frame concentration matters, not effort; a few minutes or even one minute of concentration is all that is asked; perform the algorithm calmly and naturally; straining is forbidden outright, because effort engages the inner centre of intention while reality is steered by the outer one."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 13; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTenseMusclesWhileLightingFrameInnerTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tense muscles while lighting the frame: the inner centre is working"@en, "Angespannte Muskeln beim Beleuchten: das innere Zentrum arbeitet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Diagnostic sign of a wrong execution: if muscles tense during lighting of the frame, the narrow-minded inner intention is at work; one must work exclusively with the outer centre, the plait, which is not to be strained or acted with."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Diagnostic sign of a wrong execution: if muscles tense during lighting of the frame, the narrow-minded inner intention is at work; one must work exclusively with the outer centre, the plait, which is not to be strained or acted with. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 14; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingEffortlessPlaitActivationTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Effortless plait activation and ordering of the frame"@en, "Müheloses Aktivieren des Zopfes und Bestellen des Bildes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Activate the plait lightly and without effort: it is enough to remember it, feel it and calmly concentrate on it. Then, without interrupting the sensation of the plait, concentrate on the frame you want to order and just as lightly picture the desired scene. Keep muscles relaxed; they are not needed. What is needed is calm concentration on plait and frame; the thought-stream is released from the back, from the plait, not from the forehead."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 14; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAllowRealityComeRatherThanForceTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Allow reality to come rather than force it; operator and spectator"@en, "Die Wirklichkeit kommen lassen statt sie zu zwingen; Kameramann und Zuschauer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The task is not to force reality to submit but to let it come by itself; force will not compel it. The principle is not to grapple with reality but only to illuminate it with the outer centre. One is at once camera operator and spectator: projecting the frame from behind, watching the film in front, as if uninvolved; one only lights the frame and it materialises by itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 14; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOuterCentreNearHigherSelfTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The outer centre is near the so-called higher Self"@en, "Das äußere Zentrum liegt nahe dem sogenannten höheren Selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "The outer centre feels as if it is one's own and at the same time not; being uninvolved matters because only then the outer, not the inner, centre works, a quite different mechanism. The outer centre is close to one's so-called higher Self, and one is governed from this centre."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: висш Аз."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 14; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlaitHookTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The plait tip as the hook of the puppet"@en, "Das Zopfende als Haken der Marionette"@de ;
    skos:definition "The tip of the plait is a hook by which one can be led like a marionette; unaware, one is led by the scenario or by puppeteers manipulating one's consciousness; once aware, the hook is at one's own disposal and one can move oneself by it. Ordinarily one flails trying to shift what lies ahead, not noticing being held by the scruff from behind; thus the illusion of the spectacle arises."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: кукичка."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPuppetStrings: the strings there are the channels of pendulums; the hook here is one point, the tip of the plait."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 14; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPuppeteersTf a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Puppeteers who manipulate consciousness"@en, "Puppenspieler, die das Bewusstsein manipulieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text names puppeteers who, alongside the scenario, lead unaware people by the hook at the plait tip, manipulating their consciousness; no further identification in this range."@en ;
    skos:note "Typed as a naming: the text holds the puppeteers to be agents that manipulate consciousness and lead the unaware by the hook; it says nothing more about them in this part."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "кукловодите (puppeteers)" ;
    pm:nameRole "manipulators of consciousness who, beside the scenario, lead the unaware by the hook at the plait tip" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 14; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBeingAwareBeforeHookDisposalTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Being aware before the hook is at one's disposal"@en, "Bewusstheit, bevor der Haken verfügbar ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "The hook becomes available only once one is aware."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingTakingHoldOwnHookInvertedSpectacleTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingStateOfAwarenessTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Unaware, one is led by the hook by the scenario or the puppeteers." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 14; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTakingHoldOwnHookInvertedSpectacleTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Taking hold of one's own hook: the inverted spectacle"@en, "Den eigenen Haken ergreifen: das umgekehrte Schauspiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gripping the hook oneself, one moves reality without effort and as if doing nothing; the illusion of the spectacle turns inside out: one is not moved but moves oneself; one does not do something to reality, it does itself. The illusion falls apart."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 14; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingEffortlessPlaitWorkYieldsTakingHoldTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Effortless plait work yields taking hold of the hook"@en, "Müheloses Zopfarbeiten ergibt das Ergreifen des Hakens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calm, effortless lighting from the plait is said to invert the spectacle so that reality makes itself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEffortlessPlaitActivationTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingTakingHoldOwnHookInvertedSpectacleTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРЕОБРАЗЯВАНЕ', p. 14; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'МЕТАСИЛА' (Metapower)
#

pmc:TranserfingCreateStepAsideLikeBystanderTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Create and step aside like a bystander"@en, "Erschaffen und zurücktreten wie ein Unbeteiligter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allow reality to fulfil the order: one only lights the frame and it materialises in turn; all that is required is to create one's reality and step back like a bystander, not interfering or getting under its feet."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МЕТАСИЛА', p. 14; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPhysicalForceWillpowerWorkCurrentFrameTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Physical force and willpower work only in the current frame"@en, "Körperkraft und Willenskraft wirken nur im aktuellen Bild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Physical strength, like willpower, works only in the reality of the current frame; one may fight realised actuality with all one's might, but with future reality this will not work; something else is needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie: force and willpower are confined to the current frame."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МЕТАСИЛА', p. 14; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMetapowerTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Metapower"@en, "Metakraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "There is a reverse side of power, metapower: in a sense the antipode of power, yet not weakness or apathy but something acting from the reverse side of reality. Metapower is understood only once felt, as strength cannot be explained to someone who never tried it; it must be felt and developed; its weapon is the plait. The frame-lighting algorithm is said to be the exercise that develops it."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: метасила."@en ;
    skos:note "Pass A recorded the concept and the capacity separately; they are one node here, which the yielding targets."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МЕТАСИЛА', p. 15; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingInvertedMirrorOfRealityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mirror of reality, inverted"@en, "Der Spiegel der Wirklichkeit, umgekehrt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not only the tangible is real: if an image is real, its reflection is too. The mirror of reality is inverted relative to an ordinary mirror: the reflection is tangible and lies on the front side, the image intangible on the reverse. The front side is material actuality, the reverse the dream space or archive of reels. The reel is primary and the film secondary, so actuality is a reflection of an image on the reverse side, where the many variants of the future also lie. Hence the future cannot be influenced by ordinary force, which acts only on the front side; one must act from the reverse side and by its laws."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: огледалото на реалността."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingDualMirrorCh18: image and reflection change sides; the tangible side is the reflection and the archive holds the image."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МЕТАСИЛА', p. 15; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOrdinaryForceFutureBurstingStrainNothingTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Ordinary force on the future: bursting with strain for nothing"@en, "Gewöhnliche Kraft auf die Zukunft: vor Anstrengung platzen ohne Ergebnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warning: applying ordinary force to the future, one can burst from strain and achieve nothing; to avoid this one must act from the reverse side of the mirror."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МЕТАСИЛА', p. 15; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingVirtualMannequinTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking means falling into the mirror; the virtual mannequin"@en, "Erwachen heißt in den Spiegel fallen; das virtuelle Mannequin"@de ;
    skos:definition "On waking and unsticking from the scenario one actually falls into the mirror; this is invisible because its surface is no wall but an intangible border of transition between image and reflection. Both sides look identical, material on one, not on the other: on the front the material mannequin, on the reverse the virtual one. On waking attention crosses the border into its virtual mannequin; not the body moves but attention, which suffices because attention is oneself. Both bodies move in sync; if attention is on the front side, in the frame of realisation, the scenario holds one wholly; if on the reverse, in the frame of the image, one is free to move oneself and future reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: виртуален манекен."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МЕТАСИЛА', p. 15; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMovingOneselfVersusMovingRealityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Moving oneself versus moving reality"@en, "Sich selbst bewegen gegenüber die Wirklichkeit bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving oneself means being aware and wilfully steering one's motives and actions, moving inside the frame as usual with hands, feet and force; reality is moved in quite another way, with attention, intention and metapower."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МЕТАСИЛА', p. 15; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFeelingMetapowerPrecedesUnderstandingTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling metapower precedes understanding it"@en, "Das Spüren der Metakraft geht ihrem Verstehen voraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Understanding of metapower comes only after it has been felt and developed through practice."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingMetapowerTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МЕТАСИЛА', p. 15; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmYieldsMetapowerTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Frame-lighting algorithm yields metapower"@en, "Bildbeleuchtungsalgorithmus ergibt Metakraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The algorithm of lighting the frame is called an exercise for developing metapower and at the same time a way to create the needed reality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingMetapowerTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МЕТАСИЛА', p. 15; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmYieldsCreatingNeededTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Frame-lighting algorithm yields creating needed reality"@en, "Bildbeleuchtungsalgorithmus ergibt das Erschaffen der benötigten Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The same algorithm is said to be a way to create the reality one needs."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МЕТАСИЛА', p. 15; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ' (Imitating the spectacle)
#

pmc:TranserfingWakingVersusFallingAsleepTwoPassagesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking versus falling asleep: two passages into the mirror"@en, "Erwachen und Einschlafen: zwei Übergänge in den Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "One falls into the mirror world every night on falling asleep as well. On waking in daytime, attention in the centre of awareness, the I ends up in the virtual mannequin on the reverse side; awake, both sides are one reality, material and virtual. In sleep they are asymmetric: the material world stays put while attention flies off to other worlds. Moreover, in sleep one sinks still deeper into the scenario, whereas waking in daytime unsticks one from it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 16; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingHookFreeLeadsMaterialMannequinOneselfTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "With the hook free, one leads one's material mannequin oneself"@en, "Mit freiem Haken führt man sein materielles Mannequin selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "When unaware the scenario leads one by the plait tip; when the hook is at one's disposal and one is in the virtual mannequin on the other side, one leads the material mannequin oneself, and so gains the possibility to move both oneself and future reality at will, precisely because one is on the other side."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 16; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImageMovesReflectionNotReverseIncarnationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The image moves the reflection, not the reverse; incarnation vs image"@en, "Das Bild bewegt die Spiegelung, nicht umgekehrt; Verkörperung und Bild"@de ;
    skos:definition "The image can move the reflection, not the other way round. More precisely, the material mannequin and actuality are less a reflection than an incarnation of the image. Realised reality can be coped with somehow in the frame of incarnation on the front side; future reality is so far only image and can be steered only in the frame of the image, on the reverse side. Here one copes, there one steers."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: кадъра на образа."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 16; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTransferMirrorWorldSteerFutureTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Transfer into the mirror world to steer the future"@en, "Übergang in die Spiegelwelt, um die Zukunft zu steuern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steering future reality requires transferring attention into the mirror world (the frame of the image)."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingStateOfAwarenessTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "From the front side force cannot be applied to an immaterial object; the future image cannot be steered from there." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 16; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImitationOfTheSpectacleTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spectacle here, imitation of the spectacle there; the scenario as objective reality"@en, "Schauspiel hier, Nachahmung des Schauspiels dort; das Szenario als objektive Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "On the front side force acts and there is the spectacle; on the other metapower and an imitation of the spectacle. One has no right to break the established order: one must take part in the spectacle obeying the scenario; no character may jump off the reel or do as it likes there. The scenario is not anyone's subjective will but objective reality that cannot be escaped; disagreeing, complaining or disobeying is useless; what is recorded on the reel will happen. One cannot flee the spectacle, but can imitate it, i.e. deceive reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: имитация на спектакъла."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 16; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingImitationGameTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The game of imitation"@en, "Das Spiel der Nachahmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enter the point of awareness and so be on the other side of the mirror (everything looks as before, no sense of watching through glass). From there create your reality by choosing a reel: not changing the one you are in or leaving its spectacle, but selecting another you need. Meanwhile keep playing your scripted role and everyday functions, as if standing aside, pretending not to be alive while walking in the film as a character come alive, and change reels at will; order stays unbroken, nobody notices."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: игра на имитиране."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 16; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImitationAwarenessPointYieldsChoosingNewTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Imitation from the awareness point yields choosing a new reel"@en, "Nachahmung vom Bewusstheitspunkt aus ergibt die Wahl einer neuen Rolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being on the other side of the mirror in the point of awareness is said to give the ability to choose the reel one needs."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingImitationGameTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWalkingAliveRealityChoosingNewReelTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 16; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingChangingCurrentReelJumpingBetweenReelsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Changing the current reel (jumping between reels)"@en, "Die aktuelle Filmrolle wechseln (zwischen Rollen springen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the state of awareness, unlike other characters, one gains the possibility of changing the current reel while staying as if on the sidelines, and things arrange themselves according to one's wish."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 16; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImitationGameYieldsChangingReelsTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Imitation game yields changing reels"@en, "Nachahmungsspiel ergibt Rollenwechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Playing the role while choosing another reel from the awareness point is said to change reels unnoticed."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingImitationGameTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingChangingCurrentReelJumpingBetweenReelsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 16; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityInitiatesNewScenarioStillTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating reality initiates a new scenario, still not one's own"@en, "Wirklichkeit erschaffen startet ein neues Szenario, das auch nicht das eigene ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "One cannot escape the scenario; creating one's reality initiates a new one, which also is not one's own and still holds power over one, but it leads to the desired result."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotAdvertiseYourAbilitiesTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not advertise your abilities"@en, "Die eigenen Fähigkeiten nicht zur Schau stellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "However much one wants to stand out, one should not flaunt these abilities or betray one's presence; in the Middle Ages one was burned for it, now one might be put in a mental institution."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingImitationGameTf, pmc:TranserfingChangingCurrentReelJumpingBetweenReelsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ' (Presence)
#

pmc:TranserfingPresenceTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Presence in the film"@en, "Präsenz im Film"@de ;
    skos:definition "Presence means first the presence of one's awareness, one's I: being present in oneself as a living, aware, sane individual in an unchangeable film that, though dynamic, is already laid out along with all its characters' behaviour. Presence marks one as awake among sleepers; one's behaviour inside the given film is still scripted, but presence makes it possible to change the reel, to jump from one to another."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: присъствие."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingEnteringPresenceTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Entering presence"@en, "In die Präsenz eintreten"@de ;
    skos:definition "To enter presence: come alive, shake off sleep and determine where you are, in the frame of the image or the frame of incarnation; in other words, whether attention is in the central point of awareness or on one of the screens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDualBeingsPresentHereWhenThereTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dual beings: present here when there"@en, "Duale Wesen: hier anwesend, wenn man dort ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "People are by nature dual, capable of being on this or that side of the mirror; paradoxically, presence on this side depends on being on the other side; otherwise one is absent, in an insane state entirely ruled by the scenario."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNightDreamsVirtualRealityCanMovedTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "In night dreams only virtual reality can be moved"@en, "Im Nachttraum lässt sich nur virtuelle Wirklichkeit bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Falling asleep and dreaming, attention crosses into the virtual mannequin as on waking, but in a different quality: in dreams one can move only the virtual reality; influencing actuality from that state is possible but complicated, no job for snails."@en ;
    skos:note "Text layer: the Bulgarian says that from the night dream the virtual actuality cannot be influenced, then that it can, with difficulty; the sense requires material actuality, as the capacity pmc:TranserfingMovingActualityFromTheDreamTf reads it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMovingActualityFromTheDreamTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Moving actuality from the night dream"@en, "Die Wirklichkeit aus dem Nachttraum bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "From the night dream, where only virtual reality is ordinarily moved, influencing material actuality is held possible but hard, no task for beginners."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes. No practice for it is given in this part."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingPresenceCreatingFutureRealityWillTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking presence: creating future reality that will be realised"@en, "Präsenz im Wachen: künftige Wirklichkeit erschaffen, die sich verwirklicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the state of waking presence one gains the ability to create future reality that will come to be; Tufti stresses that it can and must be created."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingEnteringPresenceYieldsCapacityWakingPresenceTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Entering presence yields the capacity of waking presence"@en, "Eintritt in die Präsenz ergibt die Fähigkeit der Wachpräsenz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shaking off sleep and placing attention in the centre is said to give the state in which future reality can be created."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEnteringPresenceTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWakingPresenceCreatingFutureRealityWillTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTargetFrameTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating defines the target frame, not the chain of events"@en, "Erschaffen bestimmt das Zielbild, nicht die Ereigniskette"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creating reality determines not the chain of events but the end goal, the upcoming frame; it is not steering the scenario but choosing the reel. The scenario is not in one's power and one is not given to know what it should be to reach the goal, nor is that needed: one works as a projector; when it lights the target frame, events develop exactly in the needed direction. The chosen reel brings a new scenario already recorded on it, without one's knowing; only the target frame is one's own, the reel selects itself according to the ordered frame, and how this happens one need not know."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: целевия кадър."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingRelightingTheTargetFrameTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Light the target frame again and again"@en, "Das Zielbild immer wieder beleuchten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep lighting the target frame again and again; in this way one moves from reel to reel and finally arrives at the destination. Fix attention on the future frame; the scenario is not one's business."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingParallelReelsDifferingSmallNuancesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Parallel reels differing by small nuances"@en, "Parallele Filmrollen, die sich in Nuancen unterscheiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the archive the reels lie in parallel and the scenarios of neighbouring reels differ in small nuances; creating reality one moves gradually from one to the next, unnoticed, with a speed of realisation depending on the goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingResultsApproachIntendedStepStepTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Results approach the intended one step by step"@en, "Ergebnisse nähern sich schrittweise dem Beabsichtigten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced course: at first one lands on a reel where the result is close to the intended but not quite the same, then ever closer; simple goals are reached almost at once, hard ones need time and patience."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced course: at first one lands on a reel where the result is close to the intended but not quite the same, then ever closer; simple goals are reached almost at once, hard ones need time and patience. It bears on pmp:TranserfingRelightingTheTargetFrameTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingHardGoalsTakeTimePatienceTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hard goals take time and patience"@en, "Schwere Ziele brauchen Zeit und Geduld"@de ;
    skos:definition "Timing condition: difficult goals are not realised at once; they require time and patience, the speed of realisation depending on the goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Timing condition: difficult goals are not realised at once; they require time and patience, the speed of realisation depending on the goal. It bears on pmp:TranserfingRelightingTheTargetFrameTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 17; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTryingCreateOrResistScenarioTrapsTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Trying to create or resist the scenario traps you"@en, "Wer das Szenario erschaffen oder ihm widerstehen will, sitzt in der Falle"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one tries to create the scenario or oppose it, it traps one: trying to influence the course of events one clings tooth and nail to the reality of the current frame, which is pointless; the harder one holds on, the more firmly one is held by the scruff, i.e. by the plait."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingRelightingTheTargetFrameTf, pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 18; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotTryInfluencePeopleTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not try to influence people"@en, "Nicht versuchen, Menschen zu beeinflussen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trying to influence people is equally pointless, thankless and ignoble; it can backfire or have the reverse effect, since characters act by their own scenario; struggling to influence them one falls into the trap again. Tufti says they will come by themselves and do what one wants (to be explained later). One must influence neither events nor people but the end result, the upcoming frame."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 18; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingStubbornlyInsistingOwnPlanTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Stubbornly insisting on one's own plan"@en, "Hartnäckig auf dem eigenen Plan bestehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Out of habit one will keep trying to influence events and insist that everything go according to one's plan; this habit must be beaten out."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Out of habit one will keep trying to influence events and insist that everything go according to one's plan; this habit must be beaten out. It bears on pmp:TranserfingRelightingTheTargetFrameTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПРИСЪСТВИЕ', p. 18; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ПОЛЗАТА' (Benefit)
#

pmc:TranserfingScenarioLikeCobwebTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The scenario is like a cobweb"@en, "Das Szenario ist wie ein Spinnennetz"@de ;
    skos:definition "The scenario is never one's own, even when one thinks one invented it; changing or resisting it traps one. It is like a cobweb: the more actively one resists the tighter one is caught; to be released one must release it. One cannot free oneself wholly from it, nor is hiding needed: the scenario works for one's goal if one orders it, adjusting to the order even when it seems otherwise; all that is required is systematically lighting the target frame."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: паяжина."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 18; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingInsistingPlanHindersRealisationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Insisting on the plan hinders realisation"@en, "Das Bestehen auf dem Plan behindert die Verwirklichung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Insisting that everything go exactly by one's plan prevents what was intended from coming true."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Insisting that everything go exactly by one's plan prevents what was intended from coming true. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 18; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingScenarioTakesPathLeastResistanceNonTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The scenario takes the path of least resistance; non-acceptance creates worse reality"@en, "Das Szenario nimmt den Weg des geringsten Widerstands; Nichtannahme erschafft schlechtere Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even when one drifts passively, the scenario does not want to harm, since harm takes much energy; it always follows the path of least resistance. Resisting spoils everything: expressing non-acceptance, one involuntarily and unconsciously creates a worse reality, less efficiently than with intention, awareness or the plait, but still; and one expresses non-acceptance whenever something does not fit one's ideas and plans."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: неприемане."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOptimalityPrinciple: least resistance is a property of the scenario, which spares harm because harm costs energy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 18; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNonAcceptanceSpoilsRealityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Non-acceptance spoils reality"@en, "Nichtannahme verdirbt die Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Expressed non-acceptance of what does not match one's plans unintentionally creates a worse reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Expressed non-acceptance of what does not match one's plans unintentionally creates a worse reality. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 18; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingPrincipleOfBenefitTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Principle of benefit: extract use from everything"@en, "Prinzip des Nutzens: aus allem Nutzen ziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Adopt a simple principle: find benefit in everything; literally draw use from every irritating situation, from every event that provokes even the smallest non-acceptance; set this as a goal. Every event has positive as well as negative traits (reality is in many respects dual). To make it work, wake in time and move attention to the centre. Activators here are mainly external (someone says or does something, something suddenly happens, anything provoking non-acceptance from mild displeasure to rage); activating feelings can also be irritation, dejection, anxiety, aggression and fear. Then pause for a moment and ask yourself what benefit you can extract, and do not resist the scenario but try to follow it."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: да извличате полза."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingIntentionCh13: no weighing of importance; one asks what benefit can be drawn and agrees."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 18; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWakeTimeBeforeApplyingBenefitPrincipleTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Wake in time before applying the benefit principle"@en, "Rechtzeitig erwachen, bevor das Nutzenprinzip greift"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the benefit principle to work one must wake in time and move attention to the centre."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingPrincipleOfBenefitTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingShiftingAttentionToTheCentreTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Otherwise it does not work: one reflexively resists on the standard reel." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 19; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingStandardReelVersusAlternativeReelBenefitTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Standard reel versus alternative reel of benefit"@en, "Standardrolle gegenüber alternativer Rolle des Nutzens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving attention to the centre unsticks one from the present reel's scenario so one can jump to an alternative reel. On the habitual reel the habitual scenario runs: reflexive resistance out of bad character, negativism, defensive habit, self-importance or because things do not go one's way, which sours life for oneself and others. On the alternative reel things go in one's favour because one paused at the right moment and opted for benefit; the choice made is the result received."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 19; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLivingReelWhereEventsDevelopFavourTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living on a reel where events develop in one's favour"@en, "Auf einer Rolle leben, auf der sich alles zum eigenen Vorteil entwickelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The claimed result of the benefit principle: transferring to an alternative reel where everything turns out to one's advantage, turning one's reality into a world pleasant in every respect."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 19; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBenefitPrincipleYieldsFavourableReelTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Benefit principle yields the favourable reel"@en, "Nutzenprinzip ergibt die günstige Rolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choosing the benefit at the activating moment is said to shift one onto the favourable reel."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPrincipleOfBenefitTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingLivingReelWhereEventsDevelopFavourTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 19; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingAlgorithmOfBenefitTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Algorithm of benefit"@en, "Algorithmus des Nutzens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not resist the scenario but try to follow it, literally: take the advice, listen to the opinion, agree to something, accept what you would formerly have refused or confronted. Steps: (1) become aware that non-acceptance has been triggered; (2) wake: I see myself and reality; (3) ask yourself what benefit you can extract; (4) if you find an answer, agree and take the benefit; (5) if you find none, try to agree anyway."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: алгоритъмът на ползата."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 19; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfRaisedObjectionNotEverythingShouldTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Self-raised objection: not everything should be agreed to"@en, "Selbst erhobener Einwand: nicht allem sollte man zustimmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti raises the doubt herself that one should not agree with everything and not every situation holds a benefit (should one offer one's horns to someone about to hit them?), and answers with the law that follows."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAlgorithmOfBenefitTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 19; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBenefitPrincipleYieldsFewerHarmfulSituationsTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Benefit principle yields fewer harmful situations"@en, "Nutzenprinzip ergibt weniger schädliche Situationen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the benefit principle is said, by a law of reality, to reduce harmful situations."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAlgorithmOfBenefitTf, pmp:TranserfingPrincipleOfBenefitTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEverFewerHarmfulSituationsLifeTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 19; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingEverFewerHarmfulSituationsLifeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ever fewer harmful situations in life"@en, "Immer weniger schädliche Situationen im Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text claims an inviolable law of reality: whoever is guided by the principle of benefit will meet ever fewer situations bringing harm, including fatal ones."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЛЗАТА', p. 19; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ' (Allowing)
#

pmc:TranserfingParadoxicalPrincipleCreateTargetFrameNotTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Paradoxical principle: create the target frame, not the scenario"@en, "Paradoxes Prinzip: das Zielbild erschaffen, nicht das Szenario"@de ;
    skos:definition "One must create not the scenario but the target frame; paradoxical because it contradicts the old belief that one can and must fight what has happened while the future cannot be created; in fact it is the reverse. One is not given to know how the goal will be reached, and need not, especially at first; one cannot know which scenario would bring one to one's goal since one is a character led by a scenario. One's job is to know the result and create the corresponding picture of reality in thoughts, words and images using the plait; then the scenario leads and shows the way. One need not be clever, only goal-directed and aware."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 19; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAskingHowFearAnswersBlocksCreationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Asking how: fear of the answers blocks creation"@en, "Die Wie-Frage: Angst vor den Antworten blockiert das Erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the likely answers to the question of how the goal will be achieved throw one into horror or despondency, the ability to create the target reality is psychologically blocked."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If the likely answers to the question of how the goal will be achieved throw one into horror or despondency, the ability to create the target reality is psychologically blocked. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 19; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOnceGoalSetScenarioMayShockTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Once the goal is set, the scenario may shock: all seems to fall apart"@en, "Ist das Ziel gesetzt, kann das Szenario schockieren: alles scheint zu zerfallen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warning: once a goal is set the scenario may shock one; it will seem everything is falling apart, a perfectly possible course of events; awareness is then needed to apply the benefit principle."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingParadoxicalPrincipleCreateTargetFrameNotTf, pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingApparentCollapseMeansOldRubbishBeingTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Apparent collapse means old rubbish is being cleared"@en, "Scheinbarer Zerfall heißt, alter Unrat wird entfernt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced interpretation: when after setting a goal everything seems to fall apart, in fact old junk is being cleared from one's reality to fill the freed space with beautiful new things; the recap calls this useful, reality is being cleansed."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced interpretation: when after setting a goal everything seems to fall apart, in fact old junk is being cleared from one's reality to fill the freed space with beautiful new things; the recap calls this useful, reality is being cleansed. It bears on pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf, pmp:TranserfingRelightingTheTargetFrameTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBenefitPrincipleSpeedsMovementTowardGoalTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Benefit principle speeds movement toward the goal"@en, "Nutzenprinzip beschleunigt die Bewegung zum Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting by the benefit principle not only avoids hindering the scenario but accelerates progress to the goal, because taking benefit unsticks one from the usual harmful scenario onto a useful reel, even without the plait; done with the plait it goes faster and better."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAlgorithmOfBenefitTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTrackingBenefitYieldsWakingTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tracking benefit yields waking"@en, "Nutzenverfolgung ergibt Erwachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tracking the benefit is called one of the ways of waking up: events should not lull one but put one on alert as wake-up signals."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAlgorithmOfBenefitTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWakingInTheFilmTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingExclaimingBenefitTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exclaim \"Benefit!\" and allow"@en, "„Nutzen!“ ausrufen und zulassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whereas formerly one shouted, waved and stamped when something went wrong, now, as soon as something is wrong, exclaim (silently or aloud) the word for benefit, and then allow the world to do something pleasant for you, help you or bring you closer to the goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Ползата!."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingAllowingTheWorldCh18: allowing follows a spoken cue, and the text bounds it at once."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAllowingDoesNotMeanBowingEverythingTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Allowing does not mean bowing to everything"@en, "Zulassen heißt nicht, sich allem zu beugen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allowing does not mean becoming Permission itself and bending under everything and everyone; not everything holds a benefit and not everything should be allowed or agreed to; one will be able to decide adequately whether to allow, because one will be sane: seeing oneself and reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Позволение."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingExclaimingBenefitTf, pmp:TranserfingAlgorithmOfBenefitTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFightOrSubmitUnconsciouslyVersusConsciousTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fight or submit unconsciously versus conscious choice in presence"@en, "Unbewusst kämpfen oder sich fügen gegenüber bewusster Wahl in Präsenz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordinarily one either meets things with a knife or submits spinelessly, both unconsciously following the scenario; with the benefit algorithm one makes a conscious choice in the state of presence, walking in the frozen cinema as a living character while pretending not to be alive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBenefitUnitesTheElementsTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The benefit principle unites tracking, imitation, presence and creation"@en, "Das Nutzenprinzip vereint Verfolgung, Nachahmung, Präsenz und Erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti presents the benefit principle as combining all prior elements: tracking (of oneself and reality), imitation (obeying the scenario but independently, deliberately, consciously, imitation in pure form), presence, and creating reality (determining the direction of the next frame)."@en ;
    skos:note "Members: pmp:TranserfingAttentionTrackingTf, pmp:TranserfingImitationGameTf, pmc:TranserfingPresenceTf, pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf, gathered in pmp:TranserfingAlgorithmOfBenefitTf."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingPeekingWithOneEyeTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Peeking with one eye: present but uninterested"@en, "Mit einem Auge spähen: anwesend, aber unbeteiligt"@de ;
    skos:definition "While tracking the benefit, peek into reality as if with one eye: like all sleepers, diligently play your role and do daily duties, while watching events from the corner of your eye; be present without betraying presence, remaining unnoticed and uninterested (disinterested)."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: незаинтересовани."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDisinterestMainPrincipleLiveWalkFilmTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Disinterest as the main principle of the live walk in the film, two reasons"@en, "Unbeteiligtheit als Grundprinzip des lebendigen Gangs im Film, zwei Gründe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being disinterested is called the basic principle of the live walk in the film, for two reasons: (1) not to betray one's presence, so others do not treat one with suspicion and caution, pretending to sleep; (2) not to act by direct attack, gripping reality by the throat and fighting events and characters in the current frame, which would sink one back into the scenario like sleep. One walks live in the film by being present with attention and moves the future frame and changes the reel with intention, the outer one."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: разходката на живо във филма."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNoDirectAttackRealityTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No direct attack on reality"@en, "Kein direkter Angriff auf die Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not act by direct assault, seizing reality by the throat and fighting events and characters in the current frame; one ends up sunk in the scenario again as in sleep."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingPeekingWithOneEyeTf, pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingEngagingOuterCentreIntentionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Engaging the outer centre of intention"@en, "Das äußere Zentrum der Absicht in Gang setzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Engagement of the outer centre of intention, which is the main one for moving the future frame; the text says it is engaged by watching from the corner of the eye while staying disinterested."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDisinterestedPeekingYieldsEngagingOuterCentreTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Disinterested peeking yields engaging the outer centre"@en, "Unbeteiligtes Spähen ergibt das Einschalten des äußeren Zentrums"@de ;
    skos:definition "Peeking from the corner of the eye and staying disinterested is said to set the outer centre of intention working."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPeekingWithOneEyeTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEngagingOuterCentreIntentionTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОЗВОЛЕНИЕ', p. 20; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'СЦЕНАРИЯТ' (The scenario)
#

pmc:TranserfingNotWakingBenefitRecognisedTooLateTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not waking: the benefit is recognised too late"@en, "Nicht erwacht: der Nutzen wird zu spät erkannt"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one does not wake and take the benefit, one will in many cases realise what the benefit was only too late, when recalling what and how one resisted and then missed the chance or got rapped on the horns."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If one does not wake and take the benefit, one will in many cases realise what the benefit was only too late, when recalling what and how one resisted and then missed the chance or got rapped on the horns. It bears on pmp:TranserfingAlgorithmOfBenefitTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЦЕНАРИЯТ', p. 21; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingForgettingRememberingLateUntilTrackingBecomesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forgetting and remembering late until tracking becomes habit"@en, "Vergessen und verspätetes Erinnern, bis die Verfolgung Gewohnheit wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "One will forget and remember belatedly many more times until tracking attention becomes a habit."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: One will forget and remember belatedly many more times until tracking attention becomes a habit. It bears on pmp:TranserfingAttentionTrackingTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЦЕНАРИЯТ', p. 21; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSnailUnconsciousQuestionWhyThingsNotTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The snail's unconscious question: why are things not as I want?"@en, "Die unbewusste Frage der Schnecke: warum ist es nicht, wie ich will?"@de ;
    skos:definition "The simplest and most important question tormenting people unawares is why things are not as they want; the answer is that the scenario leads them, they do not know it and do not create reality but live in it like fish in an aquarium."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЦЕНАРИЯТ', p. 21; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingForgettingAttentionProvesScenarioLeadsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forgetting attention proves the scenario leads"@en, "Das Vergessen der Aufmerksamkeit beweist, dass das Szenario führt"@de ;
    skos:definition "That one is constantly in an insane state and only occasionally wakes to realise one slept proves the scenario leads one; one forgets attention not from absent-mindedness but precisely because the scenario is leading."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЦЕНАРИЯТ', p. 21; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFilmExistsBecauseRealityHasFilmTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Film exists because reality has a film aspect; film as model of reality"@en, "Film existiert, weil die Wirklichkeit eine Filmseite hat; Film als Modell der Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Film characters revive whenever someone watches, even if the actors are long dead. Film was invented not as a pure invention but because such an aspect of reality exists; one cannot invent anything not in manifest or yet unmanifest reality; people have film only because they live in one; film is a model of reality. That characters (people) have self-awareness unlike film heroes is a paradox, a joke of reality and a chance."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: филмът е модел."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЦЕНАРИЯТ', p. 21; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDayRealityScenarioWillTrulyShockTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One day the reality of the scenario will truly shock you"@en, "Eines Tages wird einen die Wirklichkeit des Szenarios wirklich schockieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: people are not shocked by the idea of a scenario because the illusion is strong and they take it as a joke or esoteric nonsense; even believing it they do not fully realise it; perhaps one day, after all their experiments with reality, a moment will come when they realise it and are truly shocked."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced: people are not shocked by the idea of a scenario because the illusion is strong and they take it as a joke or esoteric nonsense; even believing it they do not fully realise it; perhaps one day, after all their experiments with reality, a moment will come when they realise it and are truly shocked. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFulfillingMomentaryWishesTf, pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЦЕНАРИЯТ', p. 21; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFateGeneralDirectionScenarioStrictProgramTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fate as general direction, scenario as strict program"@en, "Schicksal als allgemeine Richtung, Szenario als strenges Programm"@de ;
    skos:definition "People only vaguely sense the scenario as the phenomenon of fate; but fate is only a general direction that can be chosen as a path, and they worsen it by seeing harm instead of benefit and trying to steer instead of choosing. The scenario is more concrete and strict: a program for all one's behaviour and actions on the given reel; it cannot be steered at all, only another can be chosen by creating the corresponding reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЦЕНАРИЯТ', p. 21; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTemptationSteerScenarioDirectlyTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The temptation to steer the scenario directly"@en, "Die Versuchung, das Szenario direkt zu steuern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The temptation to steer the scenario is great, along with the habit and the illusion of being able to; trying to influence events and people directly is a mistake that drags a series of wrong actions and negative consequences after it: the scenario develops so that clouds gather on the horizon and one ends up like mice in a maze looking for an exit, which is extremely complicated and unproductive."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЦЕНАРИЯТ', p. 21; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDirectInfluenceEventsPeopleBringsNegativeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Direct influence on events and people brings negative consequences"@en, "Direkte Einflussnahme auf Ereignisse und Menschen bringt negative Folgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Failure mechanism: direct influence on events and people sets off wrong actions and negative consequences, the maze situation."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Failure mechanism: direct influence on events and people sets off wrong actions and negative consequences, the maze situation. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFrameLightingAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf; what fails is pmc:TranserfingCreatingRealityTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЦЕНАРИЯТ', p. 21; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingEdgePictureCanGraspedBenefitAspectTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Only the edge of the picture can be grasped; benefit as one aspect"@en, "Nur der Rand des Bildes lässt sich greifen; Nutzen als ein Aspekt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Neither the local scenario nor the general course of events can be influenced directly; one can only catch hold of the edge of the picture of reality and use certain of its aspects, benefit being one of them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЦЕНАРИЯТ', p. 22; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), part 2:
# sections ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ to МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ, pp. 22-43 of the Bulgarian
# e-book (Жрицата Тафти, translated by Vesela Petrova, spiralata.net, 2018),
# the only translation reached.
#
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 257 records, B 235;
# 4 records of B without counterpart in A: 1 added, 3 covered, 0 not owed); a
# reader of the whole part added 3 nodes both passes missed (reality pretending
# to be no film, waiting and hoping as felt unfreedom, the series from
# thought-forms to thought-markers) and 5 nodes that the cautions and chains of
# pass A needed as their objects or steps. Every locus was recomputed from its
# offset.
#
# Stupen' I to V (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl to -5.ttl) are linked,
# not restated: no record of this part repeats a node there in the same form;
# 30 nodes restate an earlier node with a difference and say so in a note.
#
# Shared terms typed here: pmc:TranserfingSparkOfTheCreatorTf,
# pmc:TranserfingOuterPowerTf, pmc:TranserfingPaperManTf,
# pmc:TranserfingRealityMirrorTf, pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheImageTf,
# pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheReflectionTf. Linked, typed by part 1:
# pmc:TranserfingPresenceTf, pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf,
# pmc:TranserfingMetapowerTf, pmc:TranserfingScenarioTf,
# pmc:TranserfingMannequinsTf, pmc:TranserfingWakingInTheFilmTf,
# pmc:TranserfingCentreOfAwarenessTf, pmc:TranserfingTwoScreensTf; the naming
# of Tufti and the receiving are part 1's (pmc:TranserfingTaftiTf,
# pmc:TranserfingTaftiReceivingTf) and are not retyped. Linked, typed by part 3:
# pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsTf, pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersTf. The plait
# algorithm, the activators and imitation are restated here from earlier
# lessons and typed with a note saying so. The polemic against official
# science is a concept, since only the author's side is read.
#


#
# section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ'
#

pmc:TranserfingOnlyTheTargetFrameCanBeCreatedTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unknown script cannot be steered, only the target frame created"@en, "Unbekanntes Drehbuch ist nicht steuerbar, nur der Zielbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because the script of the current reel is unknown, it cannot be controlled; what one can do is create the target frame, which yields a film whose script works for oneself, provided one does not obstruct it."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: целевият кадър."@en ;
    skos:note "The script as a program of behaviour on the reel is linked to pmc:TranserfingScenarioTf, typed by part 1; the target frame is ordered by pmp:TranserfingPlaitAlgorithmTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 22; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeLeversTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three levers available to the awakened character"@en, "Drei Hebel des erwachten Charakters"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti lists the only three things at one's disposal: move the current frame (by creating the target frame), move oneself, and move through oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "The second and third levers are expanded in the following sections (self-development; image and mirror)."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 22; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDevelopmentOrDegradationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Law: no development means degradation"@en, "Gesetz: ohne Entwicklung Verfall"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nature made each person perfect including flaws; one should change without betraying one's own core, since wherever there is no development degradation sets in."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 22; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingSelfDevelopmentTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Physical and spiritual self-development"@en, "Körperliche und geistige Selbstentwicklung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Work on oneself continuously, developing both body and spirit; the physical side is left to the reader's own knowledge, the spiritual side is the firefly practice (pmp:TranserfingBecomingAFireflyTf)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 22; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfDevelopmentKindlesTheSparkTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Self-development kindles the Spark"@en, "Selbstentwicklung entfacht den Funken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Developing oneself is said to kindle the Spark of the Creator within."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSelfDevelopmentTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSparkOfTheCreatorTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 22; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSparkOfTheCreatorTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Kindled Spark of the Creator"@en, "Entfachter Funke des Schöpfers"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims every person carries a Spark of the Creator; by developing oneself one kindles it and becomes able to create one's reality and oneself as perfection, as the Creator does."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term from the text: Искрата на Създателя (Spark of the Creator)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 22; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCommandingIsATemptationTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Commanding is a temptation"@en, "Gebieten ist eine Versuchung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Kindle the spark of the Creator, not of a ruler: wanting to command is named as one more temptation to avoid."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingSparkOfTheCreatorTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 22; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCreatorTf a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The (Supreme) Creator"@en, "Der (höchste) Schöpfer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text holds the Supreme Creator to be one who does not command but creates, and who granted humans alone the privilege of changing film reels (see pmc:TranserfingHowTheScriptListensTf)."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Създателя / Върховният Създател" ;
    pm:nameRole "supreme creator who creates rather than commands; source of the human spark and of the reel-changing privilege" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 22; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingBecomingAFireflyTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming a firefly: lighten attention and radiate"@en, "Glühwürmchen werden: Aufmerksamkeit erhellen und ausstrahlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spiritual side of development: illuminate attention by catching it in time and seeing oneself and reality; additionally radiate what attracts, namely joy, love and celebration."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: светулки."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOthersGatherAroundTheRadiantTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Others gather around the radiating person"@en, "Andere sammeln sich um den Ausstrahlenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: the people around come close and gather about one who radiates joy and love."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: The people around come close and gather about one who radiates joy and love. It bears on pmp:TranserfingBecomingAFireflyTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingGlowThatWinsSympathyTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Glow that wins general sympathy"@en, "Leuchten, das allgemeine Sympathie gewinnt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims that tracking attention alone makes one begin to shine, and with radiating one wins common sympathy and becomes a star in the film without changing the reel."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFireflyYieldsGlowTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Firefly practice yields the winning glow"@en, "Glühwürmchen-Praxis ergibt das gewinnende Leuchten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Learning to track attention and direct it into the needed channel, plus radiating, is said to produce the attracting glow."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingBecomingAFireflyTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingGlowThatWinsSympathyTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCreateFirstThenActTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Create first, then act on the new reel"@en, "Erst erschaffen, dann auf der neuen Spule handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "After creating reality and jumping to a new reel, one must still perform what the script requires there: go, speak, act."@en ;
    skos:note "Prior: creating the target frame; dependent: the required ordinary actions in the current frame."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingThirdMovementTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingPlaitAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMentalOrdersAloneNotEnoughTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Mental orders alone are not enough"@en, "Gedankliche Bestellungen allein genügen nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti warns against expecting results from mental instructions while never getting up from the sofa."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingThirdMovementTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBenefitForOthersTooTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Benefit for others as well as oneself"@en, "Nutzen auch für andere"@de ;
    skos:definition "Extract benefit for oneself but let others do the same; benefit for self and others should be the creed."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingStrivingToControlTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ИСКРАТА НА СЪЗДАТЕЛЯ', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА'
#

pmc:TranserfingScriptPlanOfDegradationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Script plan of degradation after age twenty"@en, "Drehbuchplan des Verfalls nach dem zwanzigsten Jahr"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims the main design of the script after one's twentieth year is degradation; the choice is to let the script lead or to take oneself in hand and so slow its execution considerably."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingControlIsParanoiaTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Striving to control the script is a paranoia"@en, "Das Drehbuch steuern wollen ist Paranoia"@de ;
    skos:definition "The wish to manage the script is called the reader's paranoia, and she must keep explaining what not to do."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingStrivingToControlTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingStrivingToControlTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Striving to control the script, events and people"@en, "Streben, Drehbuch, Ereignisse und Menschen zu steuern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The habitual wish to make people and events go one's own way, to force or influence them, accompanied by the tormenting question of how to bring it about; Tufti calls it the reader's paranoia and worst habit."@en ;
    skos:note "Object of the cautions pmc:TranserfingControlIsParanoiaTf, pmc:TranserfingWorstHabitControlTf, pmc:TranserfingResistingTheScriptBringsTroubleTf and pmc:TranserfingBenefitForOthersTooTf; written by the integrator so that these warnings name what they warn against."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNoControllingTheWorld: the control is aimed at the script of the current reel, which cannot be steered."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingHowQuestionSpoilsTheOutcomeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The question \"how?\" spoils the outcome"@en, "Die Frage „wie?“ verdirbt das Ergebnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asking by what means awakens self-consciousness, which then holds one's own considerations about method instead of the goal; the self-invented scenario contradicts the real one and, by insisting on it, one ruins everything."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Asking by what means awakens self-consciousness, which then holds one's own considerations about method instead of the goal; the self-invented scenario contradicts the real one and, by insisting on it, one ruins everything. It bears on pmp:TranserfingActingWithOnlyTheGoalTf."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: по какъв начин?"@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingActingWithOnlyTheGoalTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Acting with only the goal in mind (the jay principle)"@en, "Handeln nur mit dem Ziel im Sinn (Häher-Prinzip)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like the jay acting by instinct: approach the person and, without deliberating, say or do whatever comes to mind, holding only the goal; the one difference from the bird is conscious self-observation, watching attention so it does not slip back into inventing a plan but follows the faint pushes of the script."@en ;
    skos:note "Tufti claims that if only the goal is in one's thoughts, the script itself leads one to it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 23; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalOnlyActionYieldsSensingCommandTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Goal-only action with self-observation yields sensing the command"@en, "Zielhandeln mit Selbstbeobachtung ergibt Spüren des Befehls"@de ;
    skos:definition "Abandoning own motives and deliberately submitting while watching oneself lets the command of the Power be felt."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingActingWithOnlyTheGoalTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSensingTheCommandOfThePowerTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSensingTheCommandOfThePowerTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling the command of the Power"@en, "Den Befehl der Kraft spüren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims one will feel the command of the Power oneself if one consciously and deliberately allows it to lead."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: повелята на Силата."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWalkingPrinciplesAreParadoxicalTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The walking principles are paradoxical"@en, "Die Prinzipien des Gehens sind paradox"@de ;
    skos:definition "The principles of the live walk run against habit: asleep one resists the script, awake one rushes to act by own will; one must instead not resist reflexively but submit on purpose and consciously."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingImitationTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Imitation: the awakened mannequin"@en, "Imitation: die erwachte Schaufensterpuppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Picture oneself as a wax-faced mannequin moving as if on a spring; on entering awareness the eyes light up, but otherwise keep moving mechanically among the others, do as everyone does, give no sign of presence; feign sleep while secretly changing the reel."@en ;
    skos:note "Related to pmp:TranserfingImitationGameTf (section ИМИТИРАНЕ НА СПЕКТАКЪЛ, p. 16): the later lesson gives the outward mask of the mannequin, the earlier the choosing of a reel from behind the mirror; the self-imitation of chapter ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА is a third procedure, pmp:TranserfingTechniqueOfImitationTf."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Имитация; the section asks whether the reader has forgotten its name. The later technique of the same name (pmp:TranserfingTechniqueOfImitationTf) extends it to acquiring qualities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerLightOfTheAwakeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner light evoking unconscious sympathy"@en, "Inneres Licht, das unbewusste Sympathie weckt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign of the awakened state: one shines with a particular inner light that evokes unconscious sympathy in those around."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: One shines with a particular inner light that evokes unconscious sympathy in those around. It bears on pmp:TranserfingImitationTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImitationYieldsPowerAndWisdomTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Imitation yields use of the script's Power and Wisdom"@en, "Imitation ergibt Nutzung von Kraft und Weisheit des Drehbuchs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Conscious imitation of following lets one use the script's Power and Wisdom."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingImitationTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingPowerAndWisdomOfTheScriptTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPowerAndWisdomOfTheScriptTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Using the Power and Wisdom of the script"@en, "Kraft und Weisheit des Drehbuchs nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "By consciously letting the script lead, one in fact leads oneself, drawing on the script's Power and Wisdom."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Силата и Мъдростта на сценария."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNotLettingTheScriptLeadTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not letting the script lead ruins everything"@en, "Das Drehbuch nicht führen lassen verdirbt alles"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one does not allow the script to lead, everything is spoiled; this is given as the reason why things are not as one wants."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If one does not allow the script to lead, everything is spoiled; this is given as the reason why things are not as one wants. It bears on pmp:TranserfingImitationTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingScriptListensIfYouListenTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The script listens if you listen to it"@en, "Das Drehbuch hört, wenn man ihm zuhört"@de ;
    skos:definition "The script has no interest of its own, yet in a sense it will heed you if you heed it; the reason is deferred to a later lesson (see pmc:TranserfingTwoCentresOfIntentionTf)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlansAndExpectationsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Plans and expectations for events and people"@en, "Pläne und Erwartungen an Ereignisse und Menschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Preparing a date with a plan and expectations makes reality unfold otherwise, producing dissatisfaction and negative reactions; expecting events to follow one's design is like demanding a film plot obey one's wishes."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Preparing a date with a plan and expectations makes reality unfold otherwise, producing dissatisfaction and negative reactions; expecting events to follow one's design is like demanding a film plot obey one's wishes. It bears on pmp:TranserfingLettingGoOfEventsAndPeopleTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПОВЕЛЯТА НА СИЛАТА', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ'
#

pmc:TranserfingResistingTheScriptBringsTroubleTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Resisting the script brings much trouble"@en, "Widerstand gegen das Drehbuch bringt viel Ärger"@de ;
    skos:definition "Summary warnings: the \"how?\" question and the wish that everything go one's own way move one away from the goal; resistance to the script draws a mass of trouble."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingStrivingToControlTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingLettingGoOfEventsAndPeopleTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting go of events and people"@en, "Ereignisse und Menschen loslassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since the current reel's events and people cannot be managed, release both: let the reel turn as it turns and let people live as they live; one has no right to influence them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingReleasedPeopleComeToYouTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Released people release you and come to you"@en, "Losgelassene lassen los und kommen zu dir"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: let people go and they will let you go, and moreover come to you and do what you want (explained later)."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Let people go and they will let you go, and moreover come to you and do what you want (explained later). It bears on pmp:TranserfingLettingGoOfEventsAndPeopleTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAllChangeComesByReelTransitionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hold the end result, not the course; all change comes by reel transition"@en, "Das Endergebnis halten, nicht den Verlauf; alle Änderung durch Spulenwechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "In mind must be the final result, the target frame, not the course of events or people's acts; resisting the script is neither allowed nor possible even in presence; every willed change of reality results from moving to another reel, nothing can be done with the script on the current one."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingScriptUnchangeable: the unchangeable script of the current line is restated in film terms, and every willed change is assigned to the move to another reel, even in the state of presence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 24; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingToyingWithRealityTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Toying with reality leads nowhere"@en, "Spielerei mit der Realität führt zu nichts"@de ;
    skos:definition "An awakened person deliberately acting out of script (e.g. striking someone unprovoked) cannot claim this was not scripted; such games bring nothing good, reality must be handled intelligently."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingAllChangeComesByReelTransitionTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMinorExceptionsToTheRulesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rules have minor exceptions, to be ignored"@en, "Regeln haben kleine Ausnahmen, die zu übergehen sind"@de ;
    skos:definition "Statement on the method: small exceptions to the rules undoubtedly exist and may be noticed while experimenting, but they should not draw attention; focus on what is of principal importance."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed the rules are."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomOnlyInCreatingRealityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom only in creating reality; elsewhere awaken, observe, follow"@en, "Freiheit nur im Erschaffen; sonst erwachen, beobachten, folgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The walk does not mean acting at will once awake but consciously submitting; creating reality and switching reels is one's own discretion, everything else is waking, observing and following."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAwakenObserveFollowTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Awaken, observe, follow: three triads"@en, "Erwachen, beobachten, folgen: drei Dreiergruppen"@de ;
    skos:definition "System: awaken in order to (1) give up controlling the script, (2) begin following it, (3) define the target frame; observe in order to (1) track attention, (2) track and extract benefit, (3) track and illuminate the coming frame; follow in order to use the Power and Wisdom of the script."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingScriptAsRiverTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Script as river on the optimal path"@en, "Drehbuch als Fluss auf dem optimalen Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "The script, like a river, always moves along the optimal route; one cannot compute how to reach a goal because too many unknowns are involved, but the script solves it easily; first task name the destination, second follow."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingFocusingOnTheGoalAsAchievedNotTheRouteCh19: the route is left to the script, pictured as a river that always takes the optimal course, and following it is a task of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFollowingTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Following defined"@en, "Folgen definiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following, distinct from the principles of Benefit and Permission, is the skill of sensing the commands of the Power and obeying them; sensing is not always needed, often it suffices to watch how events unfold, accept them and act accordingly instead of resisting."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Следването."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingSensingWhereTheScriptPushesTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensing where the script pushes"@en, "Spüren, wohin das Drehbuch drängt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enter presence, seeing oneself and reality; if reality gives no clear answer about direction, listen more carefully within, to one's sensations, which is easy in presence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCatchingOneselfInTimeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Difficulty of catching oneself in time"@en, "Schwierigkeit, sich rechtzeitig zu ertappen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The only hard part is to track oneself in time so as to wake up."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The only hard part is to track oneself in time so as to wake up. It bears on pmp:TranserfingSensingWhereTheScriptPushesTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingUsingAllActivatorsTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Constant use of all activators until habitual"@en, "Ständiger Einsatz aller Aktivatoren bis zur Gewohnheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use constantly all activators set up in the algorithms of attention tracking, frame illumination and benefit, so that they become habit."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: активатори."@en ;
    skos:note "Restates and widens pmp:TranserfingTwoActivatorsTf (section ПРОСЛЕДЯВАНЕ НА ВНИМАНИЕТО, p. 6): the later lesson extends the activators to the algorithms of frame lighting and of benefit and asks that all of them become habit."@en ;
    skos:note "The activators belong to the algorithms of attention tracking, frame illumination and benefit taught earlier."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingActivatorsYieldTimelyWakingTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Habitual activators yield timely waking"@en, "Gewohnte Aktivatoren ergeben rechtzeitiges Erwachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only through habitual activators does one learn to wake in time."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingUsingAllActivatorsTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWakingUpInTimeTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingActivatorHabitBeforeWakingTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Activator habit before results"@en, "Aktivator-Gewohnheit vor Ergebnissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Timely waking, and thereby any result, depends on having built the habit of activators."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingWakingUpInTimeTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingUsingAllActivatorsTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without the habit of the activators one achieves nothing." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNoActivatorHabitNoAchievementTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No activator habit, no achievement"@en, "Keine Aktivator-Gewohnheit, kein Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Failure condition: without the habit of activators nothing will be achieved."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Without the habit of activators nothing will be achieved. It bears on pmp:TranserfingUsingAllActivatorsTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingUpInTimeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking up in time"@en, "Rechtzeitig erwachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The skill of awakening at the right moment, called the main thing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingActivatorsOfControlTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Activators of control"@en, "Aktivatoren der Kontrolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Three triggers that signal the control habit: (1) I want something from people or events; (2) I want everything to go by my plan; (3) things are not going as I want."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: активатори на контрола."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWorstHabitControlTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The worst habit: controlling script, events, people"@en, "Schlimmste Gewohnheit: Drehbuch, Ereignisse, Menschen kontrollieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Striving to control the script, events and people is named the reader's worst habit."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingStrivingToControlTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingReplacingControlWithFollowingTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Replace controlling with letting go and following"@en, "Kontrollieren durch Loslassen und Folgen ersetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Exchange the habit of control for a new one: release and follow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingAlgorithmOfFollowingTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Algorithm of following"@en, "Algorithmus des Folgens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) catch yourself triggering a control activator; (2) wake: I see myself and reality; (3) ask and feel what the first command says; (4) if an answer comes, follow it; (5) if none, define the target frame and again try to follow."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: алгоритъмът на следването."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFollowingAlgorithmYieldsSensingCommandTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Following algorithm yields sensing the command"@en, "Folgealgorithmus ergibt Spüren des Befehls"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following is defined as the skill of sensing the command of the Power and submitting; the algorithm trains it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAlgorithmOfFollowingTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSensingTheCommandOfThePowerTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЛЕДВАНЕ', p. 25; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА'
#

pmc:TranserfingTheWalkIsMeeknessTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The walk is meekness and pretence, not licence"@en, "Der Gang ist Sanftmut und Verstellung, nicht Freibrief"@de ;
    skos:definition "Walking live does not mean doing as one pleases; on the walk Tufti is meekness itself, keeping quiet, not revealing presence, watching and following; and all this is pretence and imitation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCommandIsNotIndulgenceTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not confuse the command with indulging weaknesses"@en, "Den Befehl nicht mit Nachgeben gegenüber Schwächen verwechseln"@de ;
    skos:definition "The command of the Power must not be confused with the wish to gratify one's weaknesses and bad inclinations."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingSensingTheCommandOfThePowerTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFirstImpulseTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "First impulse equals the command, intuition"@en, "Erster Impuls gleich Befehl, Intuition"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first impulse, also called intuition or premonition, is the command; following it is the right step, ignoring it is an error."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: първия си порив."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingIntuitiveKnowing: intuition is identified with the first impulse and that with the command of the Power, which one is to obey."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDisobedienceLeadsToTheWorstProgramTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Disobedience leads to the worst program"@en, "Ungehorsam führt ins schlimmste Programm"@de ;
    skos:definition "Disobedience is not freedom: one deviates from the script only to commit an error, after which the script subjugates one again, now by the worst program that accounts for the mistake."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Disobedience is not freedom: one deviates from the script only to commit an error, after which the script subjugates one again, now by the worst program that accounts for the mistake. It bears on pmp:TranserfingAlgorithmOfFollowingTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfConceitTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-conceit as cause of disobedience"@en, "Eigendünkel als Ursache des Ungehorsams"@de ;
    skos:definition "The cause of not obeying is self-consciousness, more exactly self-conceit, used against its purpose: it does not know where and in what position it is."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: самомнение."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoExceptionsToTheScriptTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two exceptions to the script"@en, "Zwei Ausnahmen vom Drehbuch"@de ;
    skos:definition "The script programs all actions on a reel with two exceptions: the harmful one, disobedience; and the useful one, waking and consciously ordering reality, the only thing not contained in the script."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingChangingFilmReelsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Changing film reels"@en, "Filmspulen wechseln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims humans can switch reels and so fall under another script; the script does not know of this ability, which the Creator gave to humans alone among living beings."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: да сменяте филмовите ленти."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingHowTheScriptListensTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "How the script \"listens\": release at illumination of the target frame"@en, "Wie das Drehbuch „hört“: Freigabe beim Erhellen des Zielbildes"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one creates reality, the current script releases one and yields to another reel, to which one moves at the moment the target frame is illuminated."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


pmc:TranserfingMovingTheFrameWithOuterIntentionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Present with attention, moving the frame with outer intention"@en, "Gegenwärtig mit Aufmerksamkeit, Filmbild mit äußerer Absicht bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One walks live when present with attention and moving the frame with intention, not with narrow intention but with the outer one, so named because it does not belong to or obey oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: външното намерение."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie: outer intention is said to be named so because it does not belong to and does not obey the person, and the frame is moved by it while attention stays present."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOuterPowerTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer intention as the Power, motor of reality"@en, "Äußere Absicht als Kraft, Motor der Realität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention is not simply the script; something stands above it: the Power, engine of reality, whose active component turns the reels as predestined; by whom and why is left aside."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Външната сила (section title), Сила (the Power)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPowerUsedThroughThePlaitTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Metapower via the plait"@en, "Metakraft über den Zopf"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Power cannot be influenced directly but used indirectly through its access point, the plait; when unaware, the Power leads one by the plait like a marionette; when awake and present and taking the plait in hand, the Power acquires its reactive component, metapower, which launches the other reel matching the ordered frame."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: метасила."@en ;
    skos:note "Links pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf and pmc:TranserfingMetapowerTf, typed by part 1; this node carries only the restated relation of the Power, the plait and metapower as given in this section."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingPlaitAlgorithmTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Plait algorithm"@en, "Algorithmus des Zopfes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) wake into the point of awareness (presence); (2) activate the plait by attending to and feeling it; (3) without moving attention off the plait, order the target frame. Attention rests on the inner screen and the plait at once; it feels the plait and paints the future on the screen visually and/or in words and thoughts, painting from the outer centre, not the inner."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: плитката."@en ;
    skos:note "Restates pmp:TranserfingPlaitTechniqueTf (the section on using the plait, p. 9) as a numbered algorithm and adds that one paints the future from the outer centre, not the inner; kept as its own node because the later statement adds this condition."@en ;
    skos:note "The point of awareness is linked to pmc:TranserfingCentreOfAwarenessTf, the inner screen to pmc:TranserfingTwoScreensTf and the plait to pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf, all typed by part 1."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 26; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlaitAlgorithmYieldsReelChangeTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Plait algorithm yields reel change"@en, "Zopf-Algorithmus ergibt Spulenwechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Activating the plait and defining reality sets off metapower, which launches the reel matching the ordered frame."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPlaitAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingChangingFilmReelsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingNonDoingWhileOrderingTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Non-doing while ordering: let it happen by itself"@en, "Nicht-Tun beim Bestellen: es von selbst geschehen lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Apply no explicit force; have nothing to do with it, act only indirectly, assist and watch it happen by itself; do not force but allow; catch and remember the sensation arising behind and around oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSensationBehindAndAroundTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensation behind and around oneself"@en, "Empfindung hinter und um einen herum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: a sensation arising behind and around oneself, identified as one's touch of the Power."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: A sensation arising behind and around oneself, identified as one's touch of the Power. It bears on pmp:TranserfingNonDoingWhileOrderingTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMasteryOfThePowerSensationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mastery of the sensation of the Power"@en, "Beherrschung der Empfindung der Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims that if one learns to command this sensation, the Power will be with one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNonDoingYieldsMasteryTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Non-doing ordering yields mastery of the Power sensation"@en, "Nicht-tuendes Bestellen ergibt Beherrschung der Kraftempfindung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeatedly catching the sensation while ordering leads to mastering it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingNonDoingWhileOrderingTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingMasteryOfThePowerSensationTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВЪНШНАТА СИЛА', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ'
#

pmc:TranserfingConstantPracticeSufficesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The technology needs only constant systematic practice"@en, "Die Technik braucht nur ständige, systematische Übung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Statement on the method: the live-walk technology is not so complex, it requires only constant and systematic practice; one who actually tries rather than only reading will succeed easily."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPaperManTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The paper figure: without attention one is absent"@en, "Die Papierfigur: ohne Aufmerksamkeit ist man abwesend"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without attention one is not oneself, merely a character like a cut-out figure slipped between book pages; only rare flashes of self-consciousness distinguish one from a true character."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Хартиеното човече (section title)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDirectAttackWithNarrowIntentionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Direct attack with narrow intention"@en, "Direkter Angriff mit enger Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Things are not as one wants because one always acts by direct attack with narrow intention, demanding love, respect, help, gifts like a child."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Things are not as one wants because one always acts by direct attack with narrow intention, demanding love, respect, help, gifts like a child. It bears on pmp:TranserfingGivingInsteadOfDemandingTf."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: тесногръдото си намерение."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRealityMirrorTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality as mirror: you receive what you send"@en, "Realität als Spiegel: man erhält, was man sendet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reaching to a mirror and demanding makes the reflection do the same and take rather than give; reality likewise returns the reflection of mental postulates and actions; even unaware one partly defines reality, less effectively than with intention and plait."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWorldMirrorRelationshipCh14 and pmc:TranserfingFirstMirrorPrincipleCh18: the mirror is shown as a person reaching toward a looking-glass with the demand to be given, whose reflection takes instead; even the unaware state is said to define reality in part."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNonAcceptanceShapesRealityTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Wholehearted non-acceptance shapes reality"@en, "Inbrünstige Nichtannahme formt die Realität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even in the unaware state one shapes reality, especially when expressing non-acceptance with all one's heart; reality as a rule reacts like a mirror."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingRealityMirrorTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingParadoxicalMirrorTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Paradoxical mirror: image and reflection swapped"@en, "Paradoxer Spiegel: Bild und Spiegelbild vertauscht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reality is a paradoxical mirror: the reflection is the surrounding current frame, attention is sunk in it, so one cannot see oneself from outside and the Self is woven into the film; no surface divides image from reflection, yet the essence is the same."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMovingThroughOneselfTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Moving oneself and moving through oneself"@en, "Sich selbst bewegen und durch sich selbst bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims the ability to move and to move through oneself, so that the reflection holds what one wants, is gained when attention is pulled out of the film/mirror and one sees oneself standing before it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 27; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingYouAreYourAttentionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "You are your attention"@en, "Man ist seine Aufmerksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "One exists as a living individual only through attention; present means attention in the auditorium, seeing oneself and reality, where the screen is really a mirror; otherwise one is a paper character."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 28; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingShootingOnesOwnFilmTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shooting one's own film"@en, "Den eigenen Film drehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving consciously before the mirror-screen yields the matching reflection, so one is in effect shooting one's own film and reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 28; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPresenceBeforeOwnFilmTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Presence first, to shoot one's own film"@en, "Erst Präsenz, um den eigenen Film zu drehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first thing needed to shoot one's own film is to wake and enter presence."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingShootingOnesOwnFilmTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingPresenceTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 28; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingEnteringPresenceAsInsiderTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Entering presence as an insider in the film"@en, "Eintritt in Präsenz als Eingeweihter im Film"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagine having come alive in the film, living in it rather than watching; open the eyes and look at everything anew, refreshing the gaze; feel oneself not as a character but as an outside visitor who entered as an insider, body inside, attention outside; feel one's separateness and presence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 28; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingColoursLookRicherTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Colours look richer"@en, "Farben wirken satter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign on refreshing the gaze: colours become juicier."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Colours become juicier. It bears on pmp:TranserfingEnteringPresenceAsInsiderTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 28; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingInsiderExerciseYieldsPresenceTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Insider exercise yields presence"@en, "Eingeweihten-Übung ergibt Präsenz"@de ;
    skos:definition "The insider exercise brings one into presence."@en ;
    skos:note "The capacity, the state of presence, is pmc:TranserfingPresenceTf, typed by part 1."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEnteringPresenceAsInsiderTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingPresenceTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 28; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingGivingInsteadOfDemandingTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Mirror first step: swap \"give\" for \"take\""@en, "Erster Schritt am Spiegel: „gib“ gegen „nimm“ tauschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before wanting, expecting or asking anything from people or reality, imagine standing before a mirror and ask what to do so the reflection comes toward you; make the first move; give first something similar to what one wants, it hardly matters what; replace every \"give me\" with \"take\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingFrailingGivePartnerAimHisInnerCh15: the giving is grounded in the mirror, one first gives something similar to what one wants, and what is given hardly matters."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 28; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingReflectionDeliversTheWantTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reflection delivers what was wanted"@en, "Das Spiegelbild liefert das Gewünschte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: after swapping to giving, one receives in the reflection, as if by magic, what one wanted; what one sends is what one gets."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: After swapping to giving, one receives in the reflection, as if by magic, what one wanted; what one sends is what one gets. It bears on pmp:TranserfingGivingInsteadOfDemandingTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ХАРТИЕНОТО ЧОВЕЧЕ', p. 28; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА'
#

pmc:TranserfingRadiatingYieldsObtainingTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Radiating yields obtaining via the reflection"@en, "Ausstrahlen ergibt Erhalten über das Spiegelbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Radiating love and charm returns love and sympathy."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRadiatingWhatYouWantTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingObtainingThroughTheReflectionTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 28; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingRadiatingWhatYouWantTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Radiate what you want to receive"@en, "Ausstrahlen, was man empfangen will"@de ;
    skos:definition "Arrange thoughts and feelings with the invisible mirror in view: needing love and sympathy, do not strive to obtain them but radiate love and love, radiate charm and feel sympathy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 28; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfTestOfTheMirrorPrincipleTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-test of the mirror principle"@en, "Selbstprüfung des Spiegelprinzips"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti invites checking the principle on oneself: who is more likeable, one who loves you or one who chases your love, one who gives freely or one who begs, one sincerely interested or one demanding attention."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how the method may be tested."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 28; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTableOfImageCreationTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Table of image creation"@en, "Tabelle der Bildgestaltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Three-column table, eleven rows, of wants, the image to create and what returns in the reflection: pleasant contact by listening attentively; being interesting by showing interest; help by helping; understanding by trying to understand; sympathy by empathising; approval by approving; respect by respecting; gratitude by thanking; being liked by showing liking; admiration by admiring; being loved by loving."@en ;
    skos:note "Text layer: the table is flattened column by column (eleven wants, then eleven images, then eleven reflections); the rows were realigned by position for this node."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 29; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingObtainingThroughTheReflectionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Obtaining from people via the reflection"@en, "Von Menschen über das Spiegelbild erhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims that the image one creates returns from people the matching response (they want to talk with you, help, understand, respect, love you), so that people themselves come to want to do what one needs."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: създаване на образа."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 29; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlusAndMinusSignTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Plus sign and minus sign"@en, "Plus- und Minuszeichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "All thoughts and actions should carry the plus sign; every \"give me\" carries the minus sign and does not work, or rather works in reverse."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 29; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBoomerangOfNegativeActsTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Boomerang of negative thoughts and acts"@en, "Bumerang negativer Gedanken und Taten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Negative thoughts and actions return like a boomerang; the mirror does not always return exactly the same thing and causal links of misfortune are often hidden, but return sooner or later, in some form, is certain."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingBoomerang: the return is placed in the reality mirror, which does not always give back the same thing and whose causal links often stay hidden."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingRealityMirrorTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 29; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTableOfWhatNotToDoTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Table of what not to do"@en, "Tabelle dessen, was zu unterlassen ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Six rows: to avoid aggression, show none; to avoid criticism, do not criticise; to avoid condemnation, do not condemn; to avoid harm, do not harm others; to avoid fear, threaten no one; to avoid being found unpleasant, cause no unpleasantness."@en ;
    skos:note "Text layer: the table is flattened row by row, want and prohibition alternating; read in that order."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 29; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheImageTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating the image (algorithm of the image)"@en, "Erschaffen des Bildes (Algorithmus des Bildes)"@de ;
    skos:definition "When wanting something from people, wake and stand before the mirror: (1) realise that you want to receive something from people; (2) enter presence: wanting is pointless, one must give; (3) ask what similar thing you can give; (4) if found, give it now and keep giving; (5) if not, give anything at all."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: алгоритъм на образа."@en ;
    skos:note "The section title names the practice: СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА; the algorithm itself is given at its end."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 29; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImageAlgorithmYieldsObtainingTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Image algorithm yields obtaining via the reflection"@en, "Bild-Algorithmus ergibt Erhalten über das Spiegelbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Giving what one wishes to receive produces it in the reflection."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheImageTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingObtainingThroughTheReflectionTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 29; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingGivingWhatTheOtherNeedsTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Giving what the other needs, found by sincere interest"@en, "Geben, was der andere braucht, durch echtes Interesse ermittelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one cannot or should not give the same thing, give whatever the person needs or would enjoy, from a compliment to a present; finding the need only requires genuine interest in them."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingShowInterestSincerelyNotAsTechniqueCh12: sincere interest serves here to find out what the other needs, so as to give it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 29; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRadiateLoveNotDemandsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Radiate love, not demands"@en, "Liebe ausstrahlen, nicht Forderungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "General principle of the image: radiate love toward the world rather than demands, loving without wanting anything back; only then does love come by itself, not the reverse order people expect."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 29; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingKeepAwayFromLoveTakersTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Keep away from those who only take love"@en, "Von denen fernhalten, die Liebe nur nehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some people will readily use one's love giving nothing back; stay away from them, they are not needed."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingRadiateLoveNotDemandsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОБРАЗА', p. 29; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО'
#

pmc:TranserfingNoEqualAmongOthersTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Without equal among others"@en, "Ohne Gleichen unter den anderen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever practises self-development and also masters the technique of creating the image is said to have no equal among the other snails."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: no equal among the others for one who joins self-development with the technique of the image. It bears on pmp:TranserfingSelfDevelopmentTf and pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheImageTf."@en ;
    skos:note "Added from pass B."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 30; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPushingTheCurrentFrameBackfiresTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Direct pushing of the current frame backfires"@en, "Direktes Schieben des aktuellen Filmbildes schlägt fehl"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attempts to move the current frame oneself, influencing the course of events directly, lead to nothing or to the opposite effect; trying to influence people is likewise pointless, as they are characters led by the script."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Attempts to move the current frame oneself, influencing the course of events directly, lead to nothing or to the opposite effect; trying to influence people is likewise pointless, as they are characters led by the script. It bears on pmp:TranserfingPlaitAlgorithmTf."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNoControllingTheWorld: direct influence on the current frame or on people is said to bring nothing or the reverse effect, because people are characters led by the script."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 30; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingEventsChangeOnlyByReelChangeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Events change only by reel change; people only indirectly by the mirror"@en, "Ereignisse nur durch Spulenwechsel; Menschen nur indirekt über den Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The course of events can be turned only by switching the reel, never within it; people can be influenced only indirectly (coercion set aside) by meeting them on the mirror principle, the one way to make them want to do what one needs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 30; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImageWorksByAMirrorMechanismTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Image creation works like reality creation but by a mirror mechanism"@en, "Bildgestaltung wirkt wie Realitätsgestaltung, aber über den Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reality is not only cinema but also a mirror; creating the image acts like creating reality but through a different, mirror mechanism; people's behaviour cannot be set the way reality can."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 30; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOrderingASpecificPersonTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ordering a specific person into the target frame"@en, "Eine bestimmte Person in den Zielbild bestellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A target frame meant to make a concrete person dance to one's tune will most likely not work or work in reverse, since it is a double breach of the rules: intruding into another's script."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A target frame meant to make a concrete person dance to one's tune will most likely not work or work in reverse, since it is a double breach of the rules: intruding into another's script. It bears on pmp:TranserfingOneselfAtTheCentreOfTheFrameTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 30; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingOneselfAtTheCentreOfTheFrameTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Composing the target frame with oneself at the centre"@en, "Den Zielbild mit sich selbst im Zentrum gestalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only one's own separate reality is available, so the central figure of the target frame must be oneself as in one's dreams (on stage, in the director's chair, on one's yacht); everyone else stays in the background as scenery; for a partner, picture marrying an abstract, imagined person or an ideal, or living happily with a future family."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 30; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCreateRealityNeverOrderPeopleTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Create reality, never order people"@en, "Realität erschaffen, nie Menschen bestellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One may create reality but must not order people; with them only mirror relations are possible; wanting something from a particular person, go and deal with them in this film as with a mirror, creating one's image."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingOneselfAtTheCentreOfTheFrameTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 30; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMeetingTheRightPersonTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Meeting the right person on the new reel"@en, "Die passende Person auf der neuen Spule treffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: picturing marriage with an abstract person changes the reel to one where one meets the person with whom that script is realised."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Picturing marriage with an abstract person changes the reel to one where one meets the person with whom that script is realised. It bears on pmp:TranserfingOneselfAtTheCentreOfTheFrameTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 30; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingChangeableReelAndDeceptiveMirrorTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Twofold position: changeable reel and deceptive mirror"@en, "Doppelte Lage: wechselbare Spule und trügerischer Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Never forget the situation: a film among script-led characters; on one side a reel one can change, on the other a deceptive mirror reality with no visible surface between image and reflection; awake one can walk live and influence reality, asleep almost nothing depends on one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 30; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerInstigatorTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The inner instigator"@en, "Der innere Anstifter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unlike dream characters and animals, humans have self-consciousness, so besides the outer motor (script) they are partly driven by an inner instigator: the need for one's own significance and the drive to self-realisation, proving one was not born in vain."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Вътрешен подбудител."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 30; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingRaisingOthersSignificanceTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Raising others' significance and aiding their self-realisation"@en, "Die Bedeutung anderer heben und ihre Selbstverwirklichung fördern"@de ;
    skos:definition "To win people's favour or get something from them, set oneself the aim of underlining their significance and helping their self-realisation, temporarily forgetting one's own importance."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingLinkingTasksToSelfWorthYieldsWillingCooperationCh12: the appeal to others' significance is grounded in the inner instigator and in the mirror, one gains by thinking of the other's benefit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRaisingSignificanceYieldsObtainingTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Raising others' significance yields obtaining via the reflection"@en, "Bedeutung anderer heben ergibt Erhalten über das Spiegelbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Paradoxically one benefits by thinking of others' benefit."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRaisingOthersSignificanceTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingObtainingThroughTheReflectionTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotWoundSignificanceTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not wound others' sense of significance"@en, "Das Bedeutungsgefühl anderer nicht verletzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Guard in every way against hurting another's feeling of importance."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingSelfWorthAsMostCherishedPossessionCh12: the warning is stated as the way to avoid making enemies within the mirror principle."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingRaisingOthersSignificanceTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBenefitToOthersBeforeOwnRealisationTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Benefit for others before own self-realisation"@en, "Nutzen für andere vor eigener Selbstverwirklichung"@de ;
    skos:definition "One's own realisation succeeds only when others also benefit from it."@en ;
    skos:note "Prior: benefit to others; dependent: own self-realisation."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingSuccessfulSelfRealisationTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingRaisingOthersSignificanceTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "If others gain nothing from what one does, one does not succeed either." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSuccessfulSelfRealisationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Successful self-realisation"@en, "Gelingende Selbstverwirklichung"@de ;
    skos:definition "One's own realisation, the second drive of the inner instigator, held to succeed when it benefits others, and then without further problems."@en ;
    skos:note "Dependent step of pmc:TranserfingBenefitToOthersBeforeOwnRealisationTf; written by the integrator from the same passage."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNoBenefitToOthersNoSuccessTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No benefit to others, no success"@en, "Kein Nutzen für andere, kein Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Failure condition: if what one does brings others no benefit, one will not succeed."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If what one does brings others no benefit, one will not succeed. It bears on pmp:TranserfingRaisingOthersSignificanceTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЩУВАНЕ С ОГЛЕДАЛОТО', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ'
#

pmc:TranserfingBecomingEveryonesFavouriteTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming everyone's favourite"@en, "Zum Liebling aller werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: in presence one appears to sleepers as a likeable firefly; communicating with them as with a mirror on top of it makes one a universal favourite."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: In presence one appears to sleepers as a likeable firefly; communicating with them as with a mirror on top of it makes one a universal favourite. It bears on pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheImageTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingManipulationByThePowerfulTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Mind manipulation by the powerful and the mass media"@en, "Bewusstseinsmanipulation durch Mächtige und Massenmedien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Others higher up, especially holders of power and mass media, will try to manipulate one's consciousness; stay alert, do not let them lead, do not fall asleep."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingManipulationAsSteeringAVectorTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingManipulationAsSteeringAVectorTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Manipulation as steering another's vector"@en, "Manipulation als Steuern eines fremden Vektors"@de ;
    skos:definition "The instigator mainly sets the direction (vector) of one's movement, the script moves; manipulation means steering someone else's vector, e.g. by deception, by false values and goals, or by exploiting weaknesses and needs; mirror principles, by contrast, leave the vector intact and help it."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Манипулиране."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingManipulators: manipulation is defined as steering another person's vector, by deception, false values and goals or exploiting weakness, with no reference to guilt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingAskingWhoProfitsTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ask who profits whenever something is imposed"@en, "Fragen, wem es nützt, wenn etwas aufgedrängt wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whenever one feels something being pressed on one, ask to whom and why it could be advantageous."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingManipulatingPeopleIsDirtyWorkTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Manipulating people is dirty work"@en, "Menschen manipulieren ist schmutzige Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti refuses to teach manipulating people; manipulating reality, which constantly misleads with illusions, is called fair."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingManipulationAsSteeringAVectorTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTwofoldHiddenNatureOfRealityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Twofold hidden nature of reality: film and volumetric mirror"@en, "Doppelte verborgene Natur der Realität: Film und räumlicher Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reality is both a film and a three-dimensional mirror, and both confuse; the chief illusion is that this true nature is hidden; knowing and remembering it ends the illusion's power."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: обемно огледало."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingDualMirrorCh18: reality is twofold as film and volumetric mirror, not as material and metaphysical faces, and its chief illusion is that this nature is hidden."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 31; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingVolumetricMirrorLagsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The volumetric mirror lags and is not one to one"@en, "Der räumliche Spiegel verzögert und ist nicht eins zu eins"@de ;
    skos:definition "No visible border separates real and virtual, one is inside and outside the mirror at once; the mirror works with delay and not one to one, messages do not act at once, causal links are not always traceable; reality pretends not to be a mirror."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingThirdMirrorPrincipleCh18: besides the delay, the mirror is said not to answer one to one, to have no visible border and to pretend it is no mirror."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 32; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingReflectionCanBecomeImageTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Image and reflection coincide, so reflection can become image"@en, "Bild und Spiegelbild fallen zusammen, also kann Spiegelbild Bild werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since in the volumetric mirror image and reflection coincide, a created image can become reflection and a reflection can flow into image: one can turn the reflection into the image by pretending to have what one lacks or be what one is not."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 32; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingPretendingToHaveTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pretending as if one already has or is"@en, "So tun, als hätte oder wäre man es schon"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wanting a home, tour shops and look at furniture as if the house were already one's own; wanting wealth, take an interest in expensive things, cars, yachts, resorts; wanting stardom, behave and live as a star, even if only in imagination; enter the state of having or being, play it deliberately and in earnest, never as a joke."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: преструвка."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingCoordinatingImportanceCh13: acting as though the goal were reached is made a pretence played in earnest before the mirror, with concrete behaviour (shops, expensive things, a star's life)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 32; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingEarnestPretenceYieldsActualityTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Earnest pretence yields the reflection"@en, "Ernsthafte Verstellung ergibt das Spiegelbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Playing in earnest forces reality to take it seriously as well."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPretendingToHaveTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingIllusionMadeActualTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 32; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRealityMatchesThePretenceTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality gradually matches the pretence"@en, "Realität passt sich allmählich der Verstellung an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: step by step the picture of reality starts to correspond to one's pretence."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Step by step the picture of reality starts to correspond to one's pretence. It bears on pmp:TranserfingPretendingToHaveTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 32; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingIllusionMadeActualTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning a staged illusion into actuality (creating the reflection)"@en, "Eine inszenierte Illusion in Wirklichkeit verwandeln (Spiegelbild erschaffen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims reality, which loves to make illusions but cannot bear being fed them, will find a way to make the illusion one created real: one becomes what one pretends to be."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: създаване на отражение."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МАНИПУЛИРАНЕ', p. 32; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ'
#

pmc:TranserfingMasksOfTheMasqueradeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The masks of the masquerade"@en, "Die Masken der Maskerade"@de ;
    skos:definition "The walk is play and masquerade, in earnest; reality has many faces and one has paired masks for it: imitation and presence, permission and following, tracking and creating, image and reflection."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 32; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDirectAndReverseProcessTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Direct and reverse process of the mirror"@en, "Direkter und umgekehrter Prozess des Spiegels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Direct: image flows into reflection; creating the image is one's message, one gets what one gives and has what one really is. Reverse: reflection flows into image; creating the reflection is pretence and imitation, one gets what one imitates and becomes what one pretends to be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 32; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMirrorWorkIsMovingThroughOneselfTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mirror work is moving through oneself; differs from reality creation"@en, "Spiegelarbeit ist Bewegen durch sich selbst; anders als Realitätsgestaltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "All these mirror manipulations constitute moving through oneself; image and reflection use reality's mirror nature, creating reality uses its film nature by illuminating the future frame; different mechanism, same result, the wanted thing becomes actual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRealityIsPlasticTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality is plastic and becomes manageable"@en, "Realität ist formbar und wird lenkbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against doubt that pretence can become real: reality is plastic and will find means, being a multi-variant film and an illusory mirror, itself an illusion that becomes controllable if remembered and used wisely."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlayInEarnestConditionTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "First necessary condition: play in full earnest"@en, "Erste notwendige Bedingung: völlig ernsthaft spielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like a good actor who becomes the character by playing seriously, go the reverse way: from the unsatisfying character one is, become an actor, play an imagined character and live into it until one becomes it for real."@en ;
    skos:note "Called a necessary condition; no consequence of omitting it is stated beyond the earlier remark that earnest play makes reality take it seriously."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingIllusionMadeActualTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingPlayingInEarnestTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingPlayingInEarnestTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Playing in full earnest"@en, "Vollkommen ernsthaft spielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take the actor's path in reverse: from the character one is and dislikes, become an actor, play an imagined character and live into the role until one becomes it."@en ;
    skos:note "Named by the text the first necessary condition of creating the reflection; prior step of pmc:TranserfingPlayInEarnestConditionTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSystematicPlayConditionTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Second necessary condition: systematic play with patience"@en, "Zweite notwendige Bedingung: systematisches Spiel mit Geduld"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because the reality mirror answers with delay, act purposefully, methodically and regularly, with patience, at first blindly without expecting instant results."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingIllusionMadeActualTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingSystematicPlayTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Results come only if reality, watching the play, loses patience first; whoever stops early gets none." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingSystematicPlayTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Systematic play"@en, "Systematisches Spiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Play with reality purposefully, methodically and regularly, with patience, acting blindly at first without hoping for instant results."@en ;
    skos:note "Named by the text the second necessary condition of creating the reflection; prior step of pmc:TranserfingSystematicPlayConditionTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLosingPatienceFirstTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Losing patience before reality does"@en, "Die Geduld vor der Realität verlieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Failure condition: results are not instant and come only if reality gives up first; one who expects immediate results or stops early does not get them."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Results are not instant and come only if reality gives up first; one who expects immediate results or stops early does not get them. It bears on pmp:TranserfingPretendingToHaveTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingReflectionAlgorithmYieldsActualityTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Reflection algorithm yields turning illusion into actuality"@en, "Spiegelbild-Algorithmus ergibt Verwandlung der Illusion in Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creating the reflection is making an illusion for reality, which then turns real."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheReflectionTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingIllusionMadeActualTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOnceYouBelieveRealityBelievesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Once you believe, reality believes"@en, "Sobald man glaubt, glaubt die Realität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: when one comes to believe the created illusion, reality believes it too, and a miracle happens."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: When one comes to believe the created illusion, reality believes it too, and a miracle happens. It bears on pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheReflectionTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheReflectionTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating the reflection (algorithm of the reflection)"@en, "Erschaffen der Spiegelung (Algorithmus der Spiegelung)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) realise: I want to get something or become someone; (2) enter presence: wanting is pointless, one must give; (3) pretend and behave as if the wish were already achieved. How to pretend is free and up to one's invention; the more creativity, the more effective. Live it in thought virtually and where possible in deeds really, until one believes the illusion oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: алгоритъмът на отражението."@en ;
    skos:note "The section title names the practice: СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPretendOnlyBeforeRealityTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pretend only before reality, not with people, and within reason"@en, "Nur vor der Realität verstellen, nicht vor Menschen, und mit Maß"@de ;
    skos:definition "Image creation is for people, reflection creation mainly for reality; with people do not pretend, be sincere and oneself; before the mirror of reality pretend as much as one likes, but within reasonable bounds and without losing the sense of reality."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheReflectionTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMirrorPlayAloneNotEnoughTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Mirror play or future frame alone is not enough"@en, "Spiegelspiel oder Zukunftsbild allein genügen nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "One must also do everything the goal requires in the current frame, taking concrete steps rather than only dreaming on the sofa."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingContemplationAloneInsufficient: the point is made for play with the mirror and the future frame, both of which need concrete steps in the current frame."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheReflectionTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪЗДАВАНЕ НА ОТРАЖЕНИЕ', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА'
#

pmc:TranserfingRealityRealButIllusoryTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality is real in itself but illusory to the ignorant"@en, "Realität ist an sich real, aber illusorisch für den Unkundigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calling reality an illusion does not mean it is unreal; it is real in itself but illusory and unmanageable for one who does not know and use its properties; like a horse, it is not yours until ridden, then the illusion obeys."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImagePrimaryReflectionIsLifeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Image primary, reflection is one's whole life"@en, "Bild primär, Spiegelbild ist das ganze Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The image is one's way of thinking and acting and is always primary; the reflection is oneself together with all one's surroundings, one's life; the two flow into each other."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 33; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFeedbackLoopDegradesTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Left to itself, the feedback loop degrades"@en, "Sich selbst überlassen führt die Rückkopplung zum Verfall"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thinking shapes life and life shapes thinking; left unattended, gloomier thoughts make life worse and so on, and both person and life degrade, as usually happens."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingImagePrimaryReflectionIsLifeTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingCombiningTheThreeCreationsTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Using image, reflection and reality creation together"@en, "Bild, Spiegelbild und Realitätsgestaltung zusammen nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The three may be used separately or all at once: while pursuing a goal, systematically order the target frame, pretend the goal is already reached, and keep every thought and act under the plus sign."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSkillOfCombinedCreationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Skill of using all creations at once"@en, "Fertigkeit, alle Gestaltungsweisen zugleich zu nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti says the ability to use everything together comes with experience."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingContinuousPracticeYieldsCombinedSkillTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous practice yields the combined skill"@en, "Ständige Übung ergibt die kombinierte Fertigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Experience gathered by continuous practice brings the skill of using all at once."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingContinuousPracticeOfTheWalkTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSkillOfCombinedCreationTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingExperienceBeforeCombinedUseTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Experience before combined use"@en, "Erfahrung vor kombinierter Nutzung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Combined use requires experience, which requires continuous systematic practice."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingSkillOfCombinedCreationTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingContinuousPracticeOfTheWalkTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingContinuousPracticeOfTheWalkTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Continuous systematic practice of the live walk"@en, "Ständige, systematische Übung des lebendigen Gangs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Practise the live walk continually and systematically: constantly watch oneself, wake up and carry out the algorithms."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAlgorithmsBuildHabitsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Algorithms build habits; habits rule when awareness lapses"@en, "Algorithmen bilden Gewohnheiten; Gewohnheiten herrschen, wenn Bewusstheit fehlt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The point of the endless algorithms is that they form new habits; habits govern a person who cannot govern self or reality; one cannot stay in presence all the time, and in the unaware state habits work for one, so right actions must run automatically."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMinimumHabitExchangesTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Minimum habit exchanges"@en, "Mindestens auszutauschende Gewohnheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "At minimum: exchange the habit of wanting for that of giving; of rejecting for accepting; of falling asleep for waking up."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAlgorithmsYieldAutomatismsTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Running the algorithms yields useful automatisms"@en, "Ausführen der Algorithmen ergibt nützliche Automatismen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeated algorithms turn into helpful automatic reactions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingContinuousPracticeOfTheWalkTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingUsefulAutomaticReactionsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingUsefulAutomaticReactionsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Useful automatic reactions, unstuck from the script"@en, "Nützliche Automatismen, vom Drehbuch gelöst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims the algorithms peel one off the script, bring one alive in the film and install useful automatic reactions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCreateInsteadTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Most useful habit and its derivatives: create instead"@en, "Nützlichste Gewohnheit und Ableitungen: stattdessen erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chief habit: not wanting something from reality but creating reality; derivatives: create rather than fear, rather than wait, rather than hope, rather than lament."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingWakingOnWaitingAndHopingTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking on waiting, hoping, fearing or heaviness"@en, "Erwachen bei Warten, Hoffen, Fürchten oder Schwere"@de ;
    skos:definition "As soon as one notices expecting, hoping, fearing something or feeling weighed down, wake up and realise that an outer script, not one's own, is leading, which is exactly what weighs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWaitingComesFromFeltUnfreedomTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waiting and hoping come from felt unfreedom"@en, "Warten und Hoffen entspringen gefühlter Unfreiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Below awareness one feels unfree, dependent on reality and shut in by circumstances like a character in a plot, without realising it, so nothing seems left but to wait and hope; once one knows the reel can be switched, waiting and hoping lose their point."@en ;
    skos:note "Ground of pmp:TranserfingWakingOnWaitingAndHopingTf."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingActivatorForEveryCaseTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "A matching activator and algorithm for every case"@en, "Für jeden Fall ein passender Aktivator und Algorithmus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since one can peel off the script and switch reels, waiting and hoping lose sense; lamenting calls for waking and extracting benefit; idle guessing calls for waking and following the commands of the Power; every case has its activator and algorithm."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingHopingIsFoolishTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Hoping whether it will come true is foolish"@en, "Hoffen, ob es eintritt, ist töricht"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is pointless and silly to hope whether something will or will not happen; it is up to one to create image, reflection, reality, or all at once."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingWakingOnWaitingAndHopingTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СЪДБОВНАТА ДИЛЕМА', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!'
#

pmc:TranserfingRealityPretendsNotToBeAFilmTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality pretends to be no film"@en, "Die Wirklichkeit gibt vor, kein Film zu sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "As reality pretends not to be a mirror, it pretends, very successfully, not to be a film; neither sleeping neighbours nor dream mannequins will grasp or believe that they are in a film or a dream."@en ;
    skos:note "Extends pmc:TranserfingVolumetricMirrorLagsTf from the mirror to the film aspect."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 34; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotConvinceSleepersTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not try to convince sleepers; convince yourself"@en, "Schläfer nicht überzeugen; sich selbst überzeugen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Telling sleeping neighbours they live in a film, or dream figures that they are dreamed, will be neither understood nor believed; do not argue with them, first convince oneself."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingWakingInTheFilmTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAFilmNotOnesOwnTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A film not one's own, and self-dislike"@en, "Ein fremder Film und Selbstablehnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reasons for misery: a film runs in one's life that is not one's own, because one does not realise it really is a film; further cause, one does not like oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Reasons for misery: a film runs in one's life that is not one's own, because one does not realise it really is a film; further cause, one does not like oneself. It bears on pmp:TranserfingPlaitAlgorithmTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRelativeFreedomAtWakingTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relative freedom at the moment of waking"@en, "Relative Freiheit im Moment des Erwachens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inside the film one is under the script but relatively free: in presence one can perform unscripted acts; a particle of freedom comes at the moment of waking, when one can come to one's senses and launch another reel; afterwards one is under a script again, but one's own film turns."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMissingTheMomentOfWakingTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Missing the moment of waking"@en, "Den Moment des Erwachens verpassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Failure condition: one's own film runs only if the moment of awakening was not let slip."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: One's own film runs only if the moment of awakening was not let slip. It bears on pmp:TranserfingUsingAllActivatorsTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingStandardisedIdealsTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Standardised ideals of beauty, success, happiness are illusions"@en, "Genormte Ideale von Schönheit, Erfolg, Glück sind Illusionen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Screens and covers display ideals that people try to match and always fail; beauty, success and happiness are strictly individual and cannot be standardised."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTryingMakeFraileFitStandardsCh9: the standards are those shown on screens and covers, and beauty, success and happiness are said to be strictly individual."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingUniquenessAsPerfectionTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNewLifeFromMondayTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why a new life from Monday never starts"@en, "Warum ein neues Leben ab Montag nie beginnt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not laziness but the script: one's \"I want\" is one's vector, which is not written into the script and does not affect it."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Not laziness but the script: one's \"I want\" is one's vector, which is not written into the script and does not affect it. It bears on pmp:TranserfingComplexAlgorithmOfTheWalkTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFailedImitationOfIdolsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why imitating screen idols failed"@en, "Warum das Nachahmen von Leinwandidolen scheiterte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inspired imitation after the cinema failed because one only wanted, unaware that a technology of imitation exists and really works, but only with a clever approach."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Inspired imitation after the cinema failed because one only wanted, unaware that a technology of imitation exists and really works, but only with a clever approach. It bears on pmp:TranserfingTechniqueOfImitationTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFirmKnowledgeOfPossibilityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Firm knowledge that self-change is possible"@en, "Festes Wissen, dass Selbstveränderung möglich ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing firmly that changing oneself, creating one's own mannequin, is possible in principle; put before anything else."@en ;
    skos:note "Prior step of pmc:TranserfingKnowingSelfChangeIsPossibleFirstTf; written by the integrator from the same passage."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingKnowingSelfChangeIsPossibleFirstTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Firm knowledge that it is possible"@en, "Feste Gewissheit, dass es möglich ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before all else one must know firmly that self-change of this kind is possible in principle."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingCreatingOneselfTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingFirmKnowledgeOfPossibilityTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCreatingOneselfTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating oneself, one's mannequin"@en, "Sich selbst, die eigene Puppe, erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims one can create not only reality but oneself, one's mannequin, which will change; moving through a sequence of reels and reflections, one becomes as one dreamed of seeing oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRunningIdleTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Idling: daydreams without the plait, unserious and unsystematic imitation"@en, "Leerlauf: Tagträume ohne Zopf, unernste und unsystematische Nachahmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Earlier attempts failed because one ran idle: picturing fame in daydreams is ineffective without the plait; imitating idols was not done in earnest, since one did not suspect one can create the reflection; nor systematically, since no results were visible at once."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Earlier attempts failed because one ran idle: picturing fame in daydreams is ineffective without the plait; imitating idols was not done in earnest, since one did not suspect one can create the reflection; nor systematically, since no results were visible at once. It bears on pmp:TranserfingTechniqueOfImitationTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBecomingMagnificentTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming magnificent; life turned into magnificence"@en, "Großartig werden; das Leben in Großartigkeit verwandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims that by moving oneself one can become magnificent, and by moving one's film at the same time turn one's whole life into splendour."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingComplexAlgorithmYieldsMagnificenceTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Complex algorithm yields magnificence"@en, "Komplexer Algorithmus ergibt Großartigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Combining self-movement with moving one's film."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingComplexAlgorithmOfTheWalkTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBecomingMagnificentTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 35; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingComplexAlgorithmOfTheWalkTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Complex algorithm of the movement-walk"@en, "Komplexer Algorithmus des Bewegungs-Gangs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) create one's new reality and one's new appearance in it; (2) pretend to have that reality and be that person already; (3) act, work on oneself, kindle the Spark of the Creator. To be done in earnest, systematically and long enough: always."@en ;
    skos:note "Joins the three levers of pmc:TranserfingThreeLeversTf: moving the future frame, moving through oneself, moving oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 36; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingComplexAlgorithmYieldsCreatingOneselfTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Complex algorithm yields creating oneself"@en, "Komplexer Algorithmus ergibt Selbsterschaffung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reel by reel and reflection by reflection the mannequin and life change."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingComplexAlgorithmOfTheWalkTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCreatingOneselfTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 36; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMannequinAndLifeVisiblyChangeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mannequin and life visibly change"@en, "Puppe und Leben ändern sich sichtbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: from reel to reel and reflection to reflection, one's mannequin and life will change, and one will undoubtedly see it."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: From reel to reel and reflection to reflection, one's mannequin and life will change, and one will undoubtedly see it. It bears on pmp:TranserfingComplexAlgorithmOfTheWalkTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ВЕЛИКОЛЕПНИ!', p. 36; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'ВИЕ СТЕ САМОТО СЪВЪРШЕНСТВО'
#

pmc:TranserfingMannequinPerReelTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Many mannequins, one per reel"@en, "Viele Puppen, eine je Spule"@de ;
    skos:definition "On the reels kept in the archive of Eternity one has one's own mannequins; in a dream consciousness finds its mannequin and animates it; likewise in waking life it enters the next version of the mannequin on each new reel; on nearby reels one looks roughly the same, on distant ones quite different."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: манекен."@en ;
    skos:note "Restates and extends pmc:TranserfingMannequinsTf, typed by part 1: the text introduces it as a reminder and adds that the mannequin differs from reel to reel."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ САМОТО СЪВЪРШЕНСТВО', p. 36; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRapidTransformationOfTheMannequinTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rapid transformation of the mannequin"@en, "Rasche Verwandlung der Puppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims the mannequin can change within a very short time, even at once: appearance can be strikingly transformed, and so can qualities and habits such as self-confidence, charm, sociability, courage, intellect, professionalism."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ САМОТО СЪВЪРШЕНСТВО', p. 36; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingChangingIsNotAbandoningOneselfTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Changing oneself is not abandoning oneself"@en, "Sich ändern heißt nicht sich aufgeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Changing means development, not renouncing oneself or one's identity, principles, convictions and creed; become better while staying oneself, kindle the Spark instead of remaking oneself; even one who likes oneself must not stop developing."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingSculptingOneselfTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ САМОТО СЪВЪРШЕНСТВО', p. 36; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingUniquenessAsPerfectionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Uniqueness as perfection and source of own standards"@en, "Einzigartigkeit als Vollkommenheit und Quelle eigener Maßstäbe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of adapting to others' standards create one's own, which is possible by accepting one's uniqueness; uniqueness is perfect because nothing like it exists anywhere, and it is largely sufficient; whether it is used or shelved is one's choice; accepting it is as hard as realising one is inside a film."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingUniquenessSoulKeySuccessX10: uniqueness is called perfect because nothing like it exists, and the ground for setting one's own standards."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ САМОТО СЪВЪРШЕНСТВО', p. 36; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingParadoxOfFlawsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Paradox of flaws: accepted becomes asset, fought becomes defect"@en, "Paradox der Makel: angenommen wird Vorzug, bekämpft wird Defekt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A flaw one accepts becomes a valuable individual trait; fought against, it turns into a defect, and others perceive it exactly so; perfection is individuality in its uniqueness at peace with itself; peace brings harmony, every non-acceptance brings a disharmony that all notice."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingCompensatingFlaws: the accepted flaw itself is said to become an asset, and others perceive it as asset or defect according to one's acceptance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ САМОТО СЪВЪРШЕНСТВО', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingDaysOfSelfAcceptanceTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "A few days of self-acceptance"@en, "Einige Tage Selbstannahme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before removing flaws, examine them closely without regard to standards; try for at least a few days to relax and accept oneself as one is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ САМОТО СЪВЪРШЕНСТВО', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingYouMayComeToLikeYourselfTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "You may come to like yourself"@en, "Man könnte sich zu mögen beginnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: one will see for oneself what happens; one may even begin to like oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: One will see for oneself what happens; one may even begin to like oneself. It bears on pmp:TranserfingDaysOfSelfAcceptanceTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ САМОТО СЪВЪРШЕНСТВО', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFlawsAreNotVicesTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Distinguish flaws from vices"@en, "Makel von Lastern unterscheiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "An obvious vice or weak spot that directly harms one's health or image, or harms others, must be rooted out."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDaysOfSelfAcceptanceTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ САМОТО СЪВЪРШЕНСТВО', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFocusingOnFlawsDeepensThemTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Focusing on flaws deepens them"@en, "Fokus auf Makel vertieft sie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not fight flaws: fixing attention on them, including physical ones that cannot be removed, only deepens them; work on a removable flaw through self-development only if one actually wishes to, otherwise leave oneself in peace and focus on one's qualities."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingDwellingOnFlaws: attention on flaws is said to deepen them, and removable flaws are to be worked on only where one wishes to."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDevelopingQualitiesTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ САМОТО СЪВЪРШЕНСТВО', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingDevelopingQualitiesTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Develop qualities rather than remove flaws"@en, "Qualitäten entwickeln statt Makel beseitigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Developing the qualities one has is far more effective than working on flaws, since it will most likely crowd them out or remove them automatically, and the question of flaws disappears."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFightingOnesOwnShortcomingsIsInnerIntentionCh12: developing qualities is said to crowd flaws out by itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ САМОТО СЪВЪРШЕНСТВО', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ'
#

pmp:TranserfingAcceptingOneselfAsAMiracleTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Accept oneself as a unique miracle and enjoy"@en, "Sich als einzigartiges Wunder annehmen und genießen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accept oneself, with all flaws, as a unique miracle, then simply enjoy oneself and life."@en ;
    skos:note "Tufti calls this a universal formula that works one hundred percent, but very hard to apply because of the load of templates and standards carried since birth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfAndLifeImproveTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self and life improve automatically"@en, "Selbst und Leben bessern sich von selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: if one can simply enjoy oneself and life, both oneself and one's life improve automatically and life sorts itself out."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: If one can simply enjoy oneself and life, both oneself and one's life improve automatically and life sorts itself out. It bears on pmp:TranserfingAcceptingOneselfAsAMiracleTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWayOfTheThreeAttainmentsTf a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "The way of the three attainments"@en, "Der Weg der drei Errungenschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "Three actions: (1) do not focus on flaws or dwell in a feeling of inferiority; (2) have an inspiring goal, a mission useful to oneself and others, and move toward it; (3) whether or not the mission is found, concentrate on development, on sculpting oneself, kindling the Spark. Together they yield three attainments: leaving the inferiority state, discovering the mission, realising it."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Начинът за трите постижения."@en ;
    skos:note "The source numbers the three actions and makes each lead to the next (the second helps out of the destructive state, the third helps where the mission is not yet found); entered as a series over the nodes that carry each action. No consequence of skipping is named, so no pm:Presupposing pairs are added beyond pmc:TranserfingDevelopmentBeforeMissionTf."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:TranserfingInferiorityStateIsDestructiveTf ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:TranserfingFindingTheMissionTf ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:TranserfingSculptingOneselfTf ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The way out of the load of standards runs in three numbered actions: leaving the destructive state of inferiority, which needs the second action; having a goal or mission, which, if not yet found, the third action supplies; and sculpting oneself, on whose path the mission finds itself. Together they give the three attainments of leaving inferiority, finding the mission and realising it." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLoadNotRemovedByThoughtTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The load is not removed by thought alone"@en, "Die Last fällt nicht durch bloßes Denken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The burden of patterns, standards, conventions and limits loaded since birth cannot be removed speculatively; three concrete actions are required."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingInferiorityStateIsDestructiveTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The inferiority state is destructive"@en, "Der Zustand der Minderwertigkeit ist zerstörerisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "One must not be in a state of feeling inadequate about anything; one must enter a constructive state instead, which the second action helps with."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingSculptingOneselfTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingFindingTheMissionTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Find a mission and move toward it"@en, "Eine Mission finden und auf sie zugehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Have a life goal that inspires, feeds enthusiasm and benefits oneself and others; discover one's cherished goal or mission and start moving toward it."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: мисия."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTsel: the goal is called the mission, the vector of self-realisation, which must benefit oneself and others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNoGoalNoLifeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No goal: apathy, no movement, no energy, no life"@en, "Kein Ziel: Apathie, keine Bewegung, keine Energie, kein Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Apathy toward everything signals having no goal; without a goal there is no movement, without movement no energy, without energy no life; without a mission one is an empty place."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Apathy toward everything signals having no goal; without a goal there is no movement, without movement no energy, without energy no life; without a mission one is an empty place. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFindingTheMissionTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 37; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingSculptingOneselfTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Constant self-sculpting"@en, "Ständiges Selbstformen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Concentrate on development and sculpting oneself, improve constantly and always, kindle the Spark of the Creator; even after the mission is found, do not stop."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeAttainmentsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The three attainments: out of inferiority, mission found, mission realised"@en, "Die drei Errungenschaften: aus der Minderwertigkeit, Mission gefunden, Mission verwirklicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims that kindling the Spark through self-improvement yields all three at once: leaving stagnation and inferiority, finding one's mission, realising it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNoMagicWandTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No magic wand; the plait needs work"@en, "Kein Zauberstab; der Zopf braucht Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "There is no magic wand; there is the plait, but one must work with it; nothing happens while lying on the sofa; goals are reached with the three movements."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingPlaitAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDevelopmentBeforeMissionTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Development before finding the mission"@en, "Entwicklung vor dem Finden der Mission"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the mission is not yet found, the third action (development) helps; on the path of self-development the mission is found by itself."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingFindingTheMissionTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingSculptingOneselfTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNeverStopDevelopingTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Never stop developing, even after the mission"@en, "Nie aufhören sich zu entwickeln, auch nach der Mission"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even when the mission is found one must not stop: there is either development or degradation."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingSculptingOneselfTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfImprovementAsPreparationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-improvement as pleasant preparation, not toil"@en, "Selbstverbesserung als angenehme Vorbereitung, nicht Mühsal"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stagnation, idleness and laziness weigh far more than development; improving oneself is pleasant preparation for something more pleasant, like dressing up for a party, except that for tomorrow, a month or a year ahead preparing once is not enough."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMissionAsVectorTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mission as the vector of self-realisation, known to the Spark"@en, "Mission als Vektor der Selbstverwirklichung, dem Funken bekannt"@de ;
    skos:definition "To become magnificent one must leave stagnation by finding the mission and moving toward it; the mission is the vector of self-realisation, without it life is senseless existence; if one does not know it, the smouldering Spark of the Creator does, but it must be kindled."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSculptingYieldsThreeAttainmentsTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Self-sculpting yields the three attainments"@en, "Selbstformen ergibt die drei Errungenschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "On the way of development the mission finds itself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSculptingOneselfTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingThreeAttainmentsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDevelopmentYieldsPersonalPowerTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Self-development yields personal energy"@en, "Selbstentwicklung ergibt persönliche Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Movement through development produces energy."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSculptingOneselfTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingPersonalPowerTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPersonalPowerBeforeMetapowerTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal energy before metapower"@en, "Persönliche Energie vor Metakraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Triggering metapower requires a sufficient amount of one's personal power, the energy acquired through movement and development."@en ;
    skos:note "The dependent step is the reel change that metapower (pmc:TranserfingMetapowerTf, part 1) launches."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingChangingFilmReelsTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingPersonalPowerTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without movement and development one lacks the strength to unlock metapower; without energy there is only fading." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPersonalPowerTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal power (energy)"@en, "Persönliche Kraft (Energie)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-development is movement and gives energy, one's personal power; Tufti claims that when in motion and developing one acquires it."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: лична сила."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingAskingTheDirectionOfDevelopmentTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ask oneself the direction of development"@en, "Sich nach der Richtung der Entwicklung fragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One knows best in which direction to develop; if not, ask oneself and set the goal \"to develop\", and one will find out."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNuancesOfTheMissionTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Nuances of the mission"@en, "Feinheiten der Mission"@de ;
    skos:definition "Two points: (1) follow the path of one's heart, finding what is truly one's own versus what only seems so; (2) follow one's own path, not others' footsteps, do not copy others' experience; allow oneself to be unique in everything."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMissionNeedsAnotherBookTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mission theme needs another book"@en, "Das Thema Mission braucht ein eigenes Buch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Statement on scope: the mission is a separate topic for a whole book; the reader is told to read other books too and study diligently."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'НАЧИНЪТ ЗА ТРИТЕ ПОСТИЖЕНИЯ', p. 38; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ'
#

pmc:TranserfingPerfectionMustBeBroughtOutTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Perfection must be brought out; its form is individual"@en, "Vollkommenheit muss hervorgebracht werden; ihre Form ist individuell"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because the Spark is present one is perfection, but it must be brought into the light by kindling; its form depends on individuality, whether it shows at all depends on one's intentions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImprovedMannequinOnAnotherReelTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wanted traits mean entering an improved mannequin on another reel"@en, "Gewünschte Eigenschaften heißt, in eine bessere Puppe auf anderer Spule zu treten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wanting a beautiful body, a charming personality or a highly paid career means entering another, improved mannequin on a fundamentally different reel; Tufti asserts that such a mannequin and reel really exist, one only needs to reach it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeMovementsTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The three movements"@en, "Die drei Bewegungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Move reality (with the plait), move through oneself (image and reflection), move oneself (material self-development)."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: трите движения."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingFirstMovementTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "First movement: creating new selves in the new reality with the plait"@en, "Erste Bewegung: neue Selbste in der neuen Realität mit dem Zopf erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Several times a day enter presence, activate the plait and, holding that sensation, paint the wanted picture (end result, target frame) mentally, in words or visually; about one minute each time, without strain, remembering that metapower works, not effort, and focus, not tension; consistently and systematically create the new self in the new reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNotEffortButMetapowerTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not effort but metapower"@en, "Nicht Anstrengung, sondern Metakraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Straining is useless in ordering: what works is metapower and concentration, not effort and tension."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingFirstMovementTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingAimingAtGeniusTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Set a high bar: aim at genius"@en, "Die Latte hoch legen: auf Genialität zielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not limit goals or waste oneself on trifles; for instance set the aim of awakening genius in oneself in some field; then, Tufti claims, one starts to act with genius regardless of abilities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingHighAimYieldsGeniusTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "High-bar aim yields acting with genius"@en, "Hohe Zielsetzung ergibt geniales Handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Setting genius as goal makes one start acting with genius."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAimingAtGeniusTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingActingWithGeniusTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingIsItYourPathTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Check whether it is your path if abilities are wholly lacking"@en, "Prüfen, ob es der eigene Weg ist, wenn Fähigkeiten völlig fehlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one lacks any ability for what attracts one, one should consider whether it is one's path; if it is the heart's path and the goal is realisable in principle, it can be realised, the rest depends on persistence."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAimingAtGeniusTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingActingWithGeniusTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Acting with genius; new abilities on new reels"@en, "Genial handeln; neue Fähigkeiten auf neuen Spulen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims that after a while one does things one could not and seemingly should not be able to do; on other reels, in the new mannequin, new abilities appear and ways to realise the plan open up, visible if one is not asleep."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGeniusLevelOriginalCreationAchievementCh9: acting with genius is ascribed to the script of the reel one is moved to, not to ability."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSurpriseAtNewAbilitiesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Surprise at doing what one could not do"@en, "Staunen, Unmögliches zu tun"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: one will be convinced and much surprised to find oneself doing things one never could."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: One will be convinced and much surprised to find oneself doing things one never could. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFirstMovementTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNotAMiracleButTechnologyTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not a miracle but technology: the script of the reel"@en, "Kein Wunder, sondern Technik: das Drehbuch der Spule"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creating a reality in which one is a genius moves one onto reels where one acts with genius, not because of ability but because that reel's script is so."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFirstMovementYieldsGeniusTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "First movement yields acting with genius"@en, "Erste Bewegung ergibt geniales Handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordering oneself as a genius via the plait shifts one to reels where one acts so."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFirstMovementTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingActingWithGeniusTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingSecondMovementTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Second movement: moving through oneself"@en, "Zweite Bewegung: durch sich selbst bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Become aware of motives and acts (otherwise messages to the mirror are only \"give\" toward people and \"I want\" toward reality); in a moment of presence recall the image and reflection algorithms; toward people replace every \"give me\" with \"take\"; toward reality use the target-frame algorithm and the principles of benefit, permission, following; turn every minus into a plus; where one has nothing to give, use imitation; re-study the chapter on image creation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingHabitualCharmTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming a charming personality by habit"@en, "Durch Gewohnheit eine charmante Persönlichkeit werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims that after persistent training the swap becomes habit, part of the new mannequin, and one becomes charming even without pretending."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSecondMovementYieldsCharmTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Second movement yields habitual charm"@en, "Zweite Bewegung ergibt gewohnheitsmäßigen Charme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Habitual giving reshapes the mannequin."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSecondMovementTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHabitualCharmTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingProblemsFallAwayTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tormenting problems drop away"@en, "Quälende Probleme fallen weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: along with the transformation, the problems that torment one will fall away or be solved."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Along with the transformation, the problems that torment one will fall away or be solved. It bears on pmp:TranserfingSecondMovementTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ВИЕ СТЕ ГЕНИАЛНИ', p. 39; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА'
#

pmc:TranserfingMechanicalDollsBetterThanMarionettesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Better mechanical dolls with right habits than marionettes"@en, "Lieber mechanische Puppen mit richtigen Gewohnheiten als Marionetten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Answering the worry that algorithms turn one into a clockwork doll: better a mechanical doll with right habits than an unaware marionette."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 40; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAcquiringAbsentQualitiesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Acquiring qualities one does not yet have"@en, "Eigenschaften erwerben, die man noch nicht hat"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims the imitation technique lets one gain qualities not yet possessed (beautiful body, charm, well-paid professional standing), since reality will turn the illusion into fact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 40; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingTechniqueOfImitationTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Technique of imitation (acquiring qualities)"@en, "Technik der Imitation (Eigenschaften erwerben)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagine already possessing the wanted qualities though it is only a game; watch those who have them and at first copy their manner if one has no idea of one's own, later individuality shows; notice what one likes in others in any field and borrow their genius (I do this as brilliantly as they do; I can create such a life too); soak up the brilliance and project it onto oneself and one's life; declare the intention with the plait; copy not the model as a whole but its state, self-regard, self-feeling and mood; enter the state in which one likes oneself and behave as if one already had the aim; build a virtual reality in thought, illuminate it now and then with the plait, keep it running in the background, systematically; live in that state even if the body is far from perfect."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: техниката на имитацията."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 40; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingProjectionIsEssenceTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Projection is essence, not form"@en, "Projektion ist Wesen, nicht Form"@de ;
    skos:definition "One need not copy others one to one, only take a projection of their genius; the projection is the essence, not a concrete form."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: проекция."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 40; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImitationTechniqueYieldsQualitiesTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Imitation technique yields new qualities"@en, "Imitationstechnik ergibt neue Eigenschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "Earnest, systematic imitation is turned into reality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTechniqueOfImitationTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAcquiringAbsentQualitiesTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 40; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingIllusionsEmbodiedOrDestroyedTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Self-made illusions are either embodied or destroyed"@en, "Selbstgemachte Illusionen werden verkörpert oder zerstört"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reality cannot bear illusions it did not produce itself, so created ones will either be made real or demolished; demolition is unlikely if one does not overdo it or ask for trouble, as even children know a game is a game and keep within the real."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingTechniqueOfImitationTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 40; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLimitsOfTheRealInTheGameTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Limits of the real in the game"@en, "Grenzen des Realen im Spiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "One sets the limits oneself: playing a charming person is quite possible, but performing professionally on a ballet stage or hockey rink never visited is not, since one has not yet reached that reel; the imitation remains no less effective; the third movement serves for this."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingTechniqueOfImitationTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 40; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingThirdMovementTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Third movement: moving oneself in the material plane"@en, "Dritte Bewegung: sich selbst auf der materiellen Ebene bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Be realistic: in a dual world act equally on the material plane; do everything needed for the goal in the current frame and sculpt oneself physically through concrete exercise, training, better nutrition and way of life, not only through plait and mirror."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 41; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBedMetaphysicsNotEnoughTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Bed metaphysics alone is not enough"@en, "Bettmetaphysik allein genügt nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Metaphysics practised in bed does not suffice."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingContemplationAloneInsufficient: the metaphysics in bed is set against concrete physical work on oneself in a dual world."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingFirstMovementTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 41; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAnswersComeOnThePathTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "On the path of development, answers come by themselves"@en, "Auf dem Entwicklungsweg kommen Antworten von selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: once on the path of development, what to do and how becomes clear, information comes by itself and the mission reveals itself; setting the aim of moving oneself brings all answers automatically."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Once on the path of development, what to do and how becomes clear, information comes by itself and the mission reveals itself; setting the aim of moving oneself brings all answers automatically. It bears on pmp:TranserfingThirdMovementTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 41; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMeansLieOnOtherReelsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Means for the mission lie on other reels"@en, "Mittel für die Mission liegen auf anderen Spulen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One need not worry about ways and means to realise the mission: they are not yet visible because they lie on reels still to be reached, which one will reach if all three movements are used."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 41; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOnlyTheThirdMovementTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Only the third movement: much effort, nothing achieved"@en, "Nur die dritte Bewegung: viel Mühe, nichts erreicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Competitors usually use only the third movement; many spend great effort and still achieve nothing."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Competitors usually use only the third movement; many spend great effort and still achieve nothing. It bears on pmp:TranserfingComplexAlgorithmOfTheWalkTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 41; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAllThreeMovementsTogetherTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Which movement works best: equally; combined gives full result; always"@en, "Welche Bewegung wirkt am besten: gleich; kombiniert volles Ergebnis; immer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Statement on method: it varies, on average equally; done in combination one gets a one-hundred-percent result; the three movements correct reality and order life in every respect; duration: always, since there is development or degradation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ТЕХНИКА НА ИМИТАЦИЯТА', p. 41; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ'
#

pmc:TranserfingFilmAspectAndMirrorAspectTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "New reality uses the film aspect, new self the mirror aspect"@en, "Neue Realität nutzt den Filmaspekt, neues Selbst den Spiegelaspekt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creating a new reality illuminates the future frame (reality as reel); imitating oneself in the new mannequin creates the reflection that then flows into the image (reality as mirror); both can and should be done with the plait."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 41; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingLivingTheNewRoleTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Living the new role"@en, "Die neue Rolle leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Create reality purposefully in set sessions several times a day, without strain; imitation, by contrast, is lived: pretend, play, live into the new role seriously and systematically, like actors before filming; forgetting the plait sometimes does no harm; absorb all information about the new mannequin and reality and try the role as circumstances allow, in thought, visually and in fact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 41; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingRepeatingThoughtFormsTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Thought-forms with the plait"@en, "Gedankenformen mit dem Zopf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeat as often as possible standard mental statements supporting the new role (examples given, own ones may be composed); activate the plait and say them aloud or silently; at the same time behave so as to match them, knowing it is a game but a serious one; and improve physically as well."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: мисъл-форми."@en ;
    skos:note "The thought-form as a term is pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsTf, typed by part 3; this node carries the practice as first given in this section."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 41; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSampleThoughtFormsTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sample thought-forms in four themes"@en, "Beispielhafte Gedankenformen in vier Themen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Model sets: top professional who is unique, in demand and valued; homemaker loved by husband and children who creates a festive home; excellent health with a body like at twenty by own decision and high vitality; charming, charismatic personality radiating a metaphysical glow that people feel."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 41; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerQualitiesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Charm, wit, intellect, confidence, genius"@en, "Charme, Witz, Intellekt, Selbstvertrauen, Genialität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims such qualities appear easily already with the first two movements; physical parameters are harder and need emphasis on the third."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 42; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsYieldInnerQualitiesTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Thought-forms and imitation yield the inner qualities"@en, "Gedankenformen und Imitation ergeben die inneren Eigenschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "First two movements suffice for these qualities."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRepeatingThoughtFormsTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingInnerQualitiesTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 42; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingComplexesMarkTheBodyTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inferiority complexes mark face and figure"@en, "Minderwertigkeitskomplexe prägen Gesicht und Gestalt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Physical attractiveness depends largely on inner qualities; complexes leave a visible imprint on face and figure, and fall away by themselves once qualities are acquired."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 42; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBecomingUnrecognisableTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming unrecognisable"@en, "Unkenntlich werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: when complexes drop away one will be so transformed that people will not recognise one."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: When complexes drop away one will be so transformed that people will not recognise one. It bears on pmp:TranserfingRepeatingThoughtFormsTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 42; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImprovingTheBodyTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Improving the body, even reversing ageing"@en, "Den Körper verbessern, sogar das Altern umkehren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims that within certain limits the mannequin's body can be much improved, strictly by entering another mannequin, and with enough persistence anything is possible, including reversing ageing."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAgeingAsAnInducedTransitionCh11: reversing ageing is said to need entering another mannequin, with enough persistence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 42; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingProjectInTheArchiveOfEternityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "DNA holds only the basics; the project lies in the archive of Eternity"@en, "DNA enthält nur Grundzüge; das Projekt liegt im Archiv der Ewigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "DNA records only main traits, barely enough to describe the embryo; a large part of the information of one's \"project\" is held in the information space called the archive of Eternity, and the project can be corrected."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: архив на Вечността."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 42; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstOfficialScienceTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against official science on the information space"@en, "Gegen die offizielle Wissenschaft zum Informationsraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Official science, the text says, refuses to admit the information space, having taken on the task of explaining everything scientifically and rejecting or ignoring what it cannot explain; the inexplicable does not thereby cease to exist."@en ;
    skos:note "Only the author's side is read, so recorded as a concept, not a dispute."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAgainstMechanisticMaterialistScienceAft: the dispute concerns the information space, called the archive of Eternity, which science is said to refuse."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 42; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCorrectingTheProjectTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Correcting one's project"@en, "Das eigene Projekt korrigieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims the project according to which one developed after the embryo stage can be corrected (method announced for the following lesson)."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: проекта."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 42; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ'
#

pmc:TranserfingThirdMovementYieldsBodilyImprovementTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Three movements yield bodily improvement"@en, "Drei Bewegungen ergeben körperliche Verbesserung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Physical parameters can be considerably improved through the three movements, with emphasis on the third."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingThirdMovementTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingImprovingTheBodyTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 42; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMindReadsInformationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mind invents nothing, it reads information"@en, "Der Verstand erfindet nichts, er liest Information"@de ;
    skos:definition "One's mind cannot construct anything on its own; it only reads information by steering attention; even self-made thought-forms are read, not invented."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 42; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBrainAsReceiverTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Brain as receiver with three functions"@en, "Gehirn als Empfänger mit drei Funktionen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The brain perceives, interprets, and tunes (to memory, thinking and state); it neither generates thoughts nor stores memories but works like a radio or TV receiver, tuning to blocks of information in the archive of Eternity and turning scanned information into a flow that appears as thoughts."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingSubconsciousReadsTheField: the brain itself is the receiver, with tuning as its third function, and thoughts and memories are held outside it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 42; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingStateSynchronisesWithProjectTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "State and its synchronisation with the project"@en, "Zustand und seine Synchronisierung mit dem Projekt"@de ;
    skos:definition "State is feeling oneself as created by Nature, more exactly according to the project; accepting what was given, one stays so, or one changes for better or worse under the vector of one's strivings and of society; each time one feels oneself a certain way the state synchronises with the project, and mismatches correct the project in that direction, whatever its initial parameters."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: синхронизиране."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRandomSynchronisationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Random synchronisation for the unaware"@en, "Zufällige Synchronisierung bei den Unbewussten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unaware characters drift with the script relying on chance and squirm in the current frame; synchronisation then happens arbitrarily, independent of them, so the lucky become stars and the unlucky slide into the pit."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Unaware characters drift with the script relying on chance and squirm in the current frame; synchronisation then happens arbitrarily, independent of them, so the lucky become stars and the unlucky slide into the pit. It bears on pmp:TranserfingFixingProgressWithThoughtMarkersTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTuningIsNotYetSynchronisationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating and tuning to new selves is not yet synchronisation"@en, "Neue Selbste erschaffen und sich einstimmen ist noch keine Synchronisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creating new reality and new selves, shaping and tuning to them means entering the new state purposefully, yet this is not synchronisation: declaring thought-forms creates a reality not yet realised, and even imitation does not fully reach the needed state."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSeeingOnesProgressTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing one's own progress on new reels"@en, "Den eigenen Fortschritt auf neuen Spulen sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: one moves to new reels, enters new mannequins and observes one's progress with one's own eyes; one will surely see it and say that it really works, and then truly enter the state."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: One moves to new reels, enters new mannequins and observes one's progress with one's own eyes; one will surely see it and say that it really works, and then truly enter the state. It bears on pmp:TranserfingRepeatingThoughtFormsTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSynchronisationSeriesTf a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "From thought-forms to thought-markers"@en, "Von Gedankenformen zu Gedankenmarkern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The source's own order of how the state is truly entered: declaring thought-forms creates a reality not yet realised, then one moves to new reels and sees one's progress, and in that true state the thought-forms become thought-markers."@en ;
    skos:note "The first and third members are typed by part 3 (pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsTf, pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersTf). The order of practice is also entered as pmc:TranserfingFormsBeforeMarkersTf."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: the series was recorded by pass A only as a prerequisite pair."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsTf ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:TranserfingSeeingOnesProgressTf ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersTf ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Each stage has its sense only after the one before: the forms define a reality not yet realised, the progress seen on new reels is what convinces, and only then do the forms turn into markers that confirm, at which moment synchronisation with the project takes place." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFormsBeforeMarkersTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "First results before thought-markers"@en, "Erste Ergebnisse vor Gedankenmarkern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thought-markers presuppose observed results: forms first, then the move to new reels and visible progress, then marking it; markers are what is already confirmed."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingFixingProgressWithThoughtMarkersTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingRepeatingThoughtFormsTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSampleThoughtMarkersTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sample thought-markers"@en, "Beispielhafte Gedankenmarker"@de ;
    skos:definition "Two lists of marker phrases, three and four items, each registering as already happening: defining one's reality, intention working, entering a new mannequin; then daily approach to the goal, growing professionalism, improving physical form, becoming charming and attractive."@en ;
    skos:note "Text layer: the sample markers are prefixed with # in the file."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingConfirmationOverAssertionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Thought-forms versus thought-markers"@en, "Gedankenformen gegenüber Gedankenmarkern"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the true state thought-forms turn into thought-markers; markers note that something is happening and so confirm it as fact, designations of what has already happened needing no proof; forms are assertions trying to prove themselves; only confirmation works one hundred percent; forms affect the project too, but more weakly, because synchronisation occurs on meeting the actual situation; forms define reality, markers correct the project."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: мисъл-маркери."@en ;
    skos:note "The two terms are pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsTf and pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersTf, typed by part 3; this node carries the claim about their difference in force as stated in this section."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingProvingAndPersuadingIsUselessTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Trying to prove or persuade is useless"@en, "Beweisen oder Überreden wollen ist nutzlos"@de ;
    skos:definition "Striving to prove something to oneself or others is unconvincing; persuading oneself or reality is futile; one may pretend but cannot convince oneself, and persuasion does not bring a pure state without a grain of doubt."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAffirmingConfidenceCh13: assertions that try to prove are set against confirmations of what has already happened."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingRepeatingThoughtFormsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingFixingProgressWithThoughtMarkersTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Fixing progress with thought-markers"@en, "Fortschritt mit Gedankenmarkern festhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perform all three movements and watch one's progress; when the first results appear, give them special attention and, again with the plait, state that everything is really working, using phrases that register a fact (e.g. that one defines one's reality, that intention works, that one is entering a new mannequin, that each day brings one closer to the goal, that skill, physique and charm are actually improving)."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: мисъл-маркери."@en ;
    skos:note "The thought-marker as a term is pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersTf, typed by part 3; the example phrases are summarised, not translated."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersYieldTouchTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Thought-markers yield touching outer intention"@en, "Gedankenmarker ergeben Berührung der äußeren Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Confirming with the plait brings the touch of outer intention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFixingProgressWithThoughtMarkersTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingTouchingOuterIntentionTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTouchingOuterIntentionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Touching outer intention at synchronisation"@en, "Berührung der äußeren Absicht bei der Synchronisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tufti claims that at the moment of confirming results with the plait one truly touches outer intention, and at that same moment synchronisation with the project takes place."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsYieldReelChangeTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Thought-forms yield defining reality"@en, "Gedankenformen ergeben Bestimmen der Realität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thought-forms define reality, i.e. order the new reel."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRepeatingThoughtFormsTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingChangingFilmReelsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersYieldProjectCorrectionTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Thought-markers yield project correction"@en, "Gedankenmarker ergeben Projektkorrektur"@de ;
    skos:definition "Markers correct the project."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFixingProgressWithThoughtMarkersTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCorrectingTheProjectTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .


#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), part 3:
# sections ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ to ОБЗОР НА ОСНОВНИТЕ ПРИНЦИПИ (pp. 44-65), with the
# conclusion, the algorithms and the overview of principles. Read in the
# Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova (spiralata.net), the only translation
# reached; places are cited by section heading and e-book page.
#
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 246 records, B 264;
# 11 records of B without counterpart in A: 0 added, 11 covered, 0 not owed);
# a reader of the whole part added 2 records both passes missed (the readers'
# greatness in former incarnations; living unaware despite self-awareness).
# The algorithms and the overview largely restate earlier chapters of this
# book: those records are counted, not written, and fixed ids of parts 1 and 2
# are linked. Stupen' I to V (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl to -5.ttl)
# are not restated; nodes that restate one with a difference say so in a note.
#
# Shared terms typed here: pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsTf,
# pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersTf, pmc:TranserfingGreedyHuntersTf,
# pmc:TranserfingLadaTf, pmc:TranserfingAlgorithmsTf,
# pmc:TranserfingOverviewOfPrinciplesTf. Tafti as named and the book as her
# speech are typed by part 1 (pmc:TranserfingTaftiTf,
# pmc:TranserfingTaftiReceivingTf) and not retyped here.
#

#
# section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ'
#

pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Thought-markers"@en, "Gedankenmarker"@de ;
    skos:definition "Short statements set with the plait once progress is actually seen, registering as fact what has already happened, such as that one comes closer to the goal each day or that one's personal power really grows. They are the confirmation that success is real, and it is they that correct the project."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: мисъл-маркери."@en ;
    skos:note "The chapter that introduces them, МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ, is cited as the place; the id was typed by the integrator of the last part, from its recapitulation, its algorithms and its overview. Thought-forms turn into thought-markers once the genuine state is reached (pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsTf)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ', p. 43; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Thought-forms"@en, "Gedankenformen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Set formulas of thought about the self and the reality one is building, to be repeated to oneself as often as possible as a support while trying on a new role in thought, in images and in deed; the chapter gives sample sets about work, home, health and charm. Later chapters have them pronounced with the plait active and contrast them with thought-markers, which register what has already happened."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: мисъл-форми."@en ;
    skos:note "The chapter that introduces them, МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ, is cited as the place; the id was typed by the integrator of the last part. Linked: pmp:TranserfingPlaitWithFlowsAlgorithmTf, pmc:TranserfingWaterSoaksIntentionTf, pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'МИСЪЛ ФОРМИ', p. 41; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCorrectedProjectTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Corrected project: becoming somewhat another person"@en, "Korrigiertes Projekt: ein etwas anderer Mensch werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "When observed progress is fixed, the project is said to be corrected: one becomes a little or a great deal different, as if stepping into a new body in new clothes, and by performing the three movements regularly one climbs step by step to ever higher levels."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: проект."@en ;
    skos:note "The project and its synchronization with the state are introduced before this part (МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ); this node carries the outcome as part 3 promises it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 44; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingSynchronizationAlgorithmTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Algorithm of synchronization"@en, "Algorithmus der Synchronisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Three steps: perform the three movements, one at a time or all together as one likes; observe attentively and catch every confirmation of one's successes eagerly; as soon as one is seen, activate the plait and fix the progress with a thought-marker."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Алгоритъм на синхронизирането."@en ;
    skos:note "Repeated in АЛГОРИТМИТЕ (p. 55) as the algorithm of synchronizing the project, framed by a recap of the DNA scheme and the project; not written again. Linked: pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersTf, pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf, pmc:TranserfingGreedyHuntersTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 44; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSynchronizationYieldsCorrectedProjectTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Synchronization algorithm yields the corrected project"@en, "Synchronisierungsalgorithmus bewirkt das korrigierte Projekt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doing the three movements regularly, catching confirmations and delighting in them with the plait is said to correct the project and lift one gradually to higher levels."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSynchronizationAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCorrectedProjectTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 44; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingGreedyHuntersTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Greedy hunters of confirmations"@en, "Gierige Jäger der Bestätigungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The figure the lesson is named after: the practitioner is to watch closely for signs that the practice works and seize every confirmation of success avidly, then savour it with the plait active, because belief and with it the genuine state come only from confirmation one has seen."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: лакомите ловци (the section title)."@en ;
    skos:note "The habit of rejoicing in observed progress with the plait is restated from the chapter МИСЪЛ МАРКЕРИ and carried here and in pmp:TranserfingSynchronizationAlgorithmTf, not as a separate practice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 44; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRealitySuppliesTheMeansTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality supplies the means of realization"@en, "Die Wirklichkeit liefert die Mittel der Verwirklichung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Progress will show both in what one intended and in the ways of achieving it: reality will throw such ways in one's path and nudge one to take them."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: progress will show both in what one intended and in the ways of achieving it: reality will throw such ways in one's path and nudge one to take them; it bears on pmp:TranserfingSynchronizationAlgorithmTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 44; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDefeatMustNotSynchronizeTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not let a defeat synchronize with the project"@en, "Eine Niederlage nicht mit dem Projekt synchronisieren lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Defeats cannot be avoided; after one, the state turns toward feeling a failure, and should that state synchronize with the project the result would be dreadful. This must never be allowed; the remedy named is the principle of benefit."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingSynchronizationAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 44; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingTendingTheStateAfterAWinTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Tending the state after a win"@en, "Den Zustand nach einem Sieg pflegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "After a success, look after the resulting state carefully and enjoy it while keeping the plait in mind; treat one's state with care and responsibility and govern it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 44; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTendingTheStateYieldsCorrectedProjectTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tending the state after a win yields the corrected project"@en, "Pflege des Zustands nach einem Sieg bewirkt das korrigierte Projekt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Caring for and savouring the winning state with the plait is said to correct the project, which then develops in the best way."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTendingTheStateAfterAWinTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCorrectedProjectTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 44; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRealizationTakesAnotherRouteTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Realization takes another route than planned"@en, "Die Verwirklichung nimmt einen anderen Weg als geplant"@de ;
    skos:definition "One cannot know how a goal will come about: it may seem that nothing works while it is working, only not in the way one had planned; nobody promised a smooth path."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingScenarioTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 44; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMissingResultsAreNoFailureTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Missing results are no failure"@en, "Fehlende Ergebnisse sind kein Scheitern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not seeing results yet should not be troubling: reality responds with a delay, so patience, persistence and consistency are needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Pass A recorded this as a failure condition; it is entered as a caution, since the text denies that missing results mean failure."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingSynchronizationAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 44; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLockedDoorTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A door locked to oneself"@en, "Eine einem selbst verschlossene Tür"@de ;
    skos:definition "If something fails in principle, as if one were knocking at a door locked to oneself, one should ask whether this path is truly one's own, the path of one's heart."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: if something fails in principle, as if one were knocking at a door locked to oneself, one should ask whether this path is truly one's own, the path of one's heart; it bears on pmp:TranserfingSynchronizationAlgorithmTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPathOfSelfDevelopmentTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-development as the path that never fails"@en, "Selbstentwicklung als der Weg, der nie im Stich lässt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The only path said never to let one down is self-development, though not any kind (learning ancient Greek is the counter-example) but one that inspires and bears real fruit for oneself. It is repeated among the recap points of the next lesson."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: пътят на саморазвитието."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNoMannequinBeforeAFlatMirrorTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No mannequin before an ordinary mirror"@en, "Kein Manekin vor dem gewöhnlichen Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "One may create oneself only in the mirror of reality, using the plait; making one's mannequin before an ordinary flat mirror is expressly forbidden, because it will not work or will work in reverse. Before a flat mirror one may only register positive changes and ignore the flaws."@en ;
    skos:note "Linked: pmc:TranserfingRealityMirrorTf, pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMannequinsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMannequinBeforeAFlatMirrorFailsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mannequin made before a flat mirror fails or reverses"@en, "Vor dem flachen Spiegel gebildetes Manekin versagt oder kehrt sich um"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creating one's mannequin before an ordinary mirror instead of the mirror of reality with the plait does not work, or works the other way round."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: creating one's mannequin before an ordinary mirror instead of the mirror of reality with the plait does not work, or works the other way round; it bears on creating one's mannequin (pmc:TranserfingMannequinsTf); see pmc:TranserfingNoMannequinBeforeAFlatMirrorTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNoAttentionOnFlawsTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not fix attention on the flaws one wants to lose"@en, "Die Aufmerksamkeit nicht auf loszuwerdende Mängel heften"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attention must not be fastened on the shortcomings one wishes to be rid of."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingDwellingOnFlaws: there, thoughts circling around physical flaws block the line with a fit body; here the injunction stands bare, within creating oneself before the mirror of reality."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingImproveOrAcceptFlawsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingImproveOrAcceptFlawsTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Improving or accepting flaws"@en, "Mängel verbessern oder annehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A shortcoming is either removed by improving oneself or accepted as part of one's uniqueness; where nothing can be done about it, it is to be left as it is."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingCompensatingFlaws: there a flaw is offset by another quality; here it is either worked away by self-improvement or accepted as uniqueness, with no compensation named."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАКОМИТЕ ЛОВЦИ', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ЛАДА'
#

pmc:TranserfingGoverningOnesStateTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Either one governs one's state or it governs one"@en, "Entweder man lenkt seinen Zustand oder er lenkt einen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state is to be handled with care and governed, being first the key to one's project and secondly something more, which the lesson then names as the climate of one's reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Repeated in АЛГОРИТМИТЕ (p. 55) in the recap before the synchronization steps."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAwakeButNotInvulnerableTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Being awake does not make one invulnerable"@en, "Wachsein macht nicht unverwundbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Waking in the film gives no protection: whatever happens in the film can happen to oneself, and the film does not change because one has woken. The task is to order a film in which things go well for oneself; for misfortune that does happen there is the principle of benefit."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingWakingInTheFilmTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingOrderingBenefitInAdvanceTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ordering benefit in advance"@en, "Nutzen im Voraus bestellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "For an event so important to one that the importance itself stands in the way of its calm success, declare beforehand every possible outcome to be beneficial: if it works out, good; if it does not, better still."@en ;
    skos:note "The text presents it as an addition to the algorithm of benefit, which applies to what has already happened, and declines to give it as a separate algorithm."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingImportanceDefeatsThePlaitTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Importance can defeat even the plait"@en, "Wichtigkeit kann selbst den Zopf vereiteln"@de ;
    skos:definition "When an event matters so much that its importance obstructs its calm and successful course, even the plait does not always help."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: when an event matters so much that its importance obstructs its calm and successful course, even the plait does not always help; it bears on the plait (pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf) and is answered by pmp:TranserfingOrderingBenefitInAdvanceTf; importance as in pmc:TranserfingVazhnost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLoweredImportanceAndRaisedMoodTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lowered importance and raised mood"@en, "Gesenkte Wichtigkeit und gehobene Stimmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Declaring all outcomes beneficial lowers importance and lifts the mood, since one does not know which turn of the scenario is truly to one's good."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Importance is the notion of pmc:TranserfingVazhnost (Stupen' I), linked, not retyped."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBenefitInAdvanceYieldsLoweredImportanceTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Benefit in advance yields lowered importance"@en, "Nutzen im Voraus bewirkt gesenkte Wichtigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordering benefit in advance is said to lower importance and raise the mood."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingOrderingBenefitInAdvanceTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingLoweredImportanceAndRaisedMoodTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingConstantOrderingIsTiringTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Constant ordering of good reels is tiring"@en, "Ständiges Bestellen guter Filmrollen ermüdet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordering, again and again, film reels in which everything goes well is useful but becomes a tiring and tense habit; the lesson offers a way to relax, the climate of one's reality."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingFilmReelTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWeatherAtHomeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Weather at home: the climate of the current reel"@en, "Wetter zu Hause: das Klima der laufenden Filmrolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Besides the principles taught so far, reality has a general condition, aggressive or peaceful, that is personal to each: in the same place one person may be in a blue lagoon and another in an icy desert. This climate is set by one's state, one's mood and one's disposition toward everyone around."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: времето вкъщи."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLadaTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lada"@en, "Lada"@de ;
    skos:definition "The general term for one's own state and the state of reality alike: harmony, pleasure and delight, living in peace and concord, order and wellbeing; the word also means the beloved. Life becomes Lada if one loves life; Lada is when all is well and as it should be, not only when it happens to be so but because one can deliberately place oneself in that state."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Лада."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 45; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingMakingLadaTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Making Lada"@en, "Lada machen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever does not love oneself is told to make Lada, and self-love will follow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingComingToLoveOneselfTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Coming to love oneself"@en, "Sich selbst lieben lernen durch Lada"@de ;
    skos:definition "Love of oneself, promised as what follows from making Lada."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMakingLadaYieldsSelfLoveTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Making Lada yields self-love"@en, "Lada machen bewirkt Selbstliebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Making Lada is said to lead one to love oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingLearningLoveCh9: there self-love is learned by accepting oneself unconditionally and treating oneself; here it follows from making Lada."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingMakingLadaTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingComingToLoveOneselfTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLadaMadeOnPurposeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lada made on purpose"@en, "Absichtlich hergestellte Lada"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the principle of benefit, ever fewer harmful events occur and Lada appears of itself; better still is to create it deliberately by dwelling in the matching state."@en ;
    skos:note "The law of benefit is recalled from the chapter ПОЛЗАТА; what is added is Lada as its result and its deliberate making."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingStateAttractsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The state attracts people and reality"@en, "Der Zustand zieht Menschen und Wirklichkeit an"@de ;
    skos:definition "State is not only the key to the project but also what attracts: people look first for pleasure and are drawn to whoever radiates it, and reality too becomes peaceful near such people, whereas discontent, anger and ill will drive people away and darken reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Given as the reason for the earlier advice to copy the self-feeling and state of one's idols."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingDwellingInLadaTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dwelling in Lada"@en, "In Lada verweilen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Try to remain in Lada: look for pleasure in small things, make a celebration of any occasion, create a light and gracious atmosphere within and around oneself, be well-disposed toward people and toward one's reality whatever it is, prepare a favourable climate for intention, and make all this a habit."@en ;
    skos:note "The text calls it perhaps the most useful of all habits taught so far."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingHabitOfPleasure: pleasure in small things is kept, but here it is joined to festivity, benevolence toward reality itself and a climate for intention, under the name Lada."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingAttractingPeopleAndRealityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Attracting people and a favourable reality"@en, "Menschen und eine günstige Wirklichkeit anziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Radiating pleasure, love, comfort and festivity, that is Lada, is said to attract people and positive reality at once; reality becomes well-disposed to those who radiate it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDwellingInLadaYieldsAttractionTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dwelling in Lada yields attraction"@en, "Verweilen in Lada bewirkt Anziehung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Benevolence and radiated Lada are said to dispose people and reality favourably toward one."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDwellingInLadaTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAttractingPeopleAndRealityTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDisplayedHappinessIsPropsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Displayed happiness is largely stage props"@en, "Zur Schau gestelltes Glück ist großenteils Kulisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "The successful, rich, beautiful and happy people of screens and magazine covers, beside whom one's own life seems a failure, are said to be in large part props and bluff; the reader now knows how to arrange genuine Lada and is able to."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЛАДА', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ'
#

pmc:TranserfingGoverningTheWeatherTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Governing the weather of one's reality"@en, "Das Wetter der eigenen Wirklichkeit lenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because one can place oneself in Lada on purpose and then all goes well, this is likened to an ability to control the weather."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDwellingInLadaYieldsWeatherControlTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Entering Lada at will yields control of the weather"@en, "Willentliches Eintreten in Lada bewirkt Herrschaft über das Wetter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Placing oneself in Lada deliberately is likened to governing the weather of one's reality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDwellingInLadaTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingGoverningTheWeatherTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingStateLeftToDriftTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A state left to drift"@en, "Ein treiben gelassener Zustand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leaving one's state to chance is like dangling as a rag doll, swung by chance or by somebody's will; govern the state and create one's own Lada."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingLadaTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingFestiveOasisTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "A festive oasis that travels with one"@en, "Eine festliche Oase, die mitreist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bring light into every group of people; create in one's frame a personal oasis of festivity that goes wherever one goes; begin each day with the word Lada; enter that state always, whatever the circumstances."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingObservingInsteadOfFightingTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Observing instead of fighting emotions"@en, "Beobachten statt Gefühle bekämpfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When overwhelming irritation, fear or anger takes hold, do not fight the emotions but begin to watch what happens to oneself and to reality; every mishap should prompt such watching; look at one's fear as through a magnifying glass."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingObservingReactions: there one watches how each negative reaction draws a further misfortune; here the watching is aimed at the emotion and at reality themselves, to take away their hold."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFearShrinksUnderObservationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear shrinks and reality loosens its hold"@en, "Angst schrumpft und die Wirklichkeit lockert den Griff"@de ;
    skos:definition "Examined closely, fear paradoxically grows smaller; observed reality loses its power over one, begins to slip away and stops ruling one."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingObservingYieldsReleaseTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Observing yields release from fear"@en, "Beobachten bewirkt Lösung von der Angst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Watching one's emotions and reality is said to diminish their power."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingObservingInsteadOfFightingTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFearShrinksUnderObservationTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCornerOfTheEyeTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Watch reality only from the corner of the eye"@en, "Die Wirklichkeit nur aus dem Augenwinkel betrachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reality dislikes being watched; look at it sideways, not head-on, so as not to anger it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingObservingInsteadOfFightingTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlaitSensationIsIndividualTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The feeling of the plait is individual"@en, "Das Gefühl des Zopfes ist individuell"@de ;
    skos:definition "One need not feel the plait literally as a plait, or more than dimly: sensations differ, and some feel only a tension or a presence on the back that is phantom rather than bodily. Even a purely imagined presence works, like the lingering sense of a stiff straight plait fixed to the nape and then taken away."@en ;
    skos:note "A friend of the speaker is cited as an example of the tension on the back; a person merely mentioned, so no naming. Linked: pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 46; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingArrowActivationTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Activating the plait with an arrow"@en, "Den Zopf mit einem Pfeil aktivieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Picture an arrow, a mere vector, running from the nape straight down to the middle of the back; breathe in, and while breathing out picture the arrow lifting away from the back at an angle. If a phantom sensation appears, use this means to activate the plait; neither angle nor distance matters, since the energy body itself settles the arrow's active position."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingPointBehindTheShoulderBladesTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Attending to a point behind the shoulder blades"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit auf einen Punkt hinter den Schulterblättern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without the arrow, simply directing attention to a point some thirty centimetres or less behind the middle of the shoulder blades is enough to activate the plait."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTangiblyFeelingThePlaitTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling the plait tangibly"@en, "Den Zopf spürbar fühlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "With time and some practice one learns to sense the plait fairly tangibly."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPhysicallyFeelingTheCentralCurrentsCh11: the growing tangibility is said here of the plait, not of the energy currents."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingArrowActivationYieldsFeelingThePlaitTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Plait practice yields feeling the plait"@en, "Zopfübung bewirkt das Spüren des Zopfes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeated activation of the plait is said to train the sense of it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingArrowActivationTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingTangiblyFeelingThePlaitTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThePlaitMustBeTrainedTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The plait must be trained"@en, "Der Zopf muss geübt werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The plait has to be exercised, because it has withered from disuse; tangible sensing comes only after practice."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMeridiansAtrophyWithLoweredIntentionCh11: atrophy through disuse is said here of the plait, not of the meridians, and is met by training rather than by renewed intention."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingTangiblyFeelingThePlaitTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingArrowActivationTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingRisingAndFallingFlowsTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Rising and falling energy flows with the breath"@en, "Auf- und absteigende Energieströme mit dem Atem"@de ;
    skos:definition "Picture an energy flow rising along the central axis of the body: on the in-breath feel a sensation creeping from the feet to the head; then picture the reverse flow and feel it descend on the out-breath. Repeat several times, up with the in-breath, down with the out-breath."@en ;
    skos:note "Offered as a further way, for advanced practitioners, to make the plait more effective."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingEnergyFountainsAndProtectiveSphereCh11: the same two breath-linked currents, but without fountains or sphere, as preparation for releasing both flows from the plait."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergyFlowsAreRealTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The energy flows are real though felt as phantom"@en, "Die Energieströme sind wirklich, auch wenn phantomhaft gefühlt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sensations of the flows are phantom, but the flows themselves are said to be entirely real; without the necessary training one may simply not feel them."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: енергийните потоци."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingEnergiya: the two currents are not placed relative to the spine by sex or derived from cosmic free energy; only their reality against their phantom feel is asserted."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingTwoArrowsReleaseTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Releasing both flows with two arrows"@en, "Beide Ströme mit zwei Pfeilen freisetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Picture two opposite arrows, one pointing forward from the chest or belly, one backward from between the shoulder blades or lower. Breathing out, turn the front one straight up and the back one straight down, and feel the rising flow just ahead of the axis and the falling flow behind it run at once. Repeat; then release both flows on an out-breath without arrows; then activate the plait with the nape arrow, breathe a few times, and on an out-breath drop it sharply downward, releasing both flows together. After some training it should work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotStrainPlaitOrFlowsTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not strain with the plait or the flows"@en, "Weder Zopf noch Ströme erzwingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Neither the plait nor the flows are to be forced: one starts the flows and they move by themselves; one only lets them go and calmly allows them to run."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNoStrainingInTheFountainExerciseCh11: the warning against strain is extended from the currents to the plait."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingTwoArrowsReleaseTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingPlaitWithFlowsAlgorithmTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Algorithm of the plait with flows"@en, "Algorithmus des Zopfes mit den Strömen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Five steps: breathe in, and breathing out picture the nape arrow turning away from the back at an angle, so the plait is active; still feeling it, create one's reality while breathing normally; still feeling the plait, breathe in and on the out-breath drop it sharply, releasing both flows; feeling the rising and falling flow, say aloud or inwardly the thought-form that one's intention is being realized; then end all sensations."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: алгоритъмът на плитката с потоците."@en ;
    skos:note "Optional: if it works and pleases, it may be used always; otherwise the basic plait algorithm suffices. Repeated in АЛГОРИТМИТЕ (pp. 52-53); not written again. Linked: pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf, pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoArrowsBeforeTheFlowAlgorithmTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Two-arrow exercise before the flow algorithm"@en, "Zwei-Pfeile-Übung vor dem Strömungsalgorithmus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The plait-with-flows algorithm is given after, and builds on, the arrow activation and the two-flow release taught just before it."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingPlaitWithFlowsAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingTwoArrowsReleaseTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingIntentionSentIntoSpaceTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intention sent into space as a message"@en, "Die Absicht als Botschaft in den Raum gesandt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Besides creating reality with the plait, one has set one's intention going as a message into space, so that the flows reinforce the plait's work."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlaitWithFlowsYieldsIntentionSentTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Plait with flows yields intention sent into space"@en, "Zopf mit Strömen bewirkt die ausgesandte Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The flows are said to dispatch the intention into space and amplify the plait."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPlaitWithFlowsAlgorithmTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingIntentionSentIntoSpaceTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingPlaitInTheBathTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The plait in the bath or any water"@en, "Der Zopf in der Wanne oder in jedem Gewässer"@de ;
    skos:definition "While lying in the bath, or in any body of water, activate the plait (the tub wall is no obstacle), with or without the flows, and create reality, oneself as a new mannequin, or both; concentrate for two or three minutes without straining, then release the plait and stay about ten more minutes in the water."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 47; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingWaterSoaksIntentionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Water records intention and soaks the fine bodies"@en, "Wasser zeichnet die Absicht auf und durchtränkt die feinen Körper"@de ;
    skos:definition "Water is said to charge thought-forms and thought-markers with information; it does not send intention into space but first records what one has spoken and then saturates all one's fine, energetic bodies with it."@en ;
    skos:note "Linked: pmc:TranserfingThoughtFormsTf, pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBroadcastingOnesIntentionTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Broadcasting one's intention like a radio station"@en, "Die eigene Absicht wie ein Sender ausstrahlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the bath one is fully charged with the spoken intention and goes about like a living radio station, transmitting it into all the surrounding space."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingBathYieldsBroadcastingTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Plait in the bath yields broadcasting one's intention"@en, "Zopf in der Wanne bewirkt das Ausstrahlen der Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working with the plait in water is said to saturate one with the intention and make one radiate it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPlaitInTheBathTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBroadcastingOnesIntentionTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingContrastShowerThenPlaitTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Contrast shower, then the plait with flows"@en, "Wechseldusche, danach der Zopf mit Strömen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without a bath: warm up for a few minutes under hot, not too hot, water, then cold for at most a minute, three or four rounds. The plait is not worked during the shower, where concentration is harder than in the bath; after turning the water off, stand quietly, concentrate and perform the plait-with-flows algorithm."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingNoMarkedDiscomfortTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No marked discomfort in the contrast shower"@en, "Kein deutliches Unbehagen bei der Wechseldusche"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sharper the contrast the better, but one must not feel clear discomfort, so as not to harm one's health."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingContrastShowerThenPlaitTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRaisedEnergyTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sharply raised energy"@en, "Sprunghaft erhöhte Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The contrast shower is said to raise one's energy sharply."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingContrastShowerYieldsRaisedEnergyTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Contrast shower yields raised energy"@en, "Wechseldusche bewirkt erhöhte Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The contrast of temperatures is said to lift one's energy steeply."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingContrastShowerThenPlaitTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRaisedEnergyTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPlaitNotAToyTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The plait is not a toy"@en, "Der Zopf ist kein Spielzeug"@de ;
    skos:definition "The plait is no gadget one may or may not buy: it is one's own and always present, and no gadget gives what it gives; switch it on only consciously and with a purpose, never playing with it needlessly."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ПЛИТКАТА И ЕНЕРГИЙНИТЕ ПОТОЦИ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ'
#

pmp:TranserfingRereadingTheBookTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Rereading the book in a new way"@en, "Das Buch auf neue Weise wiederlesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In place of further recaps, read this book again in a new way, perhaps more than once, since neither doing the practices nor merely reading lets one grasp and keep everything at once; try at least once more."@en ;
    skos:note "The overview closes the same way (p. 65): it gives only the basics, mastering the details requires reading the whole book again, and what stays unclear is to be read in the Transurfing books."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingEachRereadingBringsInsightTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Each rereading brings new insight"@en, "Jedes Wiederlesen bringt neue Einsicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "With every new reading one gains more insights and finds something new, surprised as if reading it for the first time."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: with every new reading one gains more insights and finds something new, surprised as if reading it for the first time; it bears on pmp:TranserfingRereadingTheBookTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRightToPastPowerTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The right to the power of past incarnations"@en, "Das Recht auf die Kraft früherer Verkörperungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beyond the right to create one's future reality and even a new mannequin, one is said to have a right to the personal power, the power of the soul, accumulated over previous lives. That each new life starts from nothing is called an error, a defect of the universe; whether to resign oneself to it is one's own choice, and claiming what is one's by right depends on oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Вашето право."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMeaningOfLifeIsLifeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The meaning of life is life itself"@en, "Der Sinn des Lebens ist das Leben selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Life has no deeper philosophical meaning than itself; a planet or a grain of sand simply is, and living and non-living do not differ in this. The series of incarnations has no further meaning either: every life, from a butterfly's to the universe's, is a dream of the Creator, whose Spark is present in all that exists, and the meaning and worth of every life are equal."@en ;
    skos:note "Linked: pmc:TranserfingSparkOfTheCreatorTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingKnowledgeForSeekersTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowledge only for those who seek it"@en, "Wissen nur für Suchende"@de ;
    skos:definition "What one should know is what one is capable of and what one is entitled to; but this Knowledge is not given to all, only to those who strive for it, and whoever does not want to know may simply live as they please."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingShameOfLivingUnawareTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living unaware despite self-awareness"@en, "Unbewusst leben trotz Selbstbewusstsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everyone has the right simply to live without asking questions, and a snail need not be ashamed of living as a mindless snail, since that is its nature; the question put to the reader is whether it is not shameful to live as a mindless character when one possesses self-awareness. The reader is held to be no longer content with what is given and known."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingGreatnessInPastLivesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Greatness in former incarnations"@en, "Größe in früheren Verkörperungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The readers are told they were once well-known, perhaps great, people in their previous incarnations, for otherwise they would not have earned this life; yet despite that greatness everything is now lost and the former lives are not remembered."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 48; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPowerNotExperienceReturnsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The power returns, not the experience"@en, "Die Kraft kehrt zurück, nicht die Erfahrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The experience of forgotten lives cannot be recovered, any more than what one lived through in a forgotten dream; the personal power gathered across the series of incarnations, however, is one's by right and should not go to waste."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAccessPastLifeInformationX10: there access to past-life information is reported and whether past lives happened is left open; here past lives are asserted, their content is said to be lost, and only their power is claimable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfTheRightTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Declaration of the right to one's power"@en, "Erklärung des Rechts auf die eigene Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever asserts the right receives it: with the plait activated, as when creating reality, proclaim a short declaration in three parts, that one claims one's right, takes back one's power and receives the power of all one's incarnations. Repeat it from time to time, as often as one sees fit."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: декларацията."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDeclarationNeedsThePlaitTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The declaration needs the plait"@en, "Die Erklärung braucht den Zopf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Words alone do not suffice; the archaic rudiment, the plait, must be activated for the declaration to be heard by the Power."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfTheRightTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without the plait the words are only air set moving, and the Power does not hear them." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingUnheardDeclarationTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A declaration without the plait goes unheard"@en, "Eine Erklärung ohne Zopf bleibt ungehört"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spoken without activating the plait, the declaration is mere movement of air and does not reach the Power."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: spoken without activating the plait, the declaration is mere movement of air and does not reach the Power; it bears on pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfTheRightTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingGrowingPersonalPowerTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Growing personal power, confidence and strength of spirit"@en, "Wachsende persönliche Kraft, Zuversicht und Geisteskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Personal power accumulated over incarnations is promised to return, felt as growing power, confidence and strength of Spirit."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDeclarationYieldsPersonalPowerTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Declaration yields growing personal power"@en, "Erklärung bewirkt wachsende persönliche Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Proclaiming the declaration with the plait is said to bring personal power back."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfTheRightTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingGrowingPersonalPowerTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFeelingPowerGrowTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling one's power grow"@en, "Die eigene Kraft wachsen fühlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Soon and gradually one will feel one's personal power, confidence and strength of Spirit increase; one will certainly feel it."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: soon and gradually one will feel one's personal power, confidence and strength of Spirit increase; one will certainly feel it; it bears on pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfTheRightTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingPowerThoughtMarkerTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Thought-marker for growing power"@en, "Gedankenmarker für wachsende Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whenever one finds confirmation that one's power is growing, fix the renewed project with a thought-marker to the effect that one's personal power is really increasing and one sees it."@en ;
    skos:note "Linked: pmc:TranserfingThoughtMarkersTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingConfirmationBeforePowerMarkerTf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Confirmation before the power thought-marker"@en, "Bestätigung vor dem Kraft-Gedankenmarker"@de ;
    skos:definition "The thought-marker of growing power is set only after a confirmation of the declaration's effect has been found."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingPowerThoughtMarkerTf ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingDeclarationOfTheRightTf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'СИЛАТА НА МИНАЛИТЕ ПРЕВЪПЛЪЩЕНИЯ', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'БЕЗКРАЙНОСТ В БЕЗКРАЙНОСТТА'
#

pmc:TranserfingProofByOwnPracticeTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Proof: one's own practice, then anomalies"@en, "Beweis: eigene Praxis, dann Anomalien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked for proof that one really lives in a film and can jump between reels, the text names as main proof one's own practical experience, to be checked by oneself, and as indirect proofs many anomalous and unexplained phenomena; direct proof will not be had, since reality is not inclined to reveal its secrets."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how the method is tested: by personal practice."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingProofFromPractice: practice remains the test, but anomalies are added as indirect evidence and reality itself is said to withhold direct proof."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'БЕЗКРАЙНОСТ В БЕЗКРАЙНОСТТА', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingReelsAndMirrorAsModelsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Film reels and mirror as working models"@en, "Filmrollen und Spiegel als Arbeitsmodelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "The speaker says she knows nothing except that it works; why and how is a large question. Film reels and mirror are models, interpretations of something far more complex, chosen for being understandable; reality's real structure cannot be grasped but its properties can and should be used, and a model that works must be very close to the original, so the adopted one is kept."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on the status of the method: pragmatic models, not knowledge of reality's structure."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingModelJudgedByResults: there the author was convinced by practice and values a model for its use; here the speaker disclaims all knowledge and adds that a working model must be close to the original."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'БЕЗКРАЙНОСТ В БЕЗКРАЙНОСТТА', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingOneMaterialUniverseTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One material universe, many archive reels"@en, "Ein stoffliches Universum, viele Archivrollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reality is not virtual and not a computer game but real, structured like many intertwining film reels, some being projected and some kept in the archive. There are no parallel material worlds, only one material universe and endlessly many virtual variants; a piece of an archive reel may chance to be lit in the current frame, bringing someone from the past, the future or another civilization."@en ;
    skos:note "Linked: pmc:TranserfingFilmReelTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'БЕЗКРАЙНОСТ В БЕЗКРАЙНОСТТА', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingMemoryAddressesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Memory holds addresses: deja vu and the Mandela effect"@en, "Das Gedächtnis hält Adressen: Déjà-vu und Mandela-Effekt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The brain is said to store not information but the address of it. When one passes to another reel, addresses may come loose and attach to the new one or stay with the old, causing confusions like deja vu about what did or did not happen. When common reality jumps to another reel while millions keep their old addresses, a phrase remembered from a film can vanish from every copy: the Mandela effect, a real error of reality in which the past changed."@en ;
    skos:note "Anomaly anecdotes cited around it (a train of 1911 vanishing in a tunnel and passengers appearing in Mexico in 1840; people from the past with their pocket contents; out-of-place finds) are not entered separately."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'БЕЗКРАЙНОСТ В БЕЗКРАЙНОСТТА', p. 49; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingCommonReelOfHumanityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Individual reels on a common reel of humanity"@en, "Einzelrollen auf einer gemeinsamen Rolle der Menschheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Individual reels turn separately but lie on a reel common to all humanity. An end-of-the-world variant exists in the archive, since seers see it, but so far common reality keeps jumping to a favourable reel. Where reels cross, a frame of the future can land on a reel of the past; where they only touch, a chronomirage arises."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'БЕЗКРАЙНОСТ В БЕЗКРАЙНОСТТА', p. 50; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDiscreteRealityTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "All reality is discrete"@en, "Die ganze Wirklichkeit ist diskret"@de ;
    skos:definition "Material actuality is the lit frame, reality the whole set of reels. The anomalies prove nothing but indirectly confirm an endless space of variant reels; since reels consist of frames separated by gaps, not only the quantum microworld but all reality is discrete, and instant displacement in time and space happens in those gaps."@en ;
    skos:note "The text adds that science could make many discoveries if it allowed the macroworld to be quantum too."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'БЕЗКРАЙНОСТ В БЕЗКРАЙНОСТТА', p. 50; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingLeavingTheFrameRateTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Leaving the frame rate to create the impossible"@en, "Die Bildfrequenz verlassen, um das Unmögliche zu schaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "All the practices are said to confirm that reality is discrete: by leaving the frame rate of the current reel one gains the ability to create the impossible, since every manipulation with attention and the plait throws one out of reality's frequency and phase and so lets one walk freely in the film."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "No yielding is written: the text ascribes the effect to all work with attention and the plait, practices introduced before this part with no fixed id here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'БЕЗКРАЙНОСТ В БЕЗКРАЙНОСТТА', p. 51; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingGrowingArchiveTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The archive of eternity evolved and grows"@en, "Das Archiv der Ewigkeit hat sich entwickelt und wächst"@de ;
    skos:definition "The archive did not appear at once: evolution is in a sense a production of information, living and non-living nature recording the variants of its existence, as a network accumulates what visitors add. The archive is not an all-embracing field that always was but a part of infinity that moves and grows within it, itself infinite."@en ;
    skos:note "A parenthesis grants that the archive might be said always to have existed, which would require clarifying what always means."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'БЕЗКРАЙНОСТ В БЕЗКРАЙНОСТТА', p. 51; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotRackTheMindTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not rack the mind over what reason cannot grasp"@en, "Sich nicht den Kopf über Unfassbares zerbrechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One need not try to imagine infinity within infinity; instead of struggling with it, act and take delight in knowing that one can create oneself and one's reality, which gives light at the end of the tunnel, strength, hope, aim and the energy to create what ordinary people deem impossible."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingGrowingArchiveTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'БЕЗКРАЙНОСТ В БЕЗКРАЙНОСТТА', p. 51; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ'
#

pmc:TranserfingLizardStageTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Readers as lizards between snail and firefly"@en, "Leser als Eidechsen zwischen Schnecke und Glühwürmchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Closing the first volume, the speaker tells readers that if they have not yet become fireflies they have at least come closer and are in an intermediate state, as playful, curious lizards."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: гущерчета."@en ;
    skos:note "The text orders three stages here (snail, lizard, firefly); snail and firefly belong to figures introduced before this part, so no pm:Sequencing is written from this part."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 51; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSleepersInTheAquariumTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Most people never wake"@en, "Die meisten Menschen erwachen nie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Almost everyone lives without ever waking, walking through life as in a dream without looking up or around; they never create their reality but only float in the film allotted to them, as in an aquarium. The main thing is to use the Knowledge received."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 51; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotWakeTheSleepersTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No arrogance, and do not wake the sleepers"@en, "Keine Überheblichkeit, und die Schlafenden nicht wecken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Differing from the sleepers gives no right to arrogance or, worse, contempt; waking them is a thankless task, so let them live as they want and can; whoever is able to wake will find the speaker by himself."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingWakingInTheFilmTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 51; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingFightingTheCurrentFrameTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fighting current actuality instead of creating"@en, "Die gegenwärtige Wirklichkeit bekämpfen statt erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Things also fail because one does not know how to act for them to succeed: instead of creating one's future reality one fights with current actuality."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: things also fail because one does not know how to act for them to succeed: instead of creating one's future reality one fights with current actuality; it bears on creating reality, the frame illumination of part 1."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 52; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingSeeingTheIllusionSufficesTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing one's illusion suffices to change life"@en, "Die eigene Illusion zu sehen genügt, um das Leben zu ändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The book's purpose is to pull the reader out of the illusion of spectacle; few words are needed, only understanding and seeing where one's illusion lies, and that alone is radical enough to change one's life; later books promise more."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 52; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingRedirectingTheVectorTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Redirecting the vector toward creating reality"@en, "Den Vektor auf das Erschaffen der Wirklichkeit umlenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every day something worries, oppresses or dispirits one; watch oneself constantly, do not give in, and turn the vector round: one can create one's reality and decides what is to happen. Create the end result, the target frame, never the course of events, and make this a habit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 52; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingThePowerHelpsCreatorsTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Power helps those who create"@en, "Die Kraft hilft denen, die erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Power, the engine of reality that projects the reels, notices whoever starts creating reality: it always attends to those who help it turn the reels, takes them up and begins to help them, while it has no interest in the hollow mannequins of dreams who live in the film without waking."@en ;
    skos:note "Linked: pmc:TranserfingOuterPowerTf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 52; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingPowerMottoTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Motto of seeking and acting with the Power"@en, "Wahlspruch, die Kraft zu suchen und mit ihr zu handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take as one's motto that one seeks the Power, finds it and does everything with it, meaning that one does everything strongly, brilliantly and from the soul."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 52; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingHelpOfThePowerTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Power abides with one"@en, "Die Kraft bleibt bei einem"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who create reality in this way are promised that the Power will stay with them."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 52; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingPowerMottoYieldsHelpTf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Acting with the Power yields its abiding help"@en, "Handeln mit der Kraft bewirkt ihre bleibende Hilfe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creating reality under the motto of the Power is said to draw its support."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPowerMottoTf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHelpOfThePowerTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 52; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingRejoiceQuietlyTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Rejoice quietly and do not boast"@en, "Still freuen und nicht prahlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not fall into calf-like rapture over the miracles one has made oneself; rejoice quietly, for oneself, so that reality, which can be spiteful, does not take revenge, and still less boast before others."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNeverBoast: the ground given is the spite of reality, not the balancing forces, and quiet rejoicing is prescribed in its place."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingAlgorithmsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 52; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingKeepTheTechniquesToOneselfTf a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not tell acquaintances about the techniques"@en, "Bekannten nichts von den Techniken erzählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not speak to acquaintances about the techniques of setting reality and mannequins: they will not understand and will laugh; the techniques must not be torn from their context, and one may at most advise reading everything in order."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingAlgorithmsTf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 52; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmp:TranserfingBookAsTalismanTf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping the book as a personal talisman"@en, "Das Buch als persönlichen Talisman behalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Give this book to no one: it is a kind of personal talisman; hold it in one's hands, feel it, sense it as one's own thing."@en ;
    skos:note "No effect is stated beyond its being a talisman."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ЗАКЛЮЧЕНИЕ', p. 52; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'АЛГОРИТМИТЕ'
#

pmc:TranserfingAlgorithmsTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The algorithms"@en, "Die Algorithmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author's compiled set of the book's procedures, gathered after the conclusion: awakening, illuminating the frame, the plait with energy flows, benefit, following, the image, the reflection, synchronizing the project, and the complex movement-walk. They are to be done without fail because they unglue one from the scenario, bring one alive in the film and build useful automatic habits."@en ;
    skos:note "Members restated from earlier chapters are counted, not written again: the image and reflection algorithms are pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheImageTf and pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheReflectionTf; awakening (pmc:TranserfingCentreOfAwarenessTf, pmc:TranserfingTwoScreensTf), frame illumination (pmc:TranserfingMetapowerTf), benefit, following and the complex movement-walk are practices of earlier parts. The plait-with-flows and synchronization algorithms first appear in this part: pmp:TranserfingPlaitWithFlowsAlgorithmTf, pmp:TranserfingSynchronizationAlgorithmTf."@en ;
    skos:note "The stated reason for the set (unglued from the scenario, alive in the film, automatic habits) has no single practice behind it, so no yielding is written; it stands in this definition."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Алгоритмите."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'АЛГОРИТМИТЕ', p. 52; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

#
# section 'ОБЗОР НА ОСНОВНИТЕ ПРИНЦИПИ'
#

pmc:TranserfingOverviewOfPrinciplesTf a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Overview of the main principles"@en, "Überblick über die Hauptprinzipien"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author's closing glossary of the book's notions in their order of introduction, each entry a headword with a short restatement and often a pointer to the algorithm or chapter: dream space, actuality, the layers of reality, the two screens, attention, sleep and dreams, awakening, the centre of awareness, the walk in the dream, the character and the scenario, activators, the archive of eternity, moving the frame, intention and its plait, metapower, the imitation of the spectacle, presence, benefit, allowance, moving oneself, the Spark of the Creator, the command of the Power, the outer Power, the mirror, image and reflection, manipulation, the mannequin, uniqueness, the three achievements and the mission. It ends by saying it gives only the basics."@en ;
    skos:note "Its entries restate earlier chapters and are counted, not written again; restated fixed ids: pmc:TranserfingDreamSpaceTf, pmc:TranserfingFilmReelTf, pmc:TranserfingTwoScreensTf, pmc:TranserfingCentreOfAwarenessTf, pmc:TranserfingWakingInTheFilmTf, pmc:TranserfingScenarioTf, pmc:TranserfingMannequinsTf, pmc:TranserfingPlaitTf, pmc:TranserfingMetapowerTf, pmc:TranserfingPresenceTf, pmc:TranserfingSparkOfTheCreatorTf, pmc:TranserfingOuterPowerTf, pmc:TranserfingRealityMirrorTf, pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheImageTf, pmp:TranserfingCreatingTheReflectionTf."@en ;
    skos:note "The entry on the walk in the dream (p. 57) is headed with a misprint in the Bulgarian text, Разходна for Разходка."@en ;
    skos:note "Bulgarian term: Обзор на основните принципи."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2018"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЗОР НА ОСНОВНИТЕ ПРИНЦИПИ', p. 56; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

pmc:TranserfingHigherSchoolTf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transurfing as primary school, Tafti's techniques as higher school"@en, "Transurfing als Grundschule, Taftis Techniken als Hochschule"@de ;
    skos:definition "The last line of the overview ranks the methods: Transurfing is the elementary school, Tafti's techniques the higher school and high aerobatics. An end note after a section mark adds that this book describes techniques even more powerful than those of Transurfing, an essential addition and a new, higher level of it."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on the standing of the method relative to the author's earlier Transurfing."@en ;
    skos:note "The end note (pp. 64-65) reads as a publisher's note; it also announces a separate fiction volume, Жрицата Итфат, about Tafti's adventures in metareality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingTaftiZhritsa ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Tafti zhritsa (2018), section 'ОБЗОР НА ОСНОВНИТЕ ПРИНЦИПИ', p. 65; read in the Bulgarian translation by Vesela Petrova, Жрицата Тафти. Разходка на живо във филм (e-book, spiralata.net, translation © 2018), the only translation reached; the Russian original and an English translation were not reached" .

